hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6001","5995 - Muhammad ibn Imran al-Naqit narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Makhlad narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Awn narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Zurarah narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No blessing Allah bestows upon a servant in family, wealth or child, and he says: What Allah wills, there is no power except with Allah, then he sees in it a calamity short of death, and he used to interpret this verse: {And why, when you entered your garden, did you not say: What Allah wills, there is no power except with Allah}. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Umar ibn Yunus was alone in transmitting it."
"6002","5996 - Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Walid al-Sulami al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la al-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Kahmas ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi Hind narrated to us, from Amir al-Sha'bi, he said: Abdillah ibn Umar narrated to us, from his father Umar ibn al-Khattab - the hadith of the lizard - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a gathering of his companions when a Bedouin man from Banu Sulaym came who had hunted a lizard and put it in his sleeve, and took it to his camp, then saw a gathering and said: For whom is this gathering? They said: For this one who claims he is a prophet, so he pushed through people, then came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Muhammad, no woman ever bore one with a tongue more lying than you nor more hateful, and were it not that my people would call me hasty I would hasten upon you and kill you, and delight all people with your killing, so Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, let me kill him, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you not know that the forbearing almost becomes a prophet? Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: By al-Lat and al-Uzza I will not believe in you, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said to him: O Bedouin, what made you say what you said, and speak untruth, and not honor my gathering? So he said: And you speak to me too - belittling the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - by al-Lat and al-Uzza I will not believe in you unless this lizard believes in you? So he took out a lizard from his sleeve and threw it before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: If this lizard believes in you I will believe in you, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O lizard, so the lizard spoke in clear Arabic speech understood by all the people: At your service and happiness, O Messenger of the Lord of the worlds, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Whom do you worship? He said: Him Whose Throne is in heaven, Whose authority is on earth, Whose path is in the sea, Whose mercy is in Paradise and Whose punishment is in the Fire, he said: Who am I, O lizard? He said: You are the Messenger of the Lord of the worlds and the seal of prophets, successful is he who believes you, and ruined is he who denies you, so the Bedouin said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah and that you are truly the Messenger of Allah, I came to you when none on earth was more hateful to me than you, and by Allah now you are more beloved to me than myself and my parents, and I have believed in you with my hair, my skin, my inside, my outside, my secret and my open. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Praise be to Allah Who guided you to this religion which is exalted and not surpassed, Allah does not accept it except with prayer, and does not accept prayer except with Quran, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him (al-Hamd) and: {Say: He is Allah, One}. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I never heard in prose or verse better than this, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: This is the speech of the Lord of the worlds, not poetry, when you recite {Say: He is Allah, One} once it is as if you recited a third of the Quran, and when you recite it twice it is as if you recited two thirds of the Quran, and when you recite it three times it is as if you recited the whole Quran, so the Bedouin said: Excellent is our God, He accepts little and gives much, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Give the Bedouin, so they gave him until they satiated him, then Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to give him a she-camel seeking nearness to Allah, below the Bukhti and above the Bedouin breed, ten months pregnant, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You described what you give, shall I describe to you what Allah gives you in reward? He said: Yes, he said: For you a she-camel of hollow pearl, its legs of green emerald, its neck of yellow topaz, upon it a howdah, upon the howdah silk and brocade, passing over the Sirat like flashing lightning. Then the Bedouin left the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and met a thousand Bedouins on a thousand mounts with a thousand spears and a thousand swords, so he said to them: Where are you going? They said: We will fight this one who lies and claims he is a prophet, so the Bedouin said: I bear witness there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, they said to him: Have you apostatized? He said: I have not apostatized, and narrated to them the story, so they all said: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, so that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who met them without a cloak, so they dismounted from their mounts kissing whatever of him they could, saying: There is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, so they said: Command us with a matter the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) loves, he said: Be under the banner of Khalid ibn al-Walid, he said: None of the Arabs believed like them, a thousand men all together, except Banu Sulaym. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn Abi Hind in full except Kahmas, nor from Kahmas except Mu'tamir; Muhammad ibn Abd al-A'la was alone in transmitting it."
"6003","5997 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar, the judge of Aleppo, narrated to us, from al-Shaybani, from Ibn Abi Awfa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Day of Sacrifice is the Day of the Greater Hajj. No one narrated this hadith raised from al-Shaybani except Hafs ibn Umar; Muhammad ibn Bakkar was alone in transmitting it."
"6004","5998 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: al-Fadl ibn al-Sabbah al-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Ubaydillah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Buraydah narrated to us, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three are from harshness: a man wiping dust from his face before finishing his prayer, his blowing in prayer the dust from the place of his face, and urinating standing. This hadith is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain; Abu Ubaydah al-Haddad was alone in transmitting it."
"6005","5999 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Abu Hatim al-Sijistani narrated to us, he said: Abu Jabir Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abu Mas'ud al-Badri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Is one of you unable to recite a third of the Quran in a night? They said: O Messenger of Allah, can one recite a third of the Quran? He said: Is one of you unable to recite: {Say: He is Allah, One}. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far, nor from al-Hasan except Abu Jabir; Abu Hatim al-Sijistani was alone in transmitting it."
"6006","6000 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, from Salih ibn Khawwat, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar, he is Abu Tuwalah, from Anas ibn Malik, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats seven dates of Madinah ajwah in a day, poison will not harm him that day, and whoever eats them at night, poison will not harm him. This hadith is not narrated from Anas, from Aishah, except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Qut'i was alone in transmitting it, and Sulayman ibn Bilal and others narrated it from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ma'mar Abu Tuwalah, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father."
"6007","6001 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn al-Hakam ibn Kurdi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, he said: Salamah ibn Alqamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Name with my name, and do not take my kunyah. No one narrated this hadith from Salamah ibn Alqamah except Ibn Abi Adi; Ahmad ibn Abdillah ibn Kurdi was alone in transmitting it."
"6008","6002 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bistam narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Ubadah narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Khazzaz narrated to us, from Ata, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: When one of you cleans with stones let him make it odd, for Allah is Odd and loves the odd. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Amir al-Khazzaz except Rawh; Ibn Bistam was alone in transmitting it."
"6009","6003 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim narrated to us, he said: Abu Sa'id al-Mu'addib narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Aishah, she said: Uthman entered upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and conversed with him privately at length, while I was below them, and nothing startled me except Uthman kneeling on his knees saying: Injustice and aggression, O Messenger of Allah? So I thought he informed him of his killing. No one narrated this hadith except Abu Sa'id al-Mu'addib Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah; Mansur ibn Abi Muzahim was alone in transmitting it."
"6010","6004 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sudran narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn al-Harith narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Abd al-Malik, from Asim al-Ahwal, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave choice, and it was not divorce. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath except Khalid ibn al-Harith; Ibn Sudran was alone in transmitting it."
"6011","6005 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Sharik, from Burayd, from Abu Burdah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to go out to the desert. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah except Burayd, nor from Burayd except Sharik, nor from Sharik except Ibrahim ibn Sa'd, nor from Ibrahim ibn Sa'd except Muhammad ibn Abbad; Nasr ibn Ali was alone in transmitting it."
"6012","6006 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Qutaybah narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: A man of the people of Illiyyun overlooks the people of Paradise as if a brilliant star, and Abu Bakr and Umar are of them and blessed. No one narrated this hadith from al-Sha'bi except Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq; Abu Qutaybah Salm ibn Qutaybah was alone in transmitting it."
"6013","6007 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham al-Rifa'i narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Aslami narrated to us, from Sa'd al-Iskaf, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Abu Abdillah al-Jadali, from Umm Salamah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hate a woman who leaves her house dragging her hem, complaining of her husband. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except with this chain; Yahya ibn Ya'la al-Aslami was alone in transmitting it."
"6014","6008 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Bazi' narrated to us, he said: Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, he said: Azrah ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: My brother Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Nafi', he said: Ibn Umar said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has two garments let him wear them, and whoever has one garment let him wrap with it, and not wrap like the wrapping of Jews. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Thabit except his brother Azrah, nor from him except Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Bazi' was alone in transmitting it."
"6015","6009 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Abd al-Majid narrated to us, he said: Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ali, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhiy, he said: In it is ablution, and I asked him about maniy, he said: In it is washing. No one narrated this hadith from Zufar except Abu Ali al-Hanafi; Abu Hafs was alone in transmitting it."
"6016","6010 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Abu Hamzah al-Attar narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: Amr ibn Taghlib narrated to me, he is a man from Juwatha of Abd al-Qays, and he is the one to whom the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I give and withhold, I entrust him to what is in his heart, among them Ibn Taghlib. That the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will fight before the Hour a people wearing hair, and others as if their faces are shields. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hamzah al-Attar except Muhammad ibn Abbad; Nasr ibn Ali was alone in transmitting it."
"6017","6011 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Fallas narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Habib al-Qanawi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ka'b, the silk merchant, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Hakim ibn Hizam, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me from selling what is not with me."
"6018","6012 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Rushayd narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn Habib narrated to us, Bistam ibn Habib narrated to us, Abu Ka'b narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Bakrah, from his father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: A time will soon come upon people in which they neither command good nor forbid evil. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ka'b, the silk merchant, except Bistam ibn Habib; Dawud ibn Rushayd was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Bakrah except with this chain."
"6019","6013 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harun al-Fallas narrated to us, he said: Qurrah ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Abu Ka'b, the silk merchant, narrated to us, from al-Nadr, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: My intercession on the Day of Resurrection is for him who bears witness there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abu Ka'b except Qurrah ibn Habib."
"6020","6014 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Sukkari narrated to us, he said: Hibban ibn Hilal narrated to us, he said: Aban ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray witr, O people of the Quran. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except Aban; Hibban ibn Hilal was alone in transmitting it."
"6021","6015 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Jahdam narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan narrated to us, from Kharijah ibn al-Harith ibn Rafi' ibn Makith al-Juhani, from his father, he said: I heard Sinan ibn Wabarah say: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the expedition of al-Muraysi', the expedition of Banu al-Mustaliq, and their slogan was: O Mansur, kill. This hadith is not narrated from Sinan ibn Wabarah except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Jahdam was alone in transmitting it."
"6022","6016 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Ibrahim al-Dawraqi narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Ziyad narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak informed us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Ubaydillah informed me, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in a battle, when a polytheist man duelled a Muslim man and the polytheist killed him, then another Muslim duelled him and the polytheist killed him, then he drew near and stood over the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: For what do you fight? He said: Our religion is to fight people until they bear witness there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, and that we fulfill Allah's right. He said: By Allah this is good, I believe in this, then he turned to the Muslims and charged the polytheists and fought until killed, so he was carried and placed with his two companions whom he had killed, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These are the most loving of Paradise's people to one another. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Musa except with this chain; Ibn al-Mubarak was alone in transmitting it."
"6023","6017 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: al-Husayn ibn Mansur al-Tirmidhi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, he said: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Sha'bi, from Warrad, the scribe of al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, from al-Mughirah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Leave me as I leave you, for those before you perished only by their many questions to their prophets and their differing with their prophets, so whatever I command you of a thing do of it what you can, and whatever I forbid you refrain. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Ammar ibn Ruzayq; Abu al-Jawwab was alone in transmitting it."
"6024","6018 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Umawi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi Zinad narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Habibah, from Yazid ibn Ruman, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while I lay across before him. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Ruman except Ibrahim ibn Isma'il ibn Abi Habibah, nor from Ibrahim ibn Isma'il except Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi Zinad; Sa'id ibn Yahya al-Umawi was alone in transmitting it."
"6025","6019 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us, he said: I heard my father say: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Khallad ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the most beloved of you to Allah? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and we thought he would name a man, so he said: The most beloved of you to Allah is the most beloved of you to people. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Shall I not inform you of the most hated of you to Allah? We said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, and we thought he would name a man, so he said: The most hated of you to Allah is the most hated of you to people. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; Ibn al-Mubarak was alone in transmitting it, and none narrated it from Ibn al-Mubarak except Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq, Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Shaqiq narrated to us with this hadith: I narrated this hadith to Ahmad ibn Hanbal, and he deemed it good."
"6026","6020 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Mu'min ibn Abbad narrated to us, he said: Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, from Abu Majidah, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: A funeral passed by the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), shaken like the shaking of a waterskin, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is moderation in walking with your funerals without hurrying, for if it is good you hasten it to it, and if it is evil may Allah not distance except the people of the Fire, and the funeral is followed and not following, none with it who precedes it. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abd al-Mu'min ibn Abbad; Nasr ibn Ali was alone in transmitting it."
"6027","6021 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Ali ibn Thabit, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Image-makers will be punished on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said to them: Give life to what you created. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Thabit except Imran al-Qattan; Muhammad ibn Bilal was alone in transmitting it."
"6028","6022 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn Sakan narrated to us, he said: Rayhan ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Ar'arah ibn al-Brind narrated to us, from Muhtasib, whose kunyah is Abu A'idh, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: That I sit with people remembering Allah after Fajr prayer until sunrise is more beloved to me than freeing four of the children of Isma'il, and that I sit with people remembering Allah from Asr prayer until sunset is more beloved to me than freeing four of the children of Isma'il. No one narrated this hadith from Muhtasib except Ar'arah ibn al-Brind; Rayhan ibn Sa'id was alone in transmitting it."
"6029","6023 - Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn Mukram narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Muhammad ibn al-Sakan narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Idris narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Burayd ibn Malik ibn Rabi'ah al-Saluli narrated to us, he said: Burayd ibn Malik ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from his father, that he witnessed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Day of the Tree, when the sacrificial animals were held back before reaching their place, and that a man came that day to him and said: O Muhammad, what makes you upon what I see? You want these to enter, while we dislike them, from the dregs of tribes? He said: These are better than you and than him who takes your way, they believe in Allah and the Last Day, and by Him in Whose Hand is Muhammad's soul, Allah is pleased with them. This hadith is not narrated from Malik ibn Rabi'ah except with this chain."
"6030","6024 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Shafi'i al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Uthman al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the year of al-Hudaybiyah share a camel among seven of his companions. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Mu'awiyah ibn Yahya; Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Attar was alone in transmitting it."
"6031","6025 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib ibn Sharik al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar narrated to us, from al-A'mash and al-Hasan ibn Amr, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abu Musa, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us with four, and said: Allah Almighty does not sleep, nor is it fitting for Him to sleep, He lowers the balance and raises it, to Him is raised the deed of day before the deed of night, and the deed of night before the deed of day, His veil is fire, were He to lift the veil the splendors of His Face would burn all His sight reaches. Then he recited: {Blessed is He in the fire and around it}. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Amr except Amr ibn Abd al-Ghaffar."
"6032","6026 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Hashim al-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Sukayn ibn Siraj narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are most beloved to Allah? And which deeds are most beloved to Allah Almighty? So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The most beloved people to Allah are the most beneficial to people, and the most beloved deeds to Allah are joy you bring to a Muslim, or relieve from him distress, or pay from him debt, or repel from him hunger, and that I walk with a brother of mine in a need is more beloved to me than secluding in this mosque - meaning the mosque of Madinah - a month, and whoever restrains his anger Allah covers his nakedness, and whoever swallows his rage, even if he wished to carry it out he could, Allah Almighty fills his heart with safety on the Day of Resurrection, and whoever walks with his brother in a need until he establishes it for him, Allah Almighty establishes his foot on the Sirat on the day feet slip. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Sukayn ibn Siraj; Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays was alone in transmitting it."
"6033","6027 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: al-Qasim ibn Hashim al-Simsar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Visit the sick, and order them to supplicate for you, for the sick person's supplication is answered and his sin forgiven. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays was alone in transmitting it."
"6034","6028 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Sha'bi, from Ibn Muti', from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of the conquest of Makkah: No Qurashi shall be killed after today in custody until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except Isa ibn Yunus; Sulayman ibn Umar ibn Khalid was alone in transmitting it."
"6035","6029 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, he said: Mujalid ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, he said: I entered upon Aishah, so she called for food and said: Eat, seldom do I eat my fill of food and wish to weep except I wept, I said: O Mother of the Believers, what is that from? She said: I remember the state in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left the world, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate his fill twice in a day of wheat bread until he joined Allah. He said: And Aishah said: An Ansari woman entered upon me and saw the bed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as a cloak, so she said: Has he no bed but this? I said: No, by Allah, he has no bed but it, so she took palm fiber and stuffed it with wool, then brought it to me and said: Let this be the bed of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so when he came he said: O Aishah, what is this? So I informed him, and he said: Return it. She said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left me and I did not return it, and I liked it to be in my house, so he came and said: O Aishah, did I not order you to return it? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I did not return it, and I liked it to be in my house, so he said: O Aishah, return it, for if I wished Allah would make gold and silver flow with me. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except al-Salt ibn Mas'ud."
"6036","6030 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Dinar narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Salim ibn Abdillah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Five harmful animals are killed in the sacred and profane: the mouse, the scorpion, the kite, the vicious dog, and the crow. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi; al-Salt was alone in transmitting it."
"6037","6031 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Salt ibn Mas'ud al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abi Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to us, from his father, from Bashir ibn al-Khasasiyah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and met him at al-Baqi', and heard him say: Peace upon the people of abodes among believers, then my sandal strap broke, so he said: Fix your foot. I said: O Messenger of Allah, my absence was long and I am far from my people's home, so he said: O Bashir, do you not praise Allah Who took your forelock to Islam from among Rabi'ah, a people who think that were it not for them the earth would swallow those upon it. No one narrates this hadith from al-Shaybani except his son Ishaq; Uqbah ibn al-Mughirah was alone in transmitting it."
"6038","6032 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn al-Mukhtar and Layth and al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Arfajah, raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: There will be discords and discords, so whomever you see walking to the ummah of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while they are united to divide them, kill him whoever he is. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd, from al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah, except Muhammad ibn Sulayman."
"6039","6033 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Abu Khaythamah narrated to us, from Abu Hamzah, from al-Hasan, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Quran was revealed upon seven letters, all healing sufficient. No one narrated this hadith from Maymun Abu Hamzah except Abu Khaythamah Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah; Shuja' ibn al-Walid was alone in transmitting it."
"6040","6034 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: I am your predecessor at the Hawd, and what is between its ends is as between San'a and Aylah, as if the pitchers in it are stars. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Khaythamah except Shuja' ibn al-Walid; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"6041","6035 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Shuja' ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to me, from Abdillah ibn Isa, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Abdillah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade five: the price of a dog, the price of a pig, the price of wine, the dowry of a prostitute, and the stud fee of a stallion. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn Isa except Ziyad ibn Khaythamah; Shuja' ibn al-Walid was alone in transmitting it."
"6042","6036 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: Abu Mus'ab narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Imran narrated to us, from his grandfather Uthman ibn al-Arqam, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said on the day of Badr: Return what was with you of spoils, so Abu Usayd al-Sa'idi raised a sword of Banu al-A'idh ibn al-Marzuban, so al-Arqam recognized it and said: Gift it to me, O Messenger of Allah, so he gave it to him. This hadith is not narrated from al-Arqam ibn Abi al-Arqam except with this chain; Abu Mus'ab was alone in transmitting it."
"6043","6037 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Shuja' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Raqqi narrated to us, from al-Khalil ibn Murrah, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Yazid ibn Marthad, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dawud the Prophet (upon him peace) said: My God, what is due to Your servants from You when they visit You in Your house? He said: Every visitor has a right upon the visited, O Dawud, they have upon Me to grant them health in the world and forgive them when I meet them. No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin ibn Ata except al-Khalil ibn Murrah; Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Raqqi was alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Abu Dharr except with this chain."
"6044","6038 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Asadi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, that a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was stung, and it affected him as Allah willed, so that reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Had he said in the evening - or: when evening came -: I seek refuge in Allah's perfect words from the evil of what He created, three times, it would not harm him. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd well-attested, from Abu Hurayrah, except Muhammad ibn Sulayman, and people narrated it from Hammad, from Suhayl, from his father, from a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"6045","6039 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Isa al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Sallam ibn Abi Muti' narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from Abdillah ibn Yazid, the foster brother of Aishah, from Aishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: No dead person dies and a community of Muslims reaching a hundred prays over him, all interceding for him, except they are granted intercession for him. So I narrated it to Shu'ayb ibn al-Habhab, so he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Sallam ibn Abi Muti' except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"6046","6040 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Isa al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from al-Fadl ibn al-Fadl, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib, that she slaughtered a sheep in her house, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to her: Feed us from your sheep, so she said to the messenger: Nothing remains of it except the neck, and I am shy to send to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the neck, so the messenger returned and informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Return and say: Send it, for it is the guide of the sheep, and the nearest of the sheep to good, and the farthest from harm. This hadith is not narrated from Duba'ah bint al-Zubayr except with this chain; Usamah ibn Zayd was alone in transmitting it."
"6047","6041 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Hammad Sajjadah narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, about His saying Almighty: {And give its due on the day of harvest}, he said: They used to give whoever came to them something besides charity. No one narrated this hadith from Ash'ath ibn Sawwar except Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman."
"6048","6042 - Muhammad ibn Yazdad al-Tawzi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Hammad, Sajjadah, narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah al-Ansari narrated to us, from Zufar ibn al-Hudhayl, from Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Jabir ibn Abdillah: That two brothers had land between them, and one of them gave his share as lifetime gift to his mother, then she died, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) divided between them. No one narrated this hadith from Zufar except al-Ansari, and Zufar dropped two men from the chain, because al-Thawri and Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated it: from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Humayd al-A'raj, from Tariq the judge of Makkah, from Jabir."
"6049","6043 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to me, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Ibn Kaysan, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah and Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that they both narrated: That the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool down with prayer, for intense heat is from the breath of Hell. No one narrated this hadith from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Nafi', except Sulayman ibn Bilal; Ayyub ibn Sulayman was alone in transmitting it, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways."
"6050","6044 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Isma'il al-Bukhari narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Yahya al-Shajari narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, and when he neared Madinah he said: Returning, repenting, worshipping, to our Lord praising, O Allah, I seek refuge with You from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, and evil sight in family and wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib except Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, nor from Asim except Muhammad ibn Ishaq; Yahya ibn Muhammad al-Shajari was alone in transmitting it."
"6051","6045 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn al-Munib narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, that he entered upon Anas ibn Malik, so Anas said: I bear witness I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: O Allah, forgive the Ansar, the wives of the Ansar, and their offspring. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn al-Munib except Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Athmah."
"6052","6046 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Majza'ah ibn Sufyan ibn Usayd ibn Majza'ah al-Thaqafi narrated to us, he said: al-Nu'man ibn Muhammad ibn al-Nu'man al-Minqari informed me, he said: Your grandfather Usayd ibn Majza'ah narrated to us, from his father Majza'ah, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: They disputed before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about qadar, so he disliked it intensely until as if pomegranate seeds burst upon his face, so he said: What are you about? They said: We disputed about qadar, O Messenger of Allah, so he said: Everything is by decree and ordainment, even this, and he struck with his forefinger upon the cord of his other forearm. Majza'ah Abu Usayd al-Thaqafi narrated from Thabit al-Bunani only this hadith; his son was alone in transmitting it."
"6053","6047 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Thabit and Yunus and Habib and Humayd, from al-Hasan, from Sa'sa'ah ibn Mu'awiyah, from Abu Dharr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever spends a pair of his wealth in Allah's path, the keepers of Paradise rush to him, I said: Two camels, two horses, two sheep, two dirhams, two slippers, two sandals. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Humayd, except Abu Hisham al-Makhzumi; Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari was alone in transmitting it, and Yunus and Habib are with more than one."
"6054","6048 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Hadrami narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Abi Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu al-Tufayl say: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent while I was a boy carrying meat from the plain to the mountain. No one narrated this hadith from Khalid ibn Abi Uthman except Ya'qub al-Hadrami."
"6055","6049 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Umayr ibn Abd al-Majid al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi Arib, from Kathir ibn Murrah, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, he said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will never recite a surah more beloved to Allah Almighty nor more effective than: {Say: I seek refuge with the Lord of daybreak}, so if you can not leave it in prayer then do. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan except Kathir ibn Murrah, nor from Kathir except Salih ibn Abi Arib; Abd al-Hamid ibn Ja'far was alone in transmitting it."
"6056","6050 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you are praying and a man wants to pass before you, prevent him, if he returns prevent him, if he returns prevent him, if he returns a fourth time fight him, for he is only Satan. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Sa'id ibn Abi Arubah; al-Nadr ibn Kathir was alone in transmitting it."
"6057","6051 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Sakan al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to his bed he said: O Allah, I submit myself to You, entrust my affair to You, turn my back to You, in hope and fear of You, no refuge nor escape from You except to You, I believe in what You sent down of Book, and what You sent of Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Thabit al-Bunani except Hammad ibn Salamah; Mu'ammal ibn Isma'il was alone in transmitting it."
"6058","6052 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Akhzam narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abdillah al-Kufi narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Sulayman, from al-Qasim ibn Safwan, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he said: Whoever prays four before Zhuhr it is for him as the reward of freeing a slave, or he said: Four slaves of the children of Isma'il (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Safwan al-Zuhri except with this chain; Zayd ibn Akhzam was alone in transmitting it."
"6059","6053 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Abd al-Malik al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Humayd and Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon a man among his companions while sick, and said: Remove the harm, Lord of people, heal and You are the Healer, no healer but You, a healing leaving no sickness. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman except Hammad ibn Salamah, nor from Hammad except Hilal ibn Abd al-Malik; Abu Hafs was alone in transmitting it."
"6060","6054 - Muhammad ibn Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Malik ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Dhimari narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn al-Walid ibn Surayn narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: I prayed Fajr in Makkah beside an old man, and when he finished his prayer he said: I never prayed behind anyone after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) whose prayer resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more than this youth, and the imam that day was Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, I said: Who are you, may Allah have mercy on you? He said: Anas ibn Malik. No one narrated this hadith from al-Walid ibn Surayn except his son Yahya ibn al-Walid, nor from Yahya except Abd al-Malik al-Dhimari."
"6061","6055 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: al-Minhal ibn Bahr Abu Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Hawari, the freedman of Abdillah ibn Shaqiq, narrated to us, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: We used to carry water in camel skins for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day they wounded him in his face. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Hawari except al-Minhal ibn Bahr; Abu Hafs was alone in transmitting it."
"6062","6056 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' al-Yuhmadi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Muslim, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use ithmid at sleep, for it grows hair and clears sight. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Ziyad ibn al-Rabi'."
"6063","6057 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not mix raisins and dates, nor unripe dates and dates, meaning: nabidh."
"6064","6058 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Bistam ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Ata, from Jabir, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed them and said: Umra is permissible. No one narrated these two hadiths from Bistam ibn Muslim except Abu Dawud."
"6065","6059 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, he said: Mansur ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Ata, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade raisins and dates, and unripe dates and dates. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn Dinar except Abu Asim."
"6066","6060 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Sawwaq narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Qahir ibn Shu'ayb narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps sitting has no ablution upon him, but when he lays his side he must perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far; Abd al-Qahir ibn Shu'ayb was alone in transmitting it."
"6067","6061 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Safwan ibn Isa narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Sa'id al-Maqburi narrated to us, from his father, from al-Qa'qa' ibn Abi Hadrad al-Aslami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Live like Ma'add, be coarse, and walk barefoot. This hadith comes from al-Qa'qa' ibn Abi Hadrad only with this chain; Safwan ibn Isa was alone in transmitting it."
"6068","6062 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Bara al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: Ma'qil ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Sulayman al-Ansari narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Anas, he said: I asked Anas ibn Malik about three traits: the sun, moon and stars, from what were they created? So he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me: They were created from the light of the Throne. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Bara was alone in transmitting it."
"6069","6063 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Bara al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Shaybani narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Khuthaym ibn Irak ibn Malik narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever holds authority over people's affairs, and his intention is upon truth, two angels are assigned to him guiding and directing him, and whoever holds anything of people's affairs, and his intention is other than truth, Allah entrusts him to himself. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Bara was alone in transmitting it."
"6070","6064 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Qarin ibn Sahl ibn Qarin al-Sadusi narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No worry except the worry of debt, and no pain except the pain of the eye."
"6071","6065 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Qarin ibn Sahl ibn Qarin narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two sects of my ummah have no share in Islam: the Murji'ah and the Qadariyyah."
"6072","6066 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Qarin ibn Sahl ibn Qarin narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my soul, the Ka'bah has a tongue and two lips, and it complained to Allah and said: O Lord, my visitors and pilgrims have lessened, so Allah Almighty revealed to it: I am creating humble prostrating humans who yearn to you as the dove yearns to its egg. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Sahl ibn Qarin."
"6073","6067 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Abu Hafs Amr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Khallad ibn Yazid al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mulayki, husband of Jabrah, narrated to us, he said: Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, he said: I said to Aishah: O aunt, I think about your matter and marvel at things, and do not marvel at things, I found you among the most learned people, so I said: What prevents her! Wife of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and daughter of Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and I found you learned in Arab lineages and their days, so I said: What prevents her! Her father is the scholar of Quraysh, but I only marvel that I found you learned in medicine, from where? So she said: O Urayyah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had many illnesses, so we used to treat. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Mulayki except Khallad ibn Yazid al-Bahili."
"6074","6068 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Amr ibn al-Bara al-Ghanawi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abdillah al-Sulami narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Abi Sarah narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas ibn Malik, from Aishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to her a story while with her in a quilt, so she said: By my father and mother, O Messenger of Allah, had you not narrated to me this story I would have thought it a fable, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is the story of Khurafah, O Aishah? She said: When a thing is not, it is said: The story of Khurafah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The truest story is the story of Khurafah, a man of Banu Udhrah, whom the jinn captured, and he would be with them, and when they stole hearing they informed him, so he informs people, and they find it as he said. No one narrated this hadith from Anas except Thabit, nor from Thabit except Ali ibn Abi Sarah, nor from Ali except Sa'id ibn Abdillah; Yazid ibn Amr al-Ghanawi was alone in transmitting it."
"6075","6069 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Rizqullah ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tara'ifi narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Jabbar narrated to us, from Abu Salamah Sulayman ibn Sulaym, from Ubadah ibn Nusayy, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Ghanm, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you buys a slave girl let the first thing he feeds her be sweets, for it sweetens her soul. This hadith is not narrated from Mu'adh ibn Jabal except with this chain; Uthman ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Tara'ifi was alone in transmitting it."
"6076","6070 - Muhammad ibn Yunus al-Usfuri narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Thabit al-Jahdari narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The head of intellect after faith in Allah is affection toward people."
"6077","6071 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Za'idah informed us, from Bayan, from al-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave us choice, was that divorce? No one narrated this hadith from Bayan except Za'idah, nor narrated it from Za'idah except Abdillah ibn Raja, Khalaf ibn Tamim, and Yahya ibn Ya'la ibn al-Harith."
"6078","6072 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham al-Mu'addib narrated to us, he said: Abu Awn narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abdillah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words, peace be upon you O Prophet and the mercy of Allah and His blessings, peace be upon us and upon Allah's righteous servants, I bear witness there is no god but Allah and Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. None raised this hadith from Ibn Awn except Uthman ibn al-Haytham."
"6079","6073 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd narrated to us, Muslim ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from Mujalid ibn Awf, from Kharijah ibn Zayd, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Thabit say: This verse: {And whoever kills a believer intentionally, his recompense is Hell abiding therein} was revealed after the one in al-Furqan: {And those who do not call with Allah another god nor kill the soul Allah forbade except with right} by six months. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Zayd except Muslim ibn Ibrahim."
"6080","6074 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Sallam al-Attar narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Maysarah narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever eats of these two trees let him not approach our mosque, and if you must eat them kill them by cooking. No one narrated this hadith from Mu'awiyah ibn Qurrah except Khalid ibn Maysarah."
"6081","6075 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: My father al-Haytham ibn Jahm narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No state a servant is in is more beloved to Allah than seeing him prostrating with his face in dust."
"6082","6076 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abdillah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque with Ansari women, and admonished and reminded them, and said: None of you women whose three children die except she enters Paradise, so a woman, among their noblest, stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, and one with two? He said: And one with two. No one narrated these two hadiths from Asim except al-Haytham ibn Jahm; Uthman ibn al-Haytham was alone in transmitting them."
"6083","6077 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn al-Haytham narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, he said: Khuza'i ibn Ziyad ibn Abdillah ibn Ma'qil al-Muzani narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade pebble-throwing, and said: Neither game is hunted with it, nor an enemy wounded, but it breaks a tooth and gouges an eye. No one narrated this hadith from Khuza'i ibn Ziyad except al-Haytham ibn al-Jahm."
"6084","6078 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr al-Ataki narrated to us, he said: Imran ibn Khalid al-Khuza'i narrated to us, he said: A freedman of ours called al-Ala ibn Ali narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Barzah al-Aslami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you can be behind the imam, otherwise to his right. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Barzah except with this chain; Imran ibn Khalid al-Khuza'i was alone in transmitting it."
"6085","6079 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Ishaq ibn Yahya, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Our Lord Blessed and Exalted descends every night to the lowest heaven when the last third of the night passes, and says: Is there a servant among My servants calling Me so I answer him, is there one wronging himself calling Me so I forgive him, is there one straitened in provision, is there an oppressed one remembering Me so I help him, is there a captive calling Me so I aid him. He said: So it is thus until dawn shines, then our Lord Almighty rises over His Throne. This hadith is not narrated from Ubadah ibn al-Samit except with this chain; Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak was alone in transmitting it."
"6086","6080 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Quraysh ibn Hayyan, from Abu Ghalib, he said: I heard Umm al-Darda say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made brotherhood between Salman and Abu al-Darda. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ghalib except Quraysh ibn Hayyan; Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Mubarak was alone in transmitting it."
"6087","6081 - Muhammad ibn Uthman ibn Abi Suwayd al-Dhari' narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Awn Abu Awn al-Ziyadi narrated to us, he said: Abu Azzah al-Dabbagh narrated to us, from Abu Yazid al-Madani, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was cupped and gave the cupper his wage. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yazid al-Madani except Abu Azzah al-Dabbagh."
"6088","6082 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Salam al-Sulami al-Basri narrated to us, he said: al-Jarrah ibn Mukhalid narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Asim ibn Hilal al-Bariqi narrated to us, he said: Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked a man among his companions and said: Did you visit a sick person today? He said: No, he said: Did you give charity? He said: No, he said: Did you pray over a funeral? He said: No, he said: Did you come to your family? He said: No, he said: Then come to them, for it is charity from you upon them, and that was Friday. No one narrated this hadith from Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah except al-Nadr ibn Asim ibn Hilal; al-Jarrah ibn Mujalid was alone in transmitting it, none narrated it from Nafi' except Sakhr ibn Juwayriyah, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"6089","6083 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Harithi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Umar al-Bahili narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Ta'ifi narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am a witness over Allah, that no intelligent person stumbles except He raises him until He makes his end Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Maysarah except Muhammad ibn Muslim, nor from Muhammad ibn Muslim except Muhammad ibn Umar al-Raqqi; Ya'qub ibn Ishaq al-Qulusi was alone in transmitting it."
"6090","6084 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Ishaq Abu Yusuf narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdillah al-Kurayzi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Tammam narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn Abi Bishr ibn Shaghaf, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Nothing is more honorable to Allah than the believer. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Ubaydullah ibn Tammam; Abd al-Ghaffar ibn Abdillah al-Kurayzi was alone in transmitting it."
"6091","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Mansur al-Harithi narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Husayn al-Ashqar narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated to us, he said: Abu Amir al-Murri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Burayda, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Ali as commander over Yemen and sent Khalid ibn al-Walid over the mountain, and said: If you join together then Ali is over the people. They met and obtained spoils like they had never obtained, and Ali took a slave girl from the khumus. Khalid ibn al-Walid called Burayda and said: Seize this opportunity and inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of what he did. So I came to Madina and entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in his house with some of his Companions at his door. They said: What is the news, O Burayda? I said: Good; Allah has given victory to the Muslims. They said: What brought you? He said: A slave girl Ali took from the khumus, so I came to inform the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They said: Inform him, for it will lower him in the eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard the talk. He came out angry and said: What is the matter with people who disparage Ali? Whoever disparages Ali has disparaged me, and whoever parts from Ali has parted from me. Ali is from me and I am from him; he was created from my clay and I was created from the clay of Ibrahim, and I am superior to Ibrahim: Offspring, one from another, and Allah is Hearing, Knowing. And he said: O Burayda, do you not know that Ali is entitled to more than the slave girl he took, and that he is your guardian after me? I said: O Messenger of Allah, by companionship, extend your hand so I may pledge to you upon Islam anew. He said: I did not leave him until I pledged to him upon Islam. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Ishaq except with this chain; Husayn al-Ashqar alone narrated it."
"6092","Muhammad ibn Bakr ibn Kurdan al-Hariri al-Basri narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Yahya al-Hanbashi al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Mundhir ibn Jayfar al-Abdi narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Umm Salama who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Acts of kindness protect from evil deaths, and charity given secretly extinguishes the anger of the Lord, and upholding kinship adds to lifespan, and every good deed is charity, and the people of goodness in this world are the people of goodness in the Hereafter, and the people of evil in this world are the people of evil in the Hereafter, and the first to enter Paradise are the people of goodness. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salama except with this chain; Ubaydullah ibn al-Walid al-Wassafi alone narrated it."
"6093","Muhammad ibn Bakr ibn Kurdan narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Dalham narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Kathir narrated to us, he said: Layth narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Aisha who said: I and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to bathe from a single vessel. No one narrated this hadith from Layth except Muhammad ibn Kathir."
"6094","Muhammad ibn Bakr ibn Kurdan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abu Laqab, he said: al-Aswad ibn Amir Shadhan narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, freedman of the family of Talha, from Kurayb, from Aisha who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would become junub then sleep, then wake, then sleep, without touching water. No one narrated this hadith from Kurayb except Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman, nor from Muhammad except Sharik; Shadhan alone narrated it."
"6095","Muhammad ibn Bakr ibn Kurdan narrated to us, he said: Sharik ibn Shihab al-Qazwini narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Abi Qays narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Shabi, from Qaraza ibn Kab and Zayd ibn Suhan, that they set out toward Kufa and Umar ibn al-Khattab preceded them, holding his sandals in his left hand, outpacing them by about three miles until he reached Banu Abd al-Ashhal, and said: You are coming to a city whose people have a buzzing like the buzzing of bees, so narrate little from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I am your partner in that. No one narrated this hadith from Mutarrif except Amr ibn Abi Qays; Muhammad ibn Said ibn Sabiq alone narrated it, and no one said in this hadith from al-Shabi, from Qaraza and Zayd ibn Suhan, except Mutarrif."
"6096","Muhammad ibn Bakr ibn Kurdan narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abd al-Malik al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Firas ibn Yahya, from Ibrahim ibn Yazid al-Taymi, from al-Bara ibn Azib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Mualla ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"6097","Muhammad ibn Bakr ibn Kurdan narrated to me, he said: al-Abbas ibn Abdillah al-Tarqufi narrated to us, he said: Uthman ibn Said ibn Kathir ibn Dinar al-Himsi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muhajir narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Maysara ibn Halbas, from Umm al-Darda who said: Fadala ibn Ubayd used to say: O Allah, I ask You for contentment after decree, and coolness of life after death, and the delight of looking at Your Face, and longing to meet You, without harmful adversity or misguiding trial; and he claimed they were supplications the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with. This hadith is not narrated from Fadala ibn Ubayd except with this chain; Uthman ibn Said al-Himsi alone narrated it."
"6098","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Tha'lab al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Khattab Ziyad ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: Ubayd ibn Waqid al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abdillah al-Ataki, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, that a delegation of Abd al-Qays came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and while they sat with him he turned to them and said to them: A fruit you call such-and-such, and a fruit you call such-and-such, until he described all the colors of their fruits. A man of the people said to him: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you, O Messenger of Allah; by Allah, had you been born inside Hajar you would be no more knowledgeable than you are now. I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your land has been raised up to me since you sat with me, so I looked from its nearest to its farthest, and the best of your fruits is the barni; it removes illness and there is no illness in it. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd al-Tawil except Uthman ibn Abdillah al-Ataki; Ubayd ibn Waqid alone narrated it."
"6099","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Tha'lab al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Fazara, from Miqsam or Said ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: These words are a remedy for every disease: I seek refuge in the perfect words of Allah and in all His names in general from the evil of the poisonous and the vermin, and from the evil of the harmful eye, and from the evil of an envier when he envies, and from the evil of Abu Qatara and his offspring; thirty-three angels came to their Lord and said: An ailment, an ailment in our land. He said: Take soil from your land, then wipe your sick one; it is the ruqya of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whoever takes a wage for it or conceals it from anyone will never prosper. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Mutamir ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"6100","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Tha'lab al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated to us, he said: Mutamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu Shuayb, from Uqba ibn Suhban who said: I said to Aisha: What about the saying of Allah, exalted be His mention: Then We caused to inherit the Book those We chose of Our servants; among them is one who wrongs himself, and among them is one who is moderate, and among them is one foremost in good deeds by permission of Allah, to the verse? She said: As for the foremost, he has passed during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he was testified Paradise; as for the moderate, whoever follows their traces and does like their deeds until he joins them; and as for the wrongdoer to himself, like me and like you and whoever follows us. She said: And all of them are in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Uqba ibn Suhban except Abu Shuayb al-Salt ibn Dinar; Mutamir alone narrated it."
"6101","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Tha'lab al-Basri narrated to me, he said: Ali ibn al-Husayn al-Dirhami narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Khaliq Abu Hani narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn al-Abras narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik who said: Umm Sulaym used to treat the wounded in the army of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would supplicate to Allah for my son. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Unays? She said: Yes. So he seated me before him and wiped over my head and said: O Unays, the Muslims will found cities after me; among what they found is a city called Basra. If you come to it, beware of its lowlands, its market, and the gate of its ruler, for there will be in it collapse, transformation, and pelting; the sign of that time is that justice dies, injustice spreads, adultery increases, and false testimony spreads. This hadith is not narrated from Ziyad al-Abras except with this chain."
"6102","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Tha'lab al-Basri the grammarian narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Hammam narrated to us, from Sufyan ibn Uyayna and Mansur ibn al-Mutamir, and Bakr ibn Wail, and Ziyad ibn Sad, from al-Zuhri, from Salim, from his father who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr and Umar and Uthman walking in front of the funeral. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur ibn al-Mutamir and Bakr ibn Wail except Hammam, and none narrated it from Hammam except Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri and Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi."
"6103","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Tha'lab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Nafi who said: It was said to Ibn Umar: You pray on your mount when heading to Makka, so why do you do that when returning to Madina? He said: Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do it, I would not do it. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Attab ibn Bashir; al-Muqri alone narrated it."
"6104","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Tha'lab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Marwan ibn Muawiya al-Fazari narrated to us, from Wail ibn Dawud, from Abdillah al-Bahi, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fed Khadija from the grapes of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Bahi except Wail ibn Dawud; Marwan ibn Muawiya alone narrated it."
"6105","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman Tha'lab narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Muqri narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Abu al-Sha'tha, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married his aunt's daughter Maymuna while in ihram. No one among those who narrated it from Ibn Jurayj inserted between Ata and Ibn Abbas Abu al-Sha'tha in this hadith except Said ibn Salim al-Qaddah."
"6106","Muhammad ibn Raja ibn Muhammad al-Udhri narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus al-Hafari narrated to us, he said: Hasan ibn Ayyash, brother of Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash, narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abdillah ibn Aqil, from al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution and wiped his head once. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Ayyash except Abd al-Rahman ibn Yunus; al-Abbas alone narrated it."
"6107","Muhammad ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Hatim narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Sadir al-Madaini narrated to us, he said: Fudayl ibn Sulayman al-Numayri narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Qarawanda, he said: Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa narrated to us, from his father who said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Farewell Hajj, and we kept praying two rak'as, two rak'as, until we returned. No one narrated this hadith from Kathir ibn Qarawanda except Fudayl ibn Sulayman, nor from Fudayl except Abd al-Rahman ibn Abd al-Aziz; al-Abbas alone narrated it."
"6108","Muhammad ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: al-Abbas ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Muhammad al-Muaddib narrated to us, he said: Harun ibn Musa the grammarian narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Shabi, from Alqama, from Abu al-Darda, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recite: By the male and the female. No one narrated this hadith from Harun the grammarian except Yunus ibn Muhammad; al-Abbas alone narrated it."
"6109","Muhammad ibn Abdus al-Hashimi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Salim al-Qaddah narrated to us, from Abu Yunus, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful. Ali ibn Harb said: Ismail ibn Aban narrated to me. Abu al-Qasim al-Tabarani said: Abu Yunus was only called al-Qawi due to his strength in worship; he stood until he was made to sit, wept until he went blind, and fasted until he became like wood. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Yunus except Said ibn Salim al-Qaddah; Ali ibn Harb alone narrated it."
"6110","Muhammad ibn Abdus al-Hashimi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Harb al-Mawsili narrated to us, he said: al-Muafa ibn al-Minhal al-Armani narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Said al-Rabai narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Jubayra ibn Mahmud ibn Abi Jubayra al-Ansari, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Jubayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child is a master for seven years, and a servant for seven years, and a minister for seven years; if you are pleased with his companionship at twenty-one, otherwise strike his side, for you have excused yourself to Allah, mighty and majestic. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Ali ibn Harb alone narrated it."
"6111","Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Bahili al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Baqiyya al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Ghaniyya narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Umar, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Yaqub (peace be upon him) had a devoted brother. He said to him one day: O Yaqub, what took away your sight, and what bent your back? He said: As for what took my sight, it is weeping over Yusuf, and as for what bent my back, it is grief over Binyamin. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and said: O Yaqub, Allah, mighty and majestic, sends you greetings of peace and says to you: Are you not ashamed to complain of Me to others? Yaqub said: I only complain of my suffering and grief to Allah. Jibril said: Allah knows best what you complain of, O Yaqub. Then Yaqub said: My Lord, will You not have mercy on the old man? You took my sight and bent my back, so return to me Yusuf, my sweet basil, that I may smell him once before death, then do with me, my Lord, as You will. Then Jibril (peace be upon him) came to him and said: O Yaqub, Allah sends you greetings of peace and says to you: Rejoice, and let your heart be glad; by My might, had they both been dead I would have resurrected them for you. So make food for the poor, for the most beloved of My servants to Me are the poor. And do you know why I took your sight and bent your back, and why the brothers of Yusuf did what they did to him? You slaughtered a sheep, then a fasting poor man came to you and you did not feed him anything from it. Afterwards, when lunch came to Yaqub he would order a caller to call: Whoever among the poor wants lunch, let him have lunch with Yaqub; and if he was fasting he would order a caller to call: Whoever among the poor is fasting, let him break his fast with Yaqub. This hadith is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Wahb ibn Baqiyya alone narrated it."
"6112","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yazid ibn Habib al-Muqri al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Dinar ibn Abdillah, freedman of Anas ibn Malik, narrated to us, he said: My master Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Blessed is he who saw me, and who saw one who saw me, and who saw one who saw one who saw me, three times."
"6113","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi al-Basri narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Zarir narrated to us, he said: I heard Abu Raja say: I heard Ibn Abbas say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ibn Said: I have hidden something for you. He said: It is al-dukh. He said: Be off. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Raja except Salm ibn Zarir."
"6114","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, he said: Iyas ibn Salama ibn al-Akwa narrated to us, he said: My father said: We used to pray with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Friday, and the walls had no shade to seek shade in. This hadith is not narrated from Salama ibn al-Akwa except with this chain; Yala ibn al-Harith alone narrated it."
"6115","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Abu al-Walid al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Usm, Abu Ulwan, from Ibn Abbas who said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commanded with fifty prayers, then he asked his Lord to make them five prayers. No one narrated this hadith from Abdillah ibn Usm except Sharik."
"6116","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aisha al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Huzayl ibn Shurahbil, from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting while two sheep fed, then one butted the other and caused it to miscarry. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, and it was said to him: What makes you laugh? He said: I marvel at her; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, retribution will surely be taken for her on the Day of Resurrection. Huzayl ibn Shurahbil narrated no hadith from Abu Dharr other than this, and none narrated it from Huzayl except Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan Abu Qays, nor from Abu Qays except Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, nor from Layth except Hammad ibn Salama and Sadaqa ibn Musa al-Daqiqi."
"6117","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn Bukayr al-Tayalisi narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Ukkasha al-Kirmani say: Muawiya ibn Hammad al-Kirmani informed us, from al-Zuhri who said: Whoever bathes on Friday night and prays two rak'as reciting in them a thousand times: Say, He is Allah, One, then sleeps in purity, sees the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream. Muhammad ibn Ukkasha said: I persisted in it for more than two years, bathing every Friday night, praying two rak'as reciting in them: Say, He is Allah, One, a thousand times, hoping to see the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dream. Then I prayed one Friday night two rak'as, reciting in them a thousand times, and when I lay down a wet dream befell me, so I got up, bathed, and prayed two rak'as reciting a thousand times. When I finished them it was the time of sahar; I leaned against the wall facing the qibla, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me in that description, wearing two Yemeni cloaks, wrapped with one and cloaked with the other. He came and sat upon his left leg and set up the right. Muhammad ibn Ukkasha said: I wanted to say: May Allah greet you, but he began before me and said: May Allah greet you. I loved to see his broken front tooth, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled and I looked at his broken incisor. I said: O Messenger of Allah, the jurists have confused me, and I have with me two roots of the Sunna; shall I present them to you? He said: Yes. I said: Contentment with the decree of Allah, submission to the command of Allah, patience upon His judgment, taking what Allah commanded, forbidding what Allah forbade, sincerity of action for Allah, belief in destiny, its good and evil from Allah, abandoning argument and dispute in religion, wiping over the socks, jihad with every caliph, Friday prayer with every righteous and wicked one, prayer over whoever of the people of the qibla dies, belief is word and deed, increasing and decreasing, the Quran is the speech of Allah uncreated, patience under the banner of the ruler whatever justice or injustice is in him, no revolt against rulers with the sword even if they are unjust, no one of the people of the qibla is assigned Paradise or Hell, no one of the people of tawhid is declared disbeliever even if they commit major sins, refraining from the faults of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the best of people after the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is Abu Bakr, then Umar. Muhammad ibn Ukkasha said: I stopped at Uthman and Ali, for I feared the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to prefer Uthman over Ali. I said to myself: Ali is his cousin, and Uthman is his son-in-law. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled as though he knew, then said: Uthman, then Ali. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is the Sunna; hold to it. He joined his fingers and made ninety-three, joining his thumb over his fingers. Muhammad ibn Ukkasha said: I presented these roots to him three nights; each night I stopped at Ali and Uthman, and he smiled at my stopping as though he knew (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then said: Uthman, then Ali; hold to it. Muhammad ibn Ukkasha said: I used to present these roots to him while his eyes shed tears; when I said: And refraining from the faults of the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he sobbed until his voice rose (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Muhammad ibn Ukkasha said: After my dream I found sweetness in my mouth and heart; I went eight days without eating food until I weakened from the obligatory prayer, and when I ate food that sweetness left my mouth."
"6118","Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan ibn Shibl Abu Shubayl narrated to us, he said: al-Numan ibn Shibl narrated to me, he said: Abdillah al-Makhzumi narrated to me, from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cut off for a shield worth three dirhams. No one narrates this hadith from Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn Sad except Abdillah ibn Jafar al-Makhzumi; al-Numan ibn Shibl alone narrated it."
"6119","Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan ibn Shibl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Rawq narrated to us, from his father, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, concerning the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: None knows them except a few. Ibn Abbas said: I am among those few: Maksalimlitha, and Tamlikha, and he is the one sent with the coins to the city, and Martulus, and Yathbunus, and Dhar-tunus, and Kafashtitus, and Mantanwas-isus, and he is the shepherd; and the dog's name is Qitmir, below the Kurdi and above the Qibti; I do not think above the Qibti. Abu Shubayl said: My father said: I have heard that whoever writes these names on something and throws it into a fire, the fire subsides. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Rawq except his son Yahya."
"6120","Muhammad ibn Muhammad ibn al-Numan ibn Shibl narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to me, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Numan ibn Abd al-Rahman, my father's uncle, narrated to me, from Yahya ibn al-Ala al-Razi, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya, from Mujahid, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever visits the grave of his parents or one of them every Friday is forgiven and recorded as dutiful. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Yahya ibn al-Ala alone narrated it."
"6121","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Jafar ibn Sulayman ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from his father, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, is there any supplication that is not rejected? He said: Yes; you say: I ask You by Your Highest, Mightiest, Most Sublime, Most Generous Name. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Yaqub ibn Jafar alone narrated it."
"6122","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Yaqub ibn Jafar ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to me, from my grandfather, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas who said: Uthman said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me when he married me his other daughter: Had I ten I would have married them to you one after another, and I am indeed pleased with you. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas from Uthman except with this chain; Yaqub ibn Jafar alone narrated it."
"6123","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Karran narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Suhban narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek good from those with beautiful faces. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Umar ibn Suhban; Sulayman ibn Karran alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Jabir except with this chain."
"6124","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Israil informed us, from al-Harith ibn Hasira, from Ibn Burayda, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he saw a man afflicted and said: Perhaps you asked Him to hasten the affliction for you. He said: Yes. He said: Why did you not ask Allah for well-being and say: O Allah, give us good in this world and good in the Hereafter and shield us from the punishment of the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from al-Harith ibn Hasira except Israil, and it is not narrated from Burayda except with this chain."
"6125","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Bashshar al-Ramadi narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Misar ibn Kidam, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Umar, from his father Umar, from his father Abd al-Aziz ibn Marwan, from Asma bint Umays, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gathered the Banu Abd al-Muttalib and said to them: If any of you is struck by worry, grief, distress, illness, or hardship, let him say: Allah is my Lord, I associate nothing with Him, three times. He said: And that was the last speech of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz at death. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyayna except al-Ramadi."
"6126","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bistam al-Asfar narrated to us, he said: Ashath ibn Barraz al-Hujaymi narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Detachment from this world comforts the heart and body. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Ashath ibn Barraz; Yahya ibn Bistam alone narrated it."
"6127","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aisha al-Taymi narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Kufi narrated to us, from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would give salam to his right until the whiteness of his right cheek was seen: Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah, and to his left likewise. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, except Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahman and Muhammad ibn Aban."
"6128","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Muhammad Abu al-Jamal narrated to us, whose origin was Yamami and who lived in Basra, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no ihram on a woman except in her face. No one raised this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Ayyub Abu al-Jamal; Abdillah ibn Raja alone narrated it."
"6129","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Ayyub informed me, from al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth, from Umar ibn Sad, from his father who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: I marvel at the believer: if good befalls him he praises Allah and thanks, and if calamity befalls him he praises his Lord and is patient; and in all of it the believer is rewarded, even in a morsel he lifts to his mouth. No one narrated this hadith from Jarir ibn Ayyub except Ibn Raja."
"6130","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Raja narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Ayyub informed us, he said: Amir ibn Sad al-Bajali narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Bara ibn Azib say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will come to you from this mountain pass the best of Dhu Yaman, with the touch of an angel on his face. He said: There was no man among the people but wished to be him, when a rider appeared before them. He came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), dismounted, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), took his hand, greeted him, pledged to him, and emigrated. He said: Who are you? He said: I am Jarir ibn Abdillah al-Bajali. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated him beside him, wiped with his hand over his head, face, chest, and belly until Jarir bent from shyness lest he put his hand under his waist-wrapper, while supplicating for blessing for him and his offspring; then he wiped his head and back while supplicating for him. No one narrated this hadith from Amir ibn Sad al-Bajali except Jarir ibn Ayyub."
"6131","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Bistam al-Asfar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Uthman al-Qurashi narrated to us, from Jami ibn Thawb, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Abu Umama who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to us and said: I am the best of people for the worst of my umma. We said: O Messenger of Allah, how are you for the best of it? He said: As for the best of my umma, they enter Paradise by their deeds; as for the worst of them, they enter Paradise by my intercession. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umama except with this chain; Yahya ibn Bistam alone narrated it."
"6132","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suwiyya al-Minqari narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Ikrash narrated to me, from his father Ikrash ibn Dhuayb who said: Banu Murra ibn Ubayd sent me with the charities of their wealth to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I came to him in Madina and found him sitting between the Muhajirun and the Ansar, and I brought camels like the roots of the mata plant. He said: Who is the man? I said: Ikrash ibn Dhuayb. He said: Go up in lineage. I said: Son of Hurqus ibn Jada ibn Amr ibn al-Nazzal ibn Murra ibn Ubayd; these are the charities of Banu Murra ibn Ubayd. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) smiled, then said: These are the camels of my people; these are the charities of my people. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered them branded with the brand of charity camels and joined to them. Then he took my hand and went with me to the house of Umm Salama and said: Is there any food? We were brought a large bowl of tharid and wazr, and we ate from it. I began striking with my hand at its sides, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized my right hand with his left and said: O Ikrash, eat from one place, for it is one food. Then we were brought a dish with kinds of fresh dates, and I ate from before me while the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) moved about the dish. Then he said: O Ikrash, eat from wherever you wish, for it is not one food. Then we were brought water, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) washed his hands, wiped his face, forearms, and head with the wetness of his palms, then said: O Ikrash, such is ablution from what fire has touched. This hadith is not narrated from Ikrash ibn Dhuayb except with this chain; al-Ala ibn al-Fadl ibn Abi Suwiyya alone narrated it."
"6133","Muhammad ibn Zakariyya al-Ghallabi narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn al-Fadl ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from his father Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Suwiyya al-Minqari who said: I witnessed Qays ibn Asim giving counsel; he gathered his sons, thirty-two males, and said: O my sons, when I die, make your eldest your chief and you will succeed your father; do not make your youngest your chief lest that lower you before your peers. Do not set up a wailing woman over me, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid wailing. And tend your wealth, for it alerts the generous and makes one independent of the miser. Do not give away the necks of camels except in their due, nor withhold them from their due. Beware every root of evil; whatever day delights you, what grieves you is more. Beware the sons of your enemies, for they are your enemies upon the way of their fathers. When I die, bury me in a place where this clan of Bakr ibn Wail cannot see me, for there were skirmishes between me and them in Jahiliyya, and I fear they will exhume me from my grave and you will spoil their worldly life and they will spoil your Hereafter. Then he called for his quiver and ordered his eldest son, named Ali: Take out an arrow from my quiver; he took it out and he said: Break it, and he broke it. Then he said: Take out two arrows; he took them out and said: Break them, and he broke them. He said: Take out three arrows; he took them out and said: Bind them with a bowstring; he bound them, then said: Break them, and he could not break them. He said: O my sons, thus you are with unity, and thus you are with division. Then he composed poetry. This hadith with this completeness and poetry is not narrated except with this chain; al-Ala ibn al-Fadl ibn Abi Suwiyya al-Minqari alone narrated it."
"6134","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Jumay narrated to us, from Mughira, from Ibrahim, from Alqama, from Abdillah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The camel is for seven and the cow for seven in sacrifices. No one narrated this hadith from Mughira except Hafs ibn Jumay; Umar ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"6135","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bakkai narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sleeps past a prayer or forgets it, let him pray it when he remembers it. Then he recited: And establish prayer for My remembrance. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Muhammad ibn Ishaq, nor from Muhammad ibn Ishaq except Ziyad ibn Abdillah; Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli alone narrated it."
"6136","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Thumama ibn Ubayda narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard a man say: Labbayk on behalf of Shubruma. He said: Did you perform Hajj for yourself? He said: No. He said: Perform Hajj for yourself, then perform Hajj for Shubruma. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Thumama ibn Ubayda."
"6137","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Sulayman al-Dubai narrated to us, from Said al-Jurayri, from Bahr ibn Marrar, from Yusuf ibn Abdillah ibn Salam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The worst of usury is one of you disparaging the honor of his Muslim brother. No one narrated this hadith from Bahr ibn Marrar except Said al-Jurayri, nor from al-Jurayri except Jafar ibn Sulayman; Umar ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"6138","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Asim ibn Sulayman al-Kuzi narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfa ibn Asid Abu Sariha al-Ghifari, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) looked at the House he said: O Allah, increase this House of Yours in honor, veneration, nobility, righteousness, and awe; and increase whoever honors and venerates it among those who perform Hajj or Umra in veneration, honor, nobility, righteousness, and awe. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Asim ibn Sulayman; Umar ibn Yahya alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Abu Sariha except with this chain."
"6139","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Ghassan narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When the Day of Resurrection comes, deeds will be brought in sealed scrolls, and the Blessed and Exalted will say: Accept this and leave this. The angels will say: By Your might, we wrote only what he did. He says: You spoke truthfully; his deed was for other than My Face, and today I accept only what was for My Face. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Imran al-Jawni except al-Harith ibn Ghassan."
"6140","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Ghassan narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every newborn is born upon the fitra. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except al-Harith ibn Ghassan."
"6141","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The first thing placed in the servant's scale is his spending on his family. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan."
"6142","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Hamid ibn al-Hasan al-Hilali narrated to us, from Nahshal ibn Said, from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: A safeguard for my umma from drowning when they board ships or the sea is to say: In the name of Allah the King, And they did not esteem Allah as He deserves, and the earth entirely will be His grip on the Day of Resurrection and the heavens folded in His right hand; glory be to Him and exalted above what they associate, In the name of Allah is its course and its anchorage; indeed my Lord is Forgiving, Merciful. No one narrated this hadith from al-Dahhak ibn Muzahim except Nahshal ibn Said."
"6143","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Hakim ibn Hizam narrated to us, from Abu Janab, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Among the obligations of Allah are three: when he sees a right of Allah he does not delay it to days he may not reach, and that he does righteous deed openly upon the foundation of his deed in secret, while combining with what he does the righteousness of what he hopes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Such is the friend of Allah, and he clasped his hand thirty. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Hakim ibn Hizam alone narrated it."
"6144","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Yahya al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Kathir Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim Abu Umayya, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never addressed us but he commanded us with charity and forbade us mutilation. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Yahya ibn Kathir."
"6145","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Layth al-Haddadi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ismail narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The cupper and the cupped have broken their fast. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, nor from al-Hasan except Musa ibn Ismail; Muhammad ibn al-Layth alone narrated it."
"6146","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Jundayshaburi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Bazi narrated to us, from Sadaqa ibn Abi Imran, from Abd al-Malik ibn Abi Sulayman, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The child retains his preemption until he comes of age; when he comes of age, if he wishes he takes and if he wishes he leaves. No one narrated this hadith from Sadaqa ibn Abi Imran except Abdillah ibn Bazi; Abdillah ibn Rashid alone narrated it."
"6147","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Jundayshaburi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Ubaydullah ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, from Umar ibn Dharr, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade leasing land except for gold or silver. This hadith is not narrated from Umar ibn Dharr except with this chain; Abdillah ibn Rashid alone narrated it."
"6148","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Muhammad al-Jundayshaburi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Rashid narrated to us, he said: Abu Ubayda Mujjaa ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Abi Imran al-Asadi, from Abu Wail Shaqiq ibn Salama, from Ali ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be at the end of time young in age, foolish in minds, speaking the best of speech; they pass through religion as the arrow passes through the game; they are the worst of creation and creatures, and blessed is he who kills them or whom they kill. No one narrated this hadith from Muslim except Mujjaa ibn al-Zubayr; Abdillah ibn Rashid alone narrated it."
"6149","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Ala narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from al-Ashath ibn Thurmula, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Faith restrains treacherous killing. No one inserted in this hadith from Yunus between al-Hasan and al-Zubayr al-Ashath ibn Thurmula except Abd al-Ala; Nasr ibn Ali alone narrated it."
"6150","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Hawshab al-Rahai narrated to us, he said: Salm ibn Sulayman al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Abu Hurra narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come peoples from the east reciting the Quran, it will not pass their collarbones; they scatter it like the scattering of inferior dates; they exit religion and do not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch; shaving is widespread among them. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurra except Salm ibn Sulayman."
"6151","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Azhar ibn Jamil narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Zuray narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The best of you are the best of you to their families. No one narrated this hadith from Rawh except Yazid; Azhar ibn Jamil alone narrated it."
"6152","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abda al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Muhammad al-Darawardi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sprinkled water over the grave of his son Ibrahim. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwa except al-Darawardi; Ahmad ibn Abda alone narrated it."
"6153","Muhammad ibn Zuhayr al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Abu Burayd Amr ibn Yazid al-Jarmi narrated to us, he said: al-Sumayd ibn Wahib narrated to us, he said: Shuba narrated to us, from Marwan al-Asfar, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, came from Yemen, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: With what did you enter ihram? He said: With the ihram of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I not had the sacrificial animal with me I would have exited ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Shuba except al-Sumayd ibn Wahib; Abu Burayd alone narrated it."
"6154","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Ubulli al-Muaddib narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Fazari al-Massisi narrated to us, he said: Hushaym narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Among my honor with my Lord is that I was born circumcised, and no one has seen my private parts. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Hushaym; Sufyan ibn Muhammad al-Fazari alone narrated it."
"6155","Muhammad ibn Mahan al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Adi narrated to us, from Awf, from Muhammad ibn Sirin who said: When Anas narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and finished, he said: Or as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said. No one narrated this hadith from Awf except Ibn Abi Adi."
"6156","Muhammad ibn Mahan al-Ubulli narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Habib ibn Nudba narrated to us, he said: Abu Janab Yahya ibn Abi Hayya narrated to us, from Abu al-Aliya, from Abu Umama who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I entered Paradise and heard a movement before me. I said: O Jibril, what is this movement? He said: Bilal walking ahead of you. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Aliya except Abu Janab al-Kalbi."
"6157","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti Abu Hanifa narrated to us, he said: my uncle Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan ibn Abi Hanifa narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Use ithmid at sleep, for it clears sight and grows hair. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Khalid al-Wasiti except Muhammad ibn Mahan; his son alone narrated it from him."
"6158","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Talha ibn Zayd, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Bilal ibn Sad, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever covers a private part, it is as though he revived a buried girl from her grave. No one narrated this hadith from Bilal ibn Sad except al-Wadin, nor from al-Wadin except Talha ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6159","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Talha ibn Zayd narrated to us, from al-Wadin ibn Ata, from Umayr ibn Hani, from Junada ibn Abi Umayya, from Ubada ibn al-Samit who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: There will be trials in which the believer cannot change with hand nor tongue. Ali ibn Abi Talib said: O Messenger of Allah, does that diminish their faith? He said: No, except as the drop diminishes the waterskin. He said: And why is that? He said: They hate it in their hearts. No one narrated this hadith from al-Wadin ibn Ata except Talha ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6160","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Talha ibn Musarrif, from Salim ibn Abi al-Jad, from Abdillah ibn Amr ibn al-As who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever comes to his house and is met with injustice, then fights and is killed, is killed a martyr; and whoever is asked for charity and gives, then is aggressed against, then fights and is killed, is killed a martyr. No one narrated this hadith from Talha ibn Musarrif except Sulayman ibn Khalid; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6161","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Hafs al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Abu Qatada al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not accept prayer except with purification, nor charity from misappropriation. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Sad except Abu Qatada al-Harrani, and it is not narrated from al-Zubayr except with this chain."
"6162","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Hafs al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, from Misar, from Atiyya, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah takes his sight and he is patient and expects reward, it is Allah's binding duty that his eyes not see the Fire. No one narrates this hadith from Misar except Jafar ibn Awn; Wahb ibn Hafs alone narrated it."
"6163","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Talha ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Sinan, from Yazid ibn Jabir al-Dimashqi, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever recites the sura in which the Family of Imran is mentioned on Friday, Allah and His angels send blessings upon him until the sun sets. No one narrated this hadith from Yazid ibn Jabir except Yazid ibn Sinan, nor from Yazid ibn Sinan except Talha ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6164","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Khalaf ibn Khalifa narrated to us, from Aban the teacher, from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from al-Hakam ibn Mina, from Yazid ibn Jariya al-Ansari who said: We were sitting around the couch of Muawiya, and he said: What were you talking about? They said: We were in a talk from the talk of the Ansar. He said: Shall I not narrate to you a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? They said: Yes. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever loves the Ansar, Allah loves him; and whoever hates the Ansar, Allah hates him. No one narrated this hadith from Aban the teacher except Khalaf ibn Khalifa; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6165","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Talha ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Abd al-Ala ibn Hilal al-Himsi, from Wathila ibn al-Asqa who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: The worst of lies is one who claims to other than his father, or lies upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), or lies upon his eyes. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus, nor from Yunus except Talha ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6166","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has land, let him cultivate it or grant it to his brother. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Hammad ibn Salama."
"6167","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Jabala al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Habib the judge narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Amr, from Abu Salama, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: In Paradise is a gate called al-Rayyan; none enters it on the Day of Resurrection except the fasting. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr except Umar ibn Habib; al-Hasan ibn Jabala alone narrated it."
"6168","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Jabala narrated to us, he said: Mihran ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik, that when the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) broke fast with a household he said: The fasting have broken fast with you, the righteous have eaten your food, and the angels descend upon you. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Mihran ibn Ishaq; al-Hasan ibn Jabala alone narrated it."
"6169","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mustamirr al-Uruqi narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn al-Hakam al-Jurashi narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two blessings in which many people are deceived: health and leisure. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan except Humayd ibn al-Hakam; Amr ibn Asim alone narrated it."
"6170","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Jushami al-Muqri al-Juri narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Haytham ibn Habib al-Sayrafi narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu Juhayfa who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man praying with his garment trailing, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew near him and folded his garment over him."
"6171","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Faraj al-Juri narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, from al-Haytham ibn Habib, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Sahl ibn Sad al-Saidi who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No Muslim sets out in the path of Allah, as a warrior or pilgrim, proclaiming or responding, but the sun sets with his sins and he exits them. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Haytham ibn Habib except Hafs ibn Abi Dawud; Ahmad ibn al-Faraj alone narrated them."
"6172","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Iyad informed us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah is not worshipped with anything better than understanding in religion; one jurist is harder on Satan than a thousand worshippers; everything has a pillar, and the pillar of this religion is understanding. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Yazid ibn Iyad."
"6173","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Shahin narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, even like a sandgrouse nest, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Ibn Abi Layla, nor from Ibn Abi Layla except al-Hakam ibn Zuhayr."
"6174","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, he said: Rabah ibn Abi Maruf narrated to me, from Qays ibn Sad, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man will enter Paradise, and no household or chamber will remain but will say: Welcome, welcome, welcome to us. Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you see this man to be on that day? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes, and you are he, O Abu Bakr. No one narrated this hadith from Qays ibn Sad except Rabah ibn Abi Maruf, nor from Rabah except Ibn Abi Fudayk; Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi alone narrated it."
"6175","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi narrated to us, from al-Nahhas ibn Qahm, from Ata ibn Abi Rabah, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian. No one narrated this hadith from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, except Nahhas ibn Qahm."
"6176","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Mansur al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays al-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: Hilal ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Umar ibn al-Khattab who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One who remembers Allah in Ramadan is forgiven, and one who asks Allah in it is not disappointed. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Zayd except Hilal ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abd al-Rahman ibn Qays alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Umar except with this chain."
"6177","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Hafs al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from al-Rabi ibn Anas, from Anas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever remembers Allah and his eyes overflow from fear of Allah until some of his tears reach the earth, Allah will not punish him on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Jafar al-Razi except Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud."
"6178","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Wahb ibn Hafs al-Harrani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sulayman ibn Abi Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Jafar al-Razi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Said ibn Jubayr, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has a night prayer and his eyes overcome him, Allah records for him the reward of that night, and his sleep is a charity from Allah upon him. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Said ibn Jubayr, from al-Aswad ibn Yazid, from Aisha, except Abu Jafar al-Razi; and Malik narrated it from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Said ibn Jubayr, from Aisha."
"6179","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Talha ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Safwan ibn Sulaym, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abdillah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): The angels said: Our Lord, You gave the children of Adam; they eat, drink, ride, and wear, while we glorify Your praise and do not eat, drink, or idle. As You made this world for them, make the Hereafter for us. He said: I do not make the offspring of one I created with My hands like one to whom I said: Be, and he was. No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Talha ibn Zayd and Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it from Talha ibn Zayd, and Hajjaj al-Awar alone narrated it from Abu Ghassan."
"6180","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Talha ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Yazid, from al-Zuhri, from Said ibn al-Musayyib, from Muawiya ibn al-Hakam al-Sulami, that he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I want to ask you about a matter I will ask no one after you: Who is our father? He said: Adam. He said: Who is our mother? He said: Hawwa. He said: Who is the father of the jinn? He said: Iblis. He said: Who is their mother? He said: His wife. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Yunus ibn Yazid, nor from Yunus except Talha ibn Zayd; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6181","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Salama ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu Farwa, from al-Rabi ibn Sabra al-Juhani, from his father who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muta with women. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Farwa except Salama ibn Salih; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6182","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Riyah narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Tawus, from his father, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to visit the House every night of the nights of Mina, then circumambulate and pray two rak'as for his circumambulation, and return to Mina before dawn overtook him. None narrated from Tawus except Umar ibn Riyah; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6183","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hamza ibn Jafar al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Samura the judge narrated to us, he said: Abu Shayba Ibrahim ibn Uthman narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Umm Salama who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you, is jihad upon us? He said: Yes; your jihad is this House, meaning Makka. No one narrated this hadith from Alqama ibn Marthad except Abu Shayba; Abu Samura alone narrated it."
"6184","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hamza ibn Jafar al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: Abu Samura the judge narrated to us, he said: Abu Shayba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Miqsam, from Ibn Abbas who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O company of Ansar, who is your chief? They said: Jadd ibn Qays, though we consider him miserly. He said: He is not your chief; rather your chief is Amr ibn al-Jamuh, and he was generous."
"6185","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hamza ibn Jafar narrated to us, he said: Abu Samura the judge narrated to us, he said: Abu Shayba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Muhammad ibn Kab al-Qurazi, from Abu Said al-Khudri who said: We bought a sacrifice, then a wolf attacked it and cut off its tip. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about that; he said: It does not matter; sacrifice it. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Hakam except Abu Shayba; Abu Samura alone narrated them."
"6186","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abada al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Haytham the cobbler narrated to us, he said: Abu Ali al-Rahabi narrated to us, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas who said: Among the supplication of Dawud the Prophet (peace be upon him) was: O Allah, I seek refuge in You from wealth that is a trial upon me, and from a child who is a burden upon me, and from an evil wife who brings gray hair before old age, and I seek refuge in You from an evil neighbor whose eyes watch me and whose ears listen to me; if he sees good he buries it, and if he sees evil he spreads it. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: An evil neighbor in the abode of residence is a back-breaker. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Abu Ali al-Rahabi alone narrated it, and he is Husayn ibn Abdillah ibn Ubaydillah ibn al-Abbas ibn Abd al-Muttalib."
"6187","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Nasr ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Abu Asim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Aswad, from Ibn Abi Mulayka, from Aisha, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married while in ihram. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn al-Aswad except Abu Asim."
"6188","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn al-Miqdam al-Ijli narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Waqid al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dhakwan, uncle of the children of Hammad ibn Zayd, narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Abdillah ibn Umar who said: While we sat in the courtyard of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a woman passed, and some of the people said: This is the daughter of Muhammad. Abu Sufyan said: The likeness of Muhammad among Banu Hashim is like sweet basil amid stench, or he said: straw. The woman went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him; he came out with anger known on his face and said: What is the matter with people who harm me regarding my family? Then he said: Allah created seven heavens and chose the highest and dwelt in it, and settled the rest of His heavens with whom He willed of His creation; and He created seven earths and chose the highest and settled in it whom He willed of His creation; then He created creation and chose from creation the children of Adam, and chose from the children of Adam the Arabs, and chose from the Arabs Mudar, and chose from Mudar Quraysh, and chose from Quraysh Banu Hashim, and chose me from Banu Hashim. I am from the best to the best; whoever loves the Arabs, for love of me he honors them, and whoever hates the Arabs, for hatred of me he hates them. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Dinar except Muhammad ibn Dhakwan, nor from Muhammad ibn Dhakwan except Hammad ibn Waqid, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain."
"6189","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Rawh ibn Qurra al-Yashkuri narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Khirash narrated to us, from al-Awwam ibn Hawshab, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to wear a white cap. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Umar except with this chain; Abdillah ibn Khirash alone narrated it."
"6190","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Mahan narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Learn knowledge, and learn for knowledge tranquility and dignity, and be humble to those you learn from."
"6191","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: my uncle narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, he said: Abbad ibn Kathir narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love your beloved moderately; perhaps he will be your hated one someday. And hate your hated one moderately; perhaps he will be your beloved someday. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abu al-Zinad except Abbad ibn Kathir; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated them."
"6192","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hamdun ibn Salm the cobbler narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mahan Abu Hanifa narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from Awn ibn Abdillah ibn Utba, from his father, from Ibn Masud who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the day of Hudaybiyya, and it rained that night heavily. When morning came the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do you know what your Lord said? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said it three times and they repeated. He said: Your Lord said: Whoever says: We were rained upon by such-and-such star, has disbelieved in Me and believed in that star; and whoever says: Allah gave us rain, has believed in Me and disbelieved in that star. No one narrated this hadith from Salih ibn Kaysan except Muslim ibn Khalid."
"6193","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Muawiya al-Hadhdha narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas who said: We sat with Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, and a funeral passed; he stood and we stood, then we prayed. He removed his sandals, and we said: O caliph of the Messenger of Allah, you removed your sandals while people wear their sandals. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever walks barefoot in obedience to Allah, Allah, mighty and majestic, will not ask him on the Day of Resurrection about what He obligated upon him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Muawiya al-Hadhdha al-Wasiti alone narrated it."
"6194","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Muawiya al-Hadhdha al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Habib narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Ghalib narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Alqama ibn Marthad, from Abu Habiba, from al-Ashath ibn Qays who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does not show mercy to the Muslims, Allah will not show mercy to him. No one narrated this hadith from Alqama ibn Marthad except Hisham ibn Abd al-Rahman, and it is not narrated from al-Ashath ibn Qays except with this chain."
"6195","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Dawud ibn Thabit narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mahan narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Atiyya narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seek refuge in Allah from the pit of sorrow. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the pit of sorrow? He said: A valley in Hell; Hell itself seeks refuge in Allah from the evil of that valley four hundred times each day; the deceivers are cast into it. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, who are the deceivers? He said: Those who show off with their deeds in the abode of this world. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Muhammad ibn al-Fadl; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6196","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad al-Habhabi narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Suwayd al-Maghuli narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan Abu al-Awwam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Aliya, from Ibn Abbas, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The worst food is the food of the wedding feast: the satiated is invited to it and the hungry is kept from it. No one narrated this hadith from Qatada except Imran al-Qattan, nor from Imran except Said ibn Suwayd; Abd al-Quddus ibn Muhammad alone narrated it."
"6197","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Mamar ibn Sahl al-Ahwazi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Ismail Abu Ismail al-Kufi narrated to us, he said: Kamil Abu al-Ala narrated to us, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat of reward, and whoever prays over it or walks with it until it is buried has two qarits, and the qirat is like Uhud. No one narrated this hadith from Kamil Abu al-Ala except Muhammad ibn Ismail al-Kufi; Mamar ibn Sahl alone narrated it."
"6198","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, he said: Rafia Abu Musa al-Saffar narrated to us, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas: Which charity is best? He said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I said: Which charity is best? He said: Water. I said: O Prophet of Allah, which charity is best? He said: Water; do you not see that when the people of the Fire seek help from the people of Paradise they call: Pour upon us some water or of what Allah has provided you? This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi alone narrated it."
"6199","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Ayyub ibn Waqid narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to hasten in the belly of al-Masil between al-Safa and al-Marwa. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Ayyub ibn Waqid."
"6200","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bakkai narrated to us, from Mansur, from Shaqiq ibn Salama, from Aisha who said: We used to place the vessel for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); he would pour upon his hand and wash it until clean, then pour with his right upon his left and wash his private parts, then pour upon his head three times, then bathe. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Ziyad ibn Abdillah al-Bakkai."
"6201","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: Thabit al-Bunani narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wanted to propose to a woman, he sent Umm Sulaym to look at her; she smelled her sides and looked at her ankles. This hadith is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi alone narrated it."
"6202","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Salih al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Sila ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Ashath ibn Abd al-Malik, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you eats or drinks forgetfully, let him complete his fast, for Allah fed him and gave him drink. No one narrated this hadith from Ashath except Sila ibn Sulayman."
"6203","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: I found in my grandfather's book in his handwriting: from Hushaym, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from his mother, from Umm Salama, that al-Hasan or al-Husayn urinated on the belly of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). They went to take him, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not interrupt my son, or: Do not hurry him. They left him until he finished his urine, then he called for water and poured it over it. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Hushaym; Muhammad ibn Mahan alone narrated it."
"6204","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Jabala al-Shirazi narrated to us, he said: Mujashi ibn Amr narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed at his first arrival in Madina by a bride with women, and one of them said: The club prospers. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say so, but say:. No one narrated this hadith from Layth ibn Sad except Mujashi ibn Amr, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain; and Ibn Abi Uways narrated it from his father, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amra, from Aisha."
"6205","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Jabala al-Shirazi informed us, he said: Ubayd ibn Amr al-Hanafi narrated to us, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayra, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has three daughters and maintains them, shelters them, and restrains them, Paradise is due for him. We said: And two? He said: And two. We said: And one? He said: And one. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Ubayd ibn Amr; al-Hasan ibn Jabala alone narrated it."
"6206","Muhammad ibn Hanifa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi narrated to us, he said: al-Mutamir ibn Nafi al-Hudhali narrated to us, he said: Sulayman al-Taymi narrated to us, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu Hurayra, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: No Muslim prays in a day and night twelve rak'as but Allah builds for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated the hadith from Sulayman al-Taymi except Mutamir ibn Nafi; Muhammad ibn Musa al-Harashi alone narrated it."
"6207","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Babasiri al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, he said: al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Khallad al-Saffar, from al-Hakam al-Nasri, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Juhayfa, from Ali who said: Two statements I memorized from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I love that you memorize them: Allah does not punish a sin in this world then Allah is too just to repeat His punishment; and what Allah pardons of a sin in this world, Allah is too generous to return to something He pardoned; and the veil between you and the jinn is: In the name of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq al-Sabii except al-Hakam al-Nasri and Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq; none narrated it from al-Hakam al-Nasri except Khallad al-Saffar; al-Hakam ibn Bashir ibn Sulayman alone narrated it, and al-Hajjaj al-Awar alone narrated it from Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq."
"6208","Muhammad ibn Musa al-Babasiri narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mihran al-Jammal narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salama al-Harrani narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abdillah ibn Abi Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from Abdillah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, that Umm Salama said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) married me and brought me together in Shawwal. This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salama except with this chain."
"6209","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kusa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: al-Ala ibn Salim narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Najjar narrated to us, he said: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, Umar said: I agreed with my Lord in three, and He agreed with me in three. I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is the station of our father Ibrahim; if only we took it as a prayer place. So Allah, mighty and majestic, revealed: And take from the station of Ibrahim a prayer place. No one narrated this hadith from Qurra ibn Khalid except Hafs ibn Umar al-Najjar al-Razi; al-Ala ibn Salim alone narrated it."
"6210","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kusa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hammad narrated to us, he said: Habib ibn Hassan ibn Abi al-Ashras narrated to us, from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: What about the saying of Allah, mighty and majestic: As We sent down upon the dividers, who are the dividers? He said: The Jews and Christians. He said: Those who made the Quran into parts, what is parts? He said: They believed in part and disbelieved in part. No one narrated this hadith from Habib ibn Hassan except Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar, and none raises it from Abu Zibyan except Habib ibn Hassan; and al-Amash narrated it from Abu Zibyan, from Ibn Abbas, mawquf."
"6211","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kusa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Mamar al-Bahrani narrated to us, he said: Humayd ibn Hammad ibn Khuwar narrated to us, he said: Misar ibn Kidam narrated to us, from Abdillah ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: Which people have the best voice with the Quran? He said: Whoever, when he recites, you see that he fears Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Misar except Humayd ibn Hammad; Muhammad ibn Mamar alone narrated it."
"6212","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kusa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Harb al-Nashai narrated to us, he said: Abu Marwan al-Ghassani narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uways who said: I was a merchant in Madina. I said: I come, and when I come to Madina Abu Hurayra meets me and asks me about Samura ibn Jundub, and when I come to Basra Samura asks me about Abu Hurayra. Abu Hurayra said: We were seven in a house, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon us and said: The last of you to die is in the Fire. None remained except I and Samura. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus ibn Ubayd except Abu Marwan Yahya ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Ghassani; Muhammad ibn Harb alone narrated it."
"6213","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kusa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Ismail ibn Ulayya narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Dawud al-Tai, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samura who said: People of Kufa spoke against Sad before Umar, saying he does not pray well. He said: Call Abu Ishaq to me. When he came, Umar said: These claim you do not pray well? He said: As for me, I pray with them the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not deviating from it; I prolong in the first two and shorten in the last two. He said: Such is the thought of you, O Abu Ishaq."
"6214","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kusa narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Ismail ibn Ulayya narrated to us, he said: my father narrated to us, from Dawud al-Tai, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Atiyya al-Qurazi who said: I was among those over whom Sad ibn Muadh judged. He looked at my pubic area and found it had not grown hair, so he released me. No one narrated this hadith from Dawud al-Tai except Ismail ibn Ulayya."
"6215","Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Kusa al-Wasiti narrated to us, he said: Hisham ibn Ammar narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Yazid al-Bakri narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Cool food, for hot food has no blessing. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhib except Abdillah ibn Yazid; Hisham alone narrated it."
"6216","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bishr al-Tinnisi narrated to us, he said: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Hassan ibn Atiyya, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us in his house and saw a disheveled man, and said: Could this not find what to wash his garment with and tidy his dishevelment. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Hassan ibn Atiyya; al-Awzai alone narrated it."
"6217","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yunus ibn Abi Yafur narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa, from his father who said: I was with my uncle before the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he preached, and he said: The affair of my umma will remain sound until twelve caliphs pass, and he lowered his voice with it. I said to my uncle, who was before me: What did he say, O uncle? He said: All of them from Quraysh. No one narrated this hadith from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa except Yunus ibn Abi Yafur, and it is not narrated from Abu Juhayfa except with this chain."
"6218","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from Amr ibn Shuayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Waive the prescribed punishments among you; whatever reaches me has become due. No one narrates this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ismail ibn Ayyash."
"6219","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Umar al-Allaf al-Razi narrated to us, he said: Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, from Abu Khalda who said: I heard Maymun al-Kurdi while he was with Malik ibn Dinar; Malik ibn Dinar said to him: Why does the shaykh not narrate from his father, for your father met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard from him? He said: My father would not narrate to us from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) fearing to add or omit. And he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies upon me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire. But I will narrate to you from him a hadith I heard him narrate more than once, twice, or thrice. He says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Any man who marries a woman, marrying her on the day he marries her while intending not to give her dowry, will meet Allah, mighty and majestic, on the Day of Resurrection as an adulterer; and any man who borrows a debt intending not to repay it, then dies without repaying it, will meet Allah, blessed and exalted, as a thief. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Khalda except Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, and it is not narrated from Abu Maymun al-Kurdi except with this chain."
"6220","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abu Imran al-Jawni, from Anas ibn Malik who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: While I sat, Jibril (peace be upon him) came, pushed between my shoulders, and I stood to a tree with like two bird nests; he sat in one and I sat in the other. It rose and ascended until it blocked the horizons, while I turned my glance; had I wished to touch the sky I would have touched it. I turned, and Jibril (peace be upon him) was like a lowly mat; I recognized the superiority of his knowledge of Allah over me. A gate of heaven opened for me and I saw the greatest light, and below me the veil shimmered with pearls and rubies; Allah revealed to me what He willed to reveal. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Imran al-Jawni except al-Harith."
"6221","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Zubaydi Abu Huma narrated to us, he said: Abu Qurra Musa ibn Tariq narrated to us, from Zamaa ibn Salih, from Ziyad ibn Sad, from Aban who said: Ata ibn al-Saib narrated to me, from his father, from Abdillah ibn Amr, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Two traits no Muslim servant maintains in his day and night but Allah admits him to Paradise; they are easy, yet few maintain them. They said: What are they, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The servant's tasbih after each prayer ten times, tahmid ten, tahlil ten; they are one hundred fifty in his day and night, and with Allah fifteen hundred good deeds; and he says tasbih thirty-three, tahmid thirty-three, takbir thirty-four; that is one hundred, and with Allah a thousand good deeds; that is two thousand five hundred good deeds. They said: O Messenger of Allah, why do we not maintain that? He said: When one of you finishes his prayer Satan comes to him, reminds him of his needs, and he stands before saying them; and when he goes to his bed he comes, distracts him from them until he sleeps. No one narrated this hadith from Ziyad ibn Sad except Zamaa; Abu Qurra alone narrated it."
"6222","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Salama narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Arfaja ibn Abd al-Wahid, from Asim ibn Abi al-Najud, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, that Abdillah ibn Masud said: In the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) we called it al-Mania; in the Book of Allah, mighty and majestic, it is a sura; whoever recites it every night has done much and well, meaning: Tabarak. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih except Ibn Abi Hazim."
"6223","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Qawwas narrated to us, he said: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah, from Ibn Abbas who said: A man of Banu Fazara disputed with me about the man Musa followed. I said: He is al-Khidr. The Fazari said: He is another man. Ubayy ibn Kab passed by us. Ibn Abbas said: I called him and asked him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mention the one Musa followed (peace be upon him)? He said: Yes; I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: While Musa sat among the assembly of Banu Israil, a man said to him: Is there any man more knowledgeable of Allah than you? He said: Whom do you see? Allah reproached him since he did not refer the matter to Him, and Allah revealed: Rather My servant al-Khidr. He asked the way to him; Allah made the fish a sign for him when he missed it, and what Allah narrated of his affair happened. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar ibn Muhammad except Muslim ibn Khalid and Abdillah ibn Maymun al-Qaddah."
"6224","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Salama narrated to us, and Ali ibn Ishaq al-Wazir al-Asbahani narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Zanbur al-Makki narrated to us; both said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Musa ibn Uqba, from Asim ibn Abi Ubayd, from Umm Salama, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he used to supplicate with these words: O Allah, You are the First, nothing before You; You are the Last, nothing after You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of every creature whose forelock is in Your hand; I seek refuge in You from sin and laziness, from the punishment of the grave, the trial of wealth, the trial of poverty; I seek refuge in You from sin and debt. O Allah, purify my heart from sins as You purified the white garment from filth. O Allah, distance between me and my sin as You distanced between east and west. This is what Muhammad asked his Lord: O Allah, I ask You the best of asking, the best supplication, the best success, the best deed, the best reward, the best life, the best death; make me firm, weight my scales, raise my rank, accept my prayer, forgive my sin; I ask You the highest ranks of Paradise, Amen. O Allah, I ask You Paradise, Amen. O Allah, I ask You the best done, the best acted, the best hidden, the best manifest, and the highest ranks of Paradise, Amen. O Allah, raise my mention, lay down my burden, set right my affair, purify my heart, guard my chastity, illumine my heart, forgive my sin; I ask You the highest ranks of Paradise, Amen. O Allah, save me from the Fire. And the wording is of the hadith of Muhammad ibn Zanbur."
"6225","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ismail ibn Abdillah ibn Zurara al-Raqqi narrated to us, he said: Abu Ishaq al-Fazari narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Sufyan, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The teacher of good is asked forgiveness for by everything, even the fish in the seas. No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Ishaq al-Fazari."
"6226","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: al-Musayyib ibn Wadih narrated to us, he said: Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abdillah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the muqayn and the khimar. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Makhlad ibn al-Husayn; al-Musayyib ibn Wadih alone narrated it."
"6227","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Said ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Bakr ibn Sawada al-Judhami, from Salih ibn Khaywan, from Abu Sahla al-Saib ibn Khallad, that a man led people in prayer and spat toward the qibla while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) watched. When he finished, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let this one not pray for you. Afterwards he wanted to pray with them and they prevented him, informing him of the saying of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Well done what they did, and I think he said: You harmed Allah, or something like that. This hadith is not narrated from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Amr ibn al-Harith alone narrated it."
"6228","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight people until they say: There is no god but Allah. When they say: There is no god but Allah, they have protected from me their wealth and selves except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah."
"6229","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Snakes, we have not made peace with them since we warred with them; whoever sees any of them, let him kill it, for their Muslims will not appear to you; whoever leaves any of them from fear is not of us."
"6230","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not combine my name and kunya; I am Abu al-Qasim; Allah gives and I distribute."
"6231","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No commander of ten but will be brought on the Day of Resurrection shackled, until justice frees him or injustice destroys him."
"6232","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes a handspan of land without right will be collared with it on the Day of Resurrection from seven earths."
"6233","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayra who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If someone looks into your house and you throw a pebble at him and gouge his eyes, there is no sin upon you. No one narrated these hadiths from Abdillah ibn Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami."
"6234","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya narrated to us, he said: al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Aisha who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a bed woven with palm fronds, upon it a black cloth. We seated him upon the fronds; Abu Bakr and Umar entered upon him while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat upon it. They looked and saw the mark of the bed on the side of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr and Umar wept. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: What makes you weep? They said: We weep that this bed's roughness marked your side, while Kisra and Qaysar are upon silk and brocade. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The end of Kisra and Qaysar is to the Fire, and the end of this bed of mine is Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from al-Layth except Abd al-Aziz ibn Yahya."
"6235","Muhammad ibn Ali al-Saigh al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi narrated to us, he said: Bakkar ibn Abdillah, nephew of Musa ibn Ubayda al-Rabadhi, narrated to us, he said: Musa ibn Ubayda narrated to us, he said: Zayd ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from his mother Hujja bint Qurayt, from her mother Uqayla bint Ubayd ibn al-Harith who said: I and my mother Qurayra bint al-Harith al-Utwarriya came among Muhajir women, and we pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he had a tent pitched at al-Abtah. He took from us: that we associate nothing with Allah, the whole verse. When we affirmed and extended our hands to pledge to him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I do not touch women's hands. He sought forgiveness for us, and that was our pledge. This hadith is not narrated from Uqayla bint Ubayd except with this chain; Bakkar ibn Abdillah al-Rabadhi alone narrated it."
"6236","6230 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about it on the day of Arafah, and he said: It is a binding duty, meaning: al-Atirah. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except Sufyan, and no one narrated it from Sufyan except Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani."
"6237","6231 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muawiyah an-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever corrupts a slave against his master. No one narrated from Yahya ibn Sa'id except Muhammad ibn Dinar; Muhammad ibn Muawiyah is alone in transmitting it."
"6238","6232 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Zayd, from his father Zayd ibn al-Hasan, from his grandfather, he said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir saying: A beggar stopped at Ali ibn Abi Talib while he was bowing in a voluntary prayer, so he pulled off his ring and gave it to the beggar. Then he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and informed him of that, so this verse was revealed to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Your guardian is only Allah and His Messenger and those who believe, who establish prayer and give zakah while bowing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited it, then said: Whoever I am his mawla, Ali is his mawla; O Allah, befriend whoever befriends him and oppose whoever opposes him. This hadith is not narrated from Ammar ibn Yasir except with this chain; Khalid ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"6239","6233 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Abi Khalifah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Discourse on the Decree has been left for the wicked of this ummah. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, except Umar ibn Abi Khalifah; Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi is alone in transmitting it."
"6240","6234 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Marwazi narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When dinner is served and the prayer is established, begin with dinner. No one narrated this hadith from Ma'mar except Ibn al-Mubarak."
"6241","6235 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abdur-Rahman ibn Abdul-Aziz al-Imami al-Ansari narrated to me, from Ibn Shihab, from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from Abu Hurayrah, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A paternal aunt is not married over a brother's daughter, nor is a maternal aunt married over a sister's daughter. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad except Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir."
"6242","6236 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pray while traveling upon his mount. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Harith ibn Umayr; Ibrahim ash-Shafi'i is alone in transmitting it."
"6243","6237 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Waki' ibn al-Jarrah narrated to us, he said: Mis'ar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Harithah ibn Wahb al-Khuza'i, he said: We prayed Zuhr with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, when the people were at their most numerous and most secure, two rak'ahs. No one narrated this hadith from Mis'ar except Waki'; Ya'qub ibn Humayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6244","6238 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Mis'ar, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a man driving a sacrificial camel and said: Ride it. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except Muhammad ibn Abi Umar, and no one narrated it from Mis'ar, from al-Mukhtar ibn Fulful, except Sufyan. And the people narrated it from Mis'ar, from Bukayr ibn al-Akhnas."
"6245","6239 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Hatim ibn Isma'il narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Bahz ibn Hakim, from his father, from his grandfather, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be presented with muzzles upon your mouths, so the first thing of any one of you that will speak will be his hand and his thigh. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Hatim; Ya'qub ibn Humayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6246","6240 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, from Abu Salamah, from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to sleep while in a state of janabah, would perform the ablution of prayer, and when he wanted to eat, he would perform ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Ma'mar, from Qatadah, except Ibn al-Mubarak. And Abdur-Razzaq narrated it from Ma'mar, from az-Zuhri."
"6247","6241 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Mahdi ibn Ja'far ar-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Rushdayn ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Abu Aqil Zuhrah ibn Ma'bad, from his grandfather Abdullah ibn Hisham, he said: The Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to learn this supplication when the year or the month began: O Allah, bring it upon us with security and faith, safety and Islam, pleasure from the Most Merciful, and protection from Satan. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Hisham except with this chain; Rushdayn ibn Sa'd is alone in transmitting it."
"6248","6242 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that he heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam will prevail until merchants travel across the sea, and until horses plunge forth in the path of Allah. Then there will appear a people who recite the Qur'an, saying: Who recites better than us? Who is more understanding than us? Who is more knowledgeable than us? Then he said to his Companions: Is there any good in such people? They said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: They are from you, from this ummah, and they will be the fuel of the Fire. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Zayd ibn Aslam except Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari."
"6249","6243 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ahmad ibn Abdah ad-Dabbi narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Salih ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: My uncle Mansur ibn Abi al-Aswad narrated to us, he said: A shaykh known as Abu Muhammad narrated to me, he said: A shaykh called al-Muhajir narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn Maslamah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord has breezes in the days of time, so expose yourselves to them; perhaps one of you will be touched by a breeze and will never be wretched after it. This hadith is not narrated from Muhammad ibn Maslamah except with this chain; Ahmad ibn Abdah is alone in transmitting it."
"6250","6244 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Yusuf ibn Atiyyah as-Sa'di narrated to us, from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah, he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered al-Fadl ibn Abbas to prepare his purification water for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went off for his need, and when he had a need he would go far away until he could hardly be seen. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had relieved his need, he came back, and passed by a woman at the grave of one of her dead, counting her merits and wailing. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood over her while she did not know him, and said to her: Fear Allah and be patient. She said: O servant of Allah, go about your need. He said it to her three times, then left. He came and took the water vessel from al-Fadl. Al-Fadl stood and went to the woman and said to her: What did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say to you? She stood up and said: Woe to her? This is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I did not know him. She hastened until she caught up with him at the door of the mosque and said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, I did not know you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to her: Patience is at the first shock. He said it three times. No one narrated this hadith in its fullness from Ata ibn Abi Maymunah except Yusuf ibn Atiyyah; Sa'id ibn Mansur is alone in transmitting it."
"6251","6245 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Husayn narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Hasan ibn Hasan ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib narrated to me, from Abu Rafi', he said: Fatimah, daughter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), came with Hasan and Husayn to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during the illness in which he died, and said: These two are your sons, so bequeath them something. He said to her: As for Hasan, he shall have my steadfastness and my eminence, and as for Husayn, he shall have my girding and my generosity. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Rafi' except with this chain; Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari is alone in transmitting it."
"6252","6246 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Fulayh narrated to us, he said: Abu Ghassan Muhammad ibn Mutarrif narrated to me, from Umar ibn Nafi', from his father Nafi', freedman of Ibn Umar, that a man asked Abdullah ibn Umar, saying: My maternal uncle divorced his wife, and he was seized by grief over that, and a matter that weighed heavily upon him. I wanted to marry her, though he did not command me to do that nor know of it. Ibn Umar said: No, unless you marry a marriage of sincere desire: if she suits you, keep her, and if you dislike her, part from her. Otherwise, we used to count this in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as fornication. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Nafi' except Abu Ghassan."
"6253","6247 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Jabir, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw a boy upon whom something had been hung, and said: Why do you hang things upon your children? Use costus; dissolve it in water, then administer it through the nose. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Abdul-Aziz ad-Darawardi, and it is not narrated from Jabir, from A'ishah, except with this chain."
"6254","6248 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muhriz ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, from Alqamah ibn Marthad al-Hadrami, from Hafs ibn Ubaydillah ibn Anas, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: Fever was reviled one day in the presence of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile it, for by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it removes the sins of the believer just as the bellows remove the dross of iron. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah ibn Marthad except Musa ibn Ubaydah; Abdul-Aziz ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it. And Hafs ibn Ubaydillah ibn Anas did not narrate from Abu Hurayrah any hadith other than this."
"6255","6249 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Raja narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One suckling, nor two sucklings, make unlawful. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Abdullah ibn Raja."
"6256","6250 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Humaydah bint Ubadah al-Ansari, from her sister, from Uqbah ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and addressed the people upon the pulpit in Ramadan, saying: I have stood upon this pulpit, and I know the Night of Decree, so seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd nights. This hadith is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Malik except with this chain; Abdul-Aziz ibn Yahya is alone in transmitting it."
"6257","6251 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, that Qatadah ibn Di'amah narrated to him, from Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) promised her that she would pray inside the House, and ordered her to pray in the Hijr. She said: You promised me that I would pray inside the House. He said: It is part of the House; were it not that your people are recently removed from idolatry, I would have joined it to the House. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Amr ibn al-Harith."
"6258","6252 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Dawud al-Mikhraqi narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Abu Hasan, from al-Hakam ibn Abdullah, that Muhammad ibn Ka'b al-Qurazi narrated to him, that al-Hasan ibn Abi al-Hasan narrated to him that he heard Shurayh saying: Umar ibn al-Khattab said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will be sifted until you become the dregs of the people, whose covenants are confused and whose trusts are ruined. One of our speakers said: What shall become of us, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Act upon what you know and abandon what you disapprove, and say: One, One! Help us against whoever wrongs us, and suffice us against whoever oppresses us. This hadith is not narrated from Shurayh the judge except with this chain; Ya'qub ibn Humayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6259","6253 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muawiyah an-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayb ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, he said: I saw Uthman ibn Affan perform ablution and pass his fingers through his beard, then he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing ablution and passing his fingers through his beard. No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani except Shu'ayb ibn Ruzayq."
"6260","6254 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Abdus-Salam ibn Salih al-Harawi narrated to us, he said: Ali ibn Musa ibn Ja'far ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from his father, from Ja'far ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Ali ibn al-Husayn, from his father, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Faith is knowledge by the heart, affirmation by the tongue, and action by the pillars. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Abdus-Salam ibn Salih al-Harawi is alone in transmitting it."
"6261","6255 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak narrated to us, that he heard Abdur-Rahman ibn Hurmuz al-A'raj saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: Labbayka, God of truth. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak except Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari."
"6262","6256 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak narrated to us, from his father, from Muawiyah ibn Abi Sufyan, he said: I entered upon Umm Habibah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and found the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in a single garment, knotting it behind his neck. I said to Umm Habibah: Does the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray in a single garment? She said: Yes, and it is the one in which what happened had happened. No one narrated this hadith from Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak except Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari."
"6263","6257 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, he said: Attaf ibn Khalid narrated to us, he said: My brother Abdullah ibn Khalid informed me, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Abi Amrah, from his uncle Abdur-Rahman ibn Abi Amrah, he said: Uthman ibn Affan said to me: We used to say that attending the night prayer in congregation is better than standing half the night in prayer, and attending the dawn prayer is better than standing the whole night in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Abdur-Rahman ibn Amr ibn Abi Amrah except Abdullah ibn Khalid Abu Attaf, and none from Abdullah except his brother Attaf; Sa'id ibn Mansur is alone in transmitting it."
"6264","6258 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhriz ibn Salamah narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Maghrib at Muzdalifah, and when he made his camel kneel he said: Prayer is with an iqamah. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except ad-Darawardi."
"6265","6259 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muawiyah an-Naysaburi narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Harrani narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will come in the end of time peoples whose faces will be the faces of humans but whose hearts will be the hearts of devils, like ravenous wolves; there is nothing of mercy in their hearts. They shed blood, they do not refrain from anything foul: if you follow them they deceive you, if you hide from them they backbite you, if they speak to you they lie to you, and if you trust them they betray you. Their child is insolent, their youth is dissolute, and their elder neither commands right nor forbids wrong. Honor through them is humiliation, seeking what is in their hands is poverty. The forbearing among them is astray, the one who commands right among them is accused, the believer among them is oppressed, and the sinner among them is honored. The Sunnah among them is innovation, and innovation among them is Sunnah. At that, Allah will set their worst over them, and their best will supplicate and will not be answered. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Muhammad ibn Salamah; Muhammad ibn Muawiyah is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"6266","6260 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abdul-A'la narrated to us, he said: Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Tufayl, from Humayd, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he was in a house when a man peeped into his house, so he aimed an arrow at him, directing it toward him, and the man withdrew. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Tufayl, a Basran shaykh; Mu'tamir is alone in transmitting it."
"6267","6261 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, he said: al-Mughirah ibn Abdur-Rahman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to a man: Hold to hearing and obeying in what you love or hate, unless you are commanded to disobedience, for there is no obedience to anyone in disobedience to Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abi Hind except al-Mughirah ibn Abdur-Rahman; Ya'qub ibn Humayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6268","6262 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Bishr ibn Ubays ibn Marhum al-Attar narrated to us, he said: an-Nadr ibn Arabi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim at-Taymi, from Abu Salamah ibn Abdur-Rahman, from Abu Arwa ad-Dawsi, he said: I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when Abu Bakr and Umar appeared, and he said: Praise be to Allah who has strengthened me with them. No one narrated this hadith from an-Nadr ibn Arabi except Bishr ibn Ubays, and it is not narrated from Abu Arwa except with this chain."
"6269","6263 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Jabir ibn Ghaylan ibn Munabbih as-San'ani narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Safwan narrated to us, from Idris ibn Wahb ibn Munabbih, he said: Wahb ibn Munabbih narrated to me, from Tawus, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for what has stained the Corner from the filth of the Jahiliyyah and its impurities, and the hands of wrongdoers and sinners, whoever had an illness would seek healing by it. This hadith is not narrated from Wahb ibn Munabbih, from Tawus, except with this chain; al-Hulwani is alone in transmitting it."
"6270","6264 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abdah, meaning Ibn Abi Lubabah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Ibn Umar, he said: Islam is built upon testifying that there is no god but Allah and that Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakah, pilgrimage to the House, and fasting Ramadan. And it was said to him: Fasting Ramadan, and pilgrimage to the House? He said: No, only as he said. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan, from Abdah, except Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i. And Ibrahim ibn Bashshar ar-Ramadi and others narrated it from Sufyan, from Su'ayr ibn al-Khums and Mis'ar ibn Kidam."
"6271","6265 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Shaqiq, from Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i."
"6272","6266 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Umar al-Adani narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Isma'il, from Qays, he said: Umar said to Asma: We preceded you in migration. She said: By Allah, you did precede us in migration; we were among the barefoot destitute, while you were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), teaching your ignorant and your learned, and commanding you to noble character. And she said: I shall surely come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and inform him. He said: People have one migration, but you have two migrations. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Muhammad ibn Abi Umar."
"6273","6267 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Umar narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Suqah, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: A counter would sometimes count for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a single gathering: Forgive me and accept my repentance; You are the Oft-Returning, the Forgiving, one hundred times."
"6274","6268 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about the sacrifice, is it obligatory? He said: The Messenger of Allah sacrificed, and the Muslims after him. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Isma'il ibn Ayyash."
"6275","6269 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Ata ibn Yasar, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about domestic donkeys, and he said: Nothing has come down concerning them except this unique comprehensive verse: So whoever does an atom's weight of good will see it, and whoever does an atom's weight of evil will see it. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan except Sa'id ibn Mansur."
"6276","6270 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mawhab ar-Ramli narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Abu az-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no zakah on horses and slaves, except that upon slaves there is the charity of Fitr. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Ibn Abi Za'idah; Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"6277","6271 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mawhab narrated to us, Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Ayyash al-Qitbani, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The least punished of the people of Hell will be the one who has two sandals of fire from which his brain boils. No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Ayyash except Mufaddal ibn Fudalah."
"6278","6272 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Bakr ibn Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Musa ibn Ulayy narrated to us, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not force your sick to eat and drink, for Allah feeds them and gives them drink. No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Ulayy except Bakr ibn Yunus, and it is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain."
"6279","6273 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdul-Aziz ibn Ubaydillah, from Muhammad ibn Ali, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man attains by forbearance the rank of one who fasts and stands in prayer, and a man is recorded as a tyrant though he owns nothing but the people of his house. This hadith is not narrated from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, except with this chain; Isma'il ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"6280","6274 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Anas ibn Abi al-Qasim al-Hadrami narrated to us, Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, from his father, he said: I asked A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, about a man who wishes to enter ihram applying perfume? She said: Apply the best perfume you can, for I can still see the glistening of perfume in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in ihram. Anas ibn Abi al-Qasim did not narrate from Abdur-Rahman ibn Aswad any hadith other than this, and the name of Abu al-Qasim is Malik, a Kufan."
"6281","6275 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Abdur-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah will distance him from the Fire by seventy autumns. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except his son Abdur-Rahman, and Hisham ibn Sa'd; al-Layth ibn Sa'd is alone in transmitting it from Hisham ibn Sa'd."
"6282","6276 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mawhab narrated to us, Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Za'idah narrated to us, from Mujalid, from ash-Sha'bi, from Masruq, from A'ishah, she said: There was one day of the year on which the wives of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would gather with him from daytime to night. She said: On that day he said: The quickest of you to join me will be the longest of you in arm. She said: We began measuring our arms against one another to see which of us had the longest arms. She said: Sawdah was the longest-armed among them, but when Zaynab died we learned that she had been the longest-armed among them in good and charity. She said: Zaynab used to spin yarn and give it to the detachments of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to sew with and to use in their expeditions. She said: On that day he also said: What will become of one of you when the dogs of al-Haw'ab bark at her. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except Ibn Abi Za'idah."
"6283","6277 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Yazid ibn Mawhab narrated to us, Marwan ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Ali ibn Abdul-Aziz narrated to us, from Husayn al-Mu'allim, from Abu al-Muhazzam, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ruled concerning ostrich eggs struck by one in ihram that their price is due. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except with this chain; Marwan ibn Muawiyah is alone in transmitting it, and the name of Abu al-Muhazzam is Yazid ibn Sufyan."
"6284","6278 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Uways, from Ibn Ka'b, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The two-faced one in this world will come on the Day of Resurrection with two faces of fire. This hadith is not narrated from Sa'd except with this chain; Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari is alone in transmitting it."
"6285","6279 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak narrated to us, from Abu al-Huwayrith, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two ravenous wolves among a sheepfold are not quicker in ruining it than the pursuit of wealth and the pursuit of status are in ruining a Muslim man's religion. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id except with this chain; Khalid ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"6286","6280 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, he said: Usamah ibn Zayd informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Rishdin, from Umm al-Fadl bint al-Harith, that whenever she heard someone reciting: By those sent forth in succession, she would say: May Allah bless him and grant him peace recited al-Mursalat in Maghrib, then he did not lead us in Isha until Allah took him. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri, from Abu Rishdin, who is Kurayb, except Usamah ibn Zayd. And the people narrated it from az-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah, from Ibn Abbas, from his mother Umm al-Fadl."
"6287","6281 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far ar-Ramli narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Shawdhab, from Abdullah ibn al-Qasim, from Kathir, freedman of Abdur-Rahman ibn Samurah, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Samurah, he said: Uthman ibn Affan came, when he equipped the army of hardship, with a thousand dinars, and scattered them in the lap of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Abdur-Rahman said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turning them over with his hand, saying: Nothing that Ibn Affan does after today will harm him. This hadith is not narrated from Abdur-Rahman ibn Samurah except with this chain; Abdullah ibn Shawdhab is alone in transmitting it, and none narrated it from Ibn Shawdhab except Damrah."
"6288","6282 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Umar ad-Darir Hafs ibn Abdullah al-Hulwani narrated to us, he said: Umar ibn Ubayd al-Basri, the seller of khumur, narrated to us, Hisham ibn Urwah narrated to us, from his father, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah loves that His concessions be taken just as He loves that His strict obligations be taken. I said: What are His strict obligations? He said: His prescribed duties. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Umar ibn Ubayd; Hafs ibn Abdullah is alone in transmitting it."
"6289","6283 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abdullah al-Hulwani narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd, seller of khumur, narrated to us, Suhayl ibn Abi Salih narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant attains by good character the rank of one who fasts and stands in prayer, and I think he said: One who strives in the path of Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Suhayl except Umar ibn Ubayd; Hafs ibn Abdullah is alone in transmitting it."
"6290","6284 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abbas ibn Abi Shamlah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ya'qub az-Zam'i, from Ata ibn Mas'ud, from his father, from his paternal aunt Azzah bint Khayil, that she informed him that she came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he took her pledge that: You shall not commit adultery, nor steal, nor bury alive, neither openly nor secretly. I said: As for open burying I know it, but as for secret burying, I did not ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor did he tell me, yet it occurred to me that it is spoiling the child; so by Allah, I will never spoil a child of mine. This hadith is not narrated from Azzah bint Khayil except with this chain; Musa ibn Ya'qub is alone in transmitting it, and none narrated it from Musa except Abbas ibn Abi Shamlah and Ibn Abi Fudayk."
"6291","6285 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Hafs ibn Abdullah al-Hulwani narrated to us, Bakkar ibn Abdullah ar-Rabadhi narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ubaydah, he said: Amr ibn Abdullah ibn Nawfal al-Awfi informed me, from Ibn Shihab, from Abu Salamah, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from Jibril, peace be upon him, he said: I turned over the easts of the earth and its wests, and I found no man better than Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), nor did I see any house better than the house of Banu Hashim. This hadith is not narrated from az-Zuhri except with this chain; Musa ibn Ubaydah is alone in transmitting it. And it is not narrated from A'ishah except with this chain."
"6292","6286 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Musayyib ibn Wadih narrated to us, Ata ibn Muslim al-Khaffaf narrated to us, Abu Amr al-Ashja'i narrated to me, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: I spent a night with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I saw a figure with him. He said: Did you see him, O Hudhayfah? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: This is an angel who has not descended to me since I was sent; he came to me tonight and gave me glad tidings that al-Hasan and al-Husayn are the masters of the youth of Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Qays except Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, and none from Salim except Abu Amr al-Ashja'i; Ata ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"6293","6287 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, al-Musayyib ibn Wadih narrated to us, Makhlad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, passed by Hassan ibn Thabit while he was in the mosque reciting poetry, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to him: Here? Hassan said to him: Yes; I have recited in it for one better than you. Then Hassan turned to Abu Hurayrah and said: I adjure you by Allah, O Abu Hurayrah, did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Answer on my behalf; O Allah, support him with the Holy Spirit? Abu Hurayrah said: O Allah, yes. So Umar fell silent and went on. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Makhlad ibn al-Husayn."
"6294","6288 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Bishr ibn Ubays ibn Marhum al-Attar narrated to us, my grandfather narrated to me, from Abdur-Rahim ibn Zayd al-Ammi, from his father, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed ablution washing once each, and said: This is the ablution of one whose prayer Allah does not accept except with it. Then he performed ablution washing twice each, and said: Whoever performs ablution like this, Allah doubles his reward twice. Then he performed ablution washing three times each, and said: This is the complete ablution, and this is my ablution and the ablution of Ibrahim, the close friend of Allah, peace be upon him. Whoever performs ablution like this, then says upon finishing: I testify that there is no god but Allah alone without partner, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger, Allah will open for him eight gates of Paradise, entering through whichever he wills. Thus Marhum ibn Abdul-Aziz narrated this hadith, from Abdur-Rahim ibn Zayd, from his father, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from his father, from his grandfather. And al-Hujayn and others narrated it from Abdur-Rahim ibn Zayd, from his father, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ibn Umar. And Abdullah ibn Aradah ash-Shaybani narrated it from Zayd al-Ammi, from Muawiyah ibn Qurrah, from Ubayd ibn Umayr, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b."
"6295","6289 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Bishr ibn Ubays narrated to us, Nafi' ibn Kharijah ibn Nafi', freedman of Ibn Jahsh, narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Jahsh, from Zaynab, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Accept hospitality, and the best hospitality is perfume, the lightest to carry and the sweetest in scent. This hadith is not narrated from Zaynab except with this chain; Bishr ibn Ubays is alone in transmitting it."
"6296","6290 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muqatil al-Marwazi narrated to us, Husayn ibn Umar al-Ahmasi narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Jarir, he said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sent, I came to him, and he said to me: O Jarir, for what purpose have you come to us? I said: To accept Islam at your hands, O Messenger of Allah. So he cast his cloak to me, then turned to his Companions and said: When the noble man of a people comes to you, honor him. No one narrated this hadith from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid except Husayn ibn Umar al-Ahmasi."
"6297","6291 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far ar-Ramli narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Hakam ibn Mus'ab, from Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever holds fast to seeking forgiveness, Allah will grant him relief from every worry, a way out of every straitness, and will provide for him from where he does not expect. This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Abbas except with this chain; al-Walid ibn Muslim is alone in transmitting it."
"6298","6292 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan al-Basri narrated to us, Abu Bahr al-Bakrawi narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he wanted to relieve himself, would go far away. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abu Bahr; Musa ibn Muhammad ibn Hayyan is alone in transmitting it."
"6299","6293 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu al-Akhyal Khalid ibn Amr as-Sulafi al-Himsi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Harb al-Abrash narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fasting while traveling is not part of righteousness. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Muhammad ibn Harb."
"6300","6294 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, al-Abbas ibn Abdul-Azim al-Anbari narrated to us, Abdul-Ghaffar ibn Ubaydillah al-Kurayzi narrated to us, from Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, that he narrated to them, from az-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Abu Mas'ud al-Ansari, he said: The first of the emigrants to arrive at Madinah was Mus'ab ibn Umayr, and he was the first to gather them there for Friday prayer; he gathered them before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived, and led them in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except Salih ibn Abi al-Akhdar, and none from Salih except Abdul-Ghaffar ibn Ubaydillah; Abbas al-Anbari is alone in transmitting it."
"6301","6295 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Abdul-Malik ibn Yahya ibn az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Be chaste and your women will be chaste, be dutiful to your fathers and your sons will be dutiful to you, and whoever excuses himself to his Muslim brother for something that reached him about him and he does not accept his excuse will not come to me at the Basin. No one narrated this hadith from Amir ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr except Abdul-Malik ibn Yahya ibn az-Zubayr; Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari is alone in transmitting it."
"6302","6296 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Abdul-Malik ibn Yahya ibn az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talhah, from his father, that he heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one day to his Companions, while I was present: If one of you had this pillar he would dislike that it be cut off; how then should one of you neglect and cut short his prayer which belongs to Allah? Complete your prayers, for Allah accepts only what is complete. No one narrated this hadith from Bilal ibn Yahya ibn Talhah except Abdul-Malik ibn Yahya ibn az-Zubayr; Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari is alone in transmitting it."
"6303","6297 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Zayd al-Ammi, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me and said: Convey greetings to Umar, and tell him: His pleasure is judgment and his anger is might. No one narrated this hadith from Zayd al-Ammi except Jarir ibn Hazim; Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari is alone in transmitting it."
"6304","6298 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Humayd narrated to us, Abu Safwan Abdullah ibn Sa'id ibn Abdul-Malik narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhi'b, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar: A man approached a woman in her behind during the time of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the people disapproved of that, so Allah revealed: Your women are a tilth for you. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhi'b except Abu Safwan."
"6305","6299 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdul-Aziz ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu az-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out to the people of the Suffah when their voices had risen and they had burst out laughing, and that angered him, so he said: You were not created for laughter, and he disapproved of that in them. Then Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him from Allah, exalted is His remembrance, and said: Allah commands you to make things easy and not hard, to give glad tidings and not repel. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out to them, gave them glad tidings, announced joy to them, and relaxed with them."
"6306","6300 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Abdul-Aziz ibn Yahya narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Abu az-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: When the people of Paradise enter Paradise and the people of Hell enter Hell, a caller will call out: O people of Paradise, eternity with no death in it; and O people of Hell, eternity with no death in it. No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Layth except Abdul-Aziz ibn Yahya."
"6307","6301 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi, Umar ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Kill geckos, even in the midst of the Ka'bah."
"6308","6302 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Umar ibn Qays narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever reaches Arafah before dawn breaks has attained the Hajj. No one narrated these two hadiths from Ata except Umar ibn Qays."
"6309","6303 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far ar-Ramli narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Yusuf al-Firyabi narrated to us, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Malik ibn Dinar, from Alqamah al-Muzani, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has never concealed a sin for a servant in this world except that He will conceal it for him in the Hereafter. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Dinar except Abbad; al-Firyabi is alone in transmitting it."
"6310","6304 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far ar-Ramli narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cited this verse: Then they follow what is ambiguous in it. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah has warned you; when you see them, recognize them. No one narrated this hadith from Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Qasim except Hammad ibn Salamah; al-Walid is alone in transmitting it. And others narrated it from Hammad ibn Salamah, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from al-Qasim, from A'ishah."
"6311","6305 - Muhammad ibn Ali al-Makki as-Sa'igh narrated to us, he said: Ya'qub ibn Humayd ibn Kasib narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musa at-Taymi narrated to us, from Isa ibn Abi Isa al-Hannat, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet, peace be upon him, said: Allah has made His sanctuary sacred, so it is sacred until the Day of Resurrection: its trees are not cut, its grass is not gathered, its lost property is not picked up except to announce it, and its game is not violated. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Isa al-Hannat."
"6312","6306 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Muhriz ibn Salamah narrated to us, Abdul-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim narrated to us, from ad-Dahhak ibn Uthman, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Abu Ubayd, chamberlain of Sulayman ibn Abdul-Malik, from Amr ibn Abasah, that Abu Ubayd said to him: Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, more than once, not twice nor three times, saying: When the believing servant performs ablution, rinses his mouth and sniffs water, sins fall from the edges of his eyes; when he washes his hands, sins fall from his fingernails; when he washes his feet, sins fall from his toenails. When he finishes at that, that is his share of his ablution. If he then stands and prays two rak'ahs, turning to Allah, mighty and exalted, with his heart and his gaze in them, he emerges from his sins as his mother bore him. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub ibn Musa except ad-Dahhak ibn Uthman; Abdul-Aziz ibn Abi Hazim is alone in transmitting it."
"6313","6307 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Bara ibn Azib, he said: I was with Ali when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) appointed him over Yemen, and I obtained some ounces of silver with him. When he came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: I found Fatimah had perfumed the house with scented water, so I stepped over it. She said: What is the matter with you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has ordered his Companions, and they have exited ihram. He said: I said to her: I entered ihram with the same ihram as the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: I have driven the sacrificial animals and performed qiran. And he said to his Companions: Had I known beforehand what I know now, I would have done as you did, but I have driven the sacrificial animals and performed qiran. And he said: Sacrifice sixty-seven or sixty-six camels, keep thirty-three or thirty-four for yourself, and keep a piece from each camel. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Yunus; Hajjaj ibn Muhammad is alone in transmitting it."
"6314","6308 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ma'in narrated to us, Abbad ibn Abbad al-Muhallabi narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Mu'adhah, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to seek our permission when it was the day of one of us, after there was revealed: You may defer whom you will of them and take to yourself whom you will. Mu'adhah said: I said: What would you say? She said: I would say: If that is up to me, I prefer no one over myself. No one narrated this hadith from Asim al-Ahwal except Abbad ibn Abbad."
"6315","6309 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah ibn az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr, that he said: I wished that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given us the call to prayer. I said: Why is that? He said: They will have the longest necks of the people of Paradise on the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya; Ibrahim al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Ibn az-Zubayr except with this chain."
"6316","6310 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: After me rulers will rule you; the righteous will rule you with his righteousness and the wicked with his wickedness. So hear and obey them in all that agrees with the truth, and pray behind them: if they do well, it is for you and for them, and if they do ill, it is for you and against them. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Urwah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it, and Hisham ibn Urwah did not narrate from Abu Salih any hadith other than this."
"6317","6311 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Salih ibn Abdullah, freedman of Banu Amir ibn Lu'ayy, narrated to us, Ya'qub ibn Abbad ibn Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr narrated to me, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Pilgrims for Hajj and Umrah are the delegation of Allah: if they call upon Him He answers them, and if they seek His forgiveness He forgives them. No one narrated this hadith from Ya'qub ibn Abbad except Salih ibn Abdullah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"6318","6312 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: It was forbidden to drink from the mouth of the waterskin. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Harith ibn Umayr; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i is alone in transmitting it."
"6319","6313 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far ar-Ramli narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabi'ah narrated to us, from Ibn Shawdhab, from Aban, from Abu Salih, from Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have grown old and my bones are frail, so guide me to a deed that will admit me to Paradise. He said: Bravo, bravo, you have indeed asked! Glorify Allah one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred necks you free; praise Allah one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred saddled and bridled horses you mount in the path of Allah; magnify Allah one hundred times, for it is better for you than one hundred garlanded and caparisoned camels you offer to the House of Allah, exalted; and say: There is no god but Allah, one hundred times, for it is better for you than all that heaven and earth encompass. And no deed will be raised for anyone on that day better than what is raised for you, except one who says the like of what you say, or more. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Shawdhab except Damrah ibn Rabi'ah."
"6320","6314 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Ya'qub at-Talqani narrated to us, Abdur-Rahman ibn as-Safar ad-Dimashqi narrated to us, al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Ata, Ibn Abbas narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah sends down upon the people of the mosque, the mosque of Makkah, one hundred and twenty mercies every day: sixty of them for those circumambulating, forty for those praying, and twenty of them for those gazing. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awza'i except Abdur-Rahman ibn as-Safar."
"6321","6315 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Umar al-Allaf ar-Razi narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Abu at-Tayyah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was building the mosque, and Ammar ibn Yasir was carrying two stones, so he said: Woe to Ibn Sumayyah; the rebellious party will kill him. No one narrated this hadith from Hammad ibn Salamah except Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim; Ahmad ibn Umar ar-Razi is alone in transmitting it."
"6322","6316 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Umar al-Allaf narrated to us, Abu Sa'id, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Abu Salamah, from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seated Husayn upon his thigh, and Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Is this your son? He said: Yes. He said: Your ummah will kill him after you. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shed tears. He said: If you wish, I will show you the soil of the land in which he will be killed. He said: Yes. So Jibril brought him some soil from the soil of at-Taff. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ad-Dinari."
"6323","6317 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Zahdam ibn al-Harith narrated to us, Abdullah ibn al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah narrated to us, Uthman ibn al-Aswad narrated to me, from Ata, from Jubayr ibn Mut'im, he said: I lost a donkey of mine and went out seeking it at Arafah, and I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with them at Arafah, while Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, stood at the standing places of Quraysh. No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn al-Aswad except Abdullah ibn al-Qasim; Zahdam is alone in transmitting it."
"6324","6318 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah, from Sulayman ibn Habib, from al-Walid ibn Ubadah ibn as-Samit, that his father Ubadah ibn as-Samit, when death came to him, his son Abdullah said to him: O my father, counsel me. He said: Seat me for my son. So they seated him, and he said: O my son, fear Allah, and you will never fear Allah until you believe in Allah, and you will never believe in Allah until you believe in the Decree, its good and its evil, and know that what struck you could never have missed you, and what missed you could never have struck you. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Decree is upon this; whoever dies upon other than this, Allah will admit him to the Fire. None narrated it from Sulayman ibn Habib al-Muharibi except Uthman ibn Abi al-Atikah; al-Walid is alone in transmitting it."
"6325","6319 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Ja'far ar-Ramli narrated to us, Ali ibn Thabit narrated to us, from al-Wazi' ibn Nafi', from Salim, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Reflect upon the blessings of Allah, but do not reflect upon Allah. No one narrated this hadith from Salim except al-Wazi'; Ali ibn Thabit is alone in transmitting it."
"6326","6320 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr at-Tinnisi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz az-Zubaydi, he said: One day we were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the mosque, and food was prepared for us. We ate, then the prayer was established, and we prayed without performing ablution. No one narrated this hadith from Uqbah ibn Muslim except Haywah ibn Shurayh."
"6327","6321 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bishr at-Tinnisi narrated to us, Haywah ibn Shurayh narrated to us, Ibn al-Had narrated to me, from Zumayl, freedman of Urwah, from Urwah ibn az-Zubayr, from A'ishah, may Allah be pleased with her, she said: Food was gifted to me and to Hafsah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while we were both fasting. One of us said to her companion: Would you like to break the fast? She said: Yes. So we broke the fast. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in to us, and we said: O Messenger of Allah, a gift was gifted to us, and we craved it, so we broke the fast. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No harm upon you both; fast a day in its place. None narrates this hadith from Zumayl, freedman of Urwah, except Ibn al-Had; Haywah is alone in transmitting it."
"6328","6322 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yazid al-Asamm narrated to us, he said: I heard as-Suddi narrating from Abu Abdir-Rahman as-Sulami, from Ali, he said: When Abu Talib died, I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your old uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him in the ground, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I buried him, then came to him, and he said: Go and wash, and do not do anything until you come to me. So I washed, then came to him, and he supplicated for me with supplications by which red camels would not delight me as much. No one narrated this hadith from as-Suddi except Yahya ibn Yazid."
"6329","6323 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ya'qub ibn Ata, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: People of two different religions do not inherit from one another at all. No one narrated this hadith from Ya'qub ibn Ata except Sufyan; Sa'id ibn Mansur is alone in transmitting it."
"6330","6324 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi al-Abyad narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abdir-Rahman, from Hafs ibn Asim, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Seven will Allah shade in His shade on a day when there is no shade but His shade: a just ruler, a youth who grew up in the worship of Allah, two men who loved each other for Allah, gathering upon that and parting upon it, a man whose heart is attached to the mosque, hardly leaving it until he returns to it, a man whom a woman of rank and status calls to herself and he says: I fear Allah, a man who gives charity concealing it from his left hand, so that his left hand does not know what his right hand spends, and a man who remembers Allah and his eyes overflow."
"6331","6325 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, al-Qa'nabi narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Abi al-Abyad narrated to us, from Abu az-Zinad, from al-A'raj, from Abu Hurayrah, may Allah be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you puts on sandals, let him begin with the right, and when he removes them let him begin with the left, or let him remove them both together or wear them both together. No one narrated these two hadiths from Sa'id ibn Abi al-Abyad except al-Qa'nabi."
"6332","6326 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Shabib ibn Sa'id narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, raising his voice with that: Kill dogs."
"6333","6327 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Shabib narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to forbid selling dates until their ripeness appeared, and he forbade muzabanah. No one narrated these two hadiths from az-Zuhri except Yunus, and none from Yunus except Shabib ibn Sa'id; Ahmad ibn Shabib is alone in transmitting them."
"6334","6328 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi narrated to us, Mu'adh ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Yunus ibn Ubayd, from al-Hasan, from Samurah ibn Jundub, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The likeness of one who flees from death is like the likeness of the fox whom the earth demands a debt from. He kept running until, when he was exhausted and panting, he entered his den. So he came out, with a rustling sound, and remained so until his neck broke and he died. No one narrated this hadith from Yunus except Mu'adh ibn Muhammad al-Hudhali, nephew of Abu Bakr al-Hudhali, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"6335","6329 - as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Fulayh ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Abdir-Rahman, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from A'ishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was summoned for prayer, and he said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer. Then he fainted, and when he recovered, he said: Have you commanded Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer? We said: Abu Bakr is a tender man; if he leads the people in prayer he will not make them hear. If only you commanded Umar to lead the people in prayer. He said: Command Abu Bakr to lead the people in prayer, for you are like the companions of Yusuf; many are the speakers and the wishers, but Allah and the believers refuse. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad except Sulayman ibn Abdir-Rahman; Fulayh ibn Sulayman is alone in transmitting it."
"6336","6330 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh al-Makki narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi narrated to us, Abdul-Warith narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Ziyad ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Umar saw a man slaughtering his sacrificial camel while it was kneeling, and said: Make it stand, for it is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Abdul-Warith; Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi is alone in transmitting it."
"6337","6331 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Umar al-Allaf ar-Razi narrated to us, Abu Zuhayr Abdur-Rahman ibn Maghra narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim at-Taymi, from Malik ibn Abi Amir, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not precede it, meaning the month of Ramadan: fast upon seeing it, and break fast upon seeing it; if it is obscured from you, complete thirty. This hadith is not narrated from Umar except with this chain; Abdur-Rahman ibn Maghra is alone in transmitting it."
"6338","6332 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Nahid ibn Salim al-Bahili narrated to us, Ammar Abu Hashim narrated to us, from ar-Rabi' ibn Lut, from his uncle al-Bara ibn Azib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever prays four rak'ahs before Zuhr, it is as though he stood in night prayer with them; whoever prays them after Isha, they are like the same on the Night of Decree. And when one Muslim meets another Muslim and takes his hand, both being sincere, they do not part until they are forgiven. No one narrated this hadith from ar-Rabi' ibn Lut except Ammar Abu Hashim; Nahid ibn Salim is alone in transmitting it."
"6339","6333 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Fudayl narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sa'd al-Ansari narrated to us, I heard Abu Taybah saying: I heard al-Miqdad ibn al-Aswad saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For a man to commit adultery with ten women is easier for him than to commit adultery with his neighbor's wife, and for him to steal from ten houses is easier for him than to steal from his neighbor's house. This hadith is not narrated from al-Miqdad except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Fudayl is alone in transmitting it."
"6340","6334 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: I read to al-Harith ibn Umayr, from Ayyub as-Sakhtiyani, from Qatadah, from Musa ibn Salamah, he said: I said to Ibn Abbas: We were with you, then we left and returned, and prayed two rak'ahs? He said: That is the Sunnah of Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), even if it displeases you. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Harith ibn Umayr and Muhammad ibn Abdir-Rahman at-Tafawi."
"6341","6335 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Muslim al-Makki narrated to us, Thumamah ibn Ubaydah narrated to us, from Abu az-Zubayr, from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O sons of Abd Manaf, if you are entrusted with any worldly affair, do not prevent anyone from circumambulating the House or praying, at whatever time it is. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Abdullah ibn Abbas except Abu az-Zubayr; Thumamah ibn Ubaydah is alone in transmitting it."
"6342","6336 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, Hafs ibn Ghiyath narrated to us, he said: I heard al-Muthanna ibn as-Sabbah narrating from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: A bedouin said: O Messenger of Allah, we are in the sands, and among us occur menstruation, janabah, and postnatal bleeding? He said: Use the earth. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri except al-Muthanna ibn as-Sabbah, and none narrated it from al-Muthanna except Hafs; Ibrahim ash-Shafi'i is alone in transmitting it. And ath-Thawri, Abdur-Razzaq, and others narrated it from al-Muthanna, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib."
"6343","6337 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi narrated to us, Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Abu Hayyah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Ibn Abbas, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed at Khaybar for six months, praying Zuhr and Asr together, and Maghrib and Isha together. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir ibn Zayd except Abu Hayyah; Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd is alone in transmitting it."
"6344","6338 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi narrated to us, Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Jurjah, from az-Zuhri, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Shaddad ibn Aws, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He is not a liar who speaks good or spreads good. No one narrated this hadith from az-Zuhri, from Mahmud, from Shaddad ibn Aws, except Yahya ibn Jurjah; Qaza'ah ibn Suwayd is alone in transmitting it. And the people narrated it from az-Zuhri, from Humayd ibn Abdir-Rahman, from his mother Umm Kulthum."
"6345","6339 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Nabhan narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are those who learn the Qur'an and teach the Qur'an. This hadith was not narrated from Sa'd except with this chain; al-Harith ibn Nabhan is alone in transmitting it."
"6346","6340 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar informed me, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, he said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your Lord greets you with peace, and has sent me to you with this cluster of grapes for you to eat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it."
"6347","6341 - And with this chain, from Ibn Shihab, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Jibril came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Your Lord greets you with peace, and has sent me to you with this cluster of grapes for you to eat. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it. No one narrated these two hadiths from az-Zuhri except Uqayl, and none from Uqayl except Hafs ibn Umar; Ibn Wahb is alone in transmitting it. And the hadith of az-Zuhri from Anas was transmitted alone by Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir from Ibn Wahb."
"6348","6342 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Musaffa narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to me, from Ibrahim ibn Abdir-Rahman ibn Awf, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah and His angels send blessings upon the first row. No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abdir-Rahman except Muhammad ibn Amr; Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad is alone in transmitting it."
"6349","6343 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Abdul-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Iyas ibn Salamah ibn al-Akwa', from his father, from his grandfather, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by some people of Aslam while they were competing in archery, and said: Shoot, O sons of Isma'il, for you had a father who was an archer. No one narrated this hadith from Iyas ibn Salamah except Abdur-Rahman ibn Harmalah; Sulayman ibn Bilal is alone in transmitting it."
"6350","6344 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Hudayj ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Habib, from Ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Mufassal was revealed at Makkah, and we remained years reciting it, with nothing else being revealed. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Habib Abu Abdir-Rahman, except Hudayj ibn Muawiyah."
"6351","6345 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Abdul-Aziz ibn Yahya al-Madani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd, from Humaydah bint Ayyad al-Ansariyyah, from Ka'b ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and addressed the people upon the pulpit in Ramadan, saying: I have stood upon this pulpit, and I know the Night of Decree, so seek it in the last ten nights, on the odd night. This hadith is not narrated from Ka'b ibn Malik except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Bilal is alone in transmitting it."
"6352","6346 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Bakkar al-Ayshi narrated to us, Mu'tamir ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Nusayb, Musallam ibn Abdullah ibn Sabrah narrated to us, from his father, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Allah forbids you three things: gossip, excessive questioning, and wasting wealth. This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Sabrah except with this chain; Mu'tamir is alone in transmitting it."
"6353","6347 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abbas ibn Uthman narrated to us, from his father, from Umar ibn Muhammad ibn Ali ibn Abi Talib, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Dinar for dinar, and dirham for dirham, with no excess between them. Whoever needs gold, let him exchange it for silver, and whoever needs silver, let him exchange it for gold, hand to hand. This hadith is not narrated from Ali except with this chain; Ibrahim ash-Shafi'i is alone in transmitting it."
"6354","6348 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hanzalah al-Makhzumi narrated to us, from Ma'ruf ibn Mushkan, from Abdur-Rahman ibn Kaysan, from his father, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night praying in a single garment, wrapped in it. No one narrated this hadith from Ma'ruf except Muhammad ibn Hanzalah al-Makhzumi."
"6355","6349 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah ibn az-Zubayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Asma bint Abi Bakr, she said: I testify that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will emerge from Thaqif a liar and a destroyer. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir is alone in transmitting it."
"6356","6350 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Muslim ibn Banak narrated to us, that he heard Amrah narrating from A'ishah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Isaf and Na'ilah were a man and a woman, then Allah turned them into two stones, and they were at Makkah. No one narrated this hadith from Amrah except Sa'id ibn Muslim; Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari is alone in transmitting it."
"6357","6351 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Khalid ibn Yazid al-Umari narrated to us, Abu al-Ghusn Thabit ibn Qays narrated to us, that he heard Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah, coming to visit him in the illness in which he died, saying: When I die, do not put a shirt on me, for I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither shrouded in a shirt nor turbaned. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm except Abu al-Ghusn; Khalid ibn Yazid is alone in transmitting it."
"6358","6352 - Muhammad ibn Ali narrated to us, Khalid narrated to us, Abu al-Ghusn narrated to us, that he heard Urwah ibn az-Zubayr narrating from A'ishah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Any woman who marries without the permission of her guardian, her marriage is invalid; if he has entered with her, she gets her dowry for what he made lawful of her private part. If they dispute, the ruler is the guardian of one who has no guardian. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Ghusn except Khalid ibn Yazid."
"6359","6353 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ash-Shafi'i narrated to us, he said: I heard my grandfather Muhammad ibn Ali saying: Abdullah ibn Ali ibn as-Sa'ib narrated to me, from Amr ibn Uhayhah ibn al-Julah, he said: I heard Khuzaymah ibn Thabit saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah forbids you to approach women in their behinds. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Uhayhah except Abdullah ibn Ali ibn as-Sa'ib; Ibrahim ash-Shafi'i is alone in transmitting it."
"6360","6354 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa at-Talhi narrated to us, from Mansur ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Muslim Abu ad-Duha, from Masruq, he said: A'ishah said: Abu Bakr gifted us a leg of sheep, and I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat in the darkness of night cutting it. Masruq said: I said: Did you not light a lamp? She said: Had we had a lamp, we would have used it as condiment."
"6361","6355 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Sa'id ibn Mansur narrated to us, Salih ibn Musa at-Talhi narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad, from A'ishah, she said: The household of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never ate their fill for three consecutive days of wheat bread since we came to Madinah. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Salih ibn Musa."
"6362","6356 - Muhammad ibn Ali as-Sa'igh narrated to us, Hafs ibn Umar al-Juddi narrated to us, Umar ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Muthanna, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he stayed behind for his need. He caught up with me and said: Is there any water? He performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks, then caught up with the army and led them in prayer. No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani except Umar ibn al-Muthanna; Umar ibn Ubayd at-Tanafisi is alone in transmitting it."
"6363","6357 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Yazid ibn al-Had, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from al-Harith ibn Mukhallad az-Zuraqi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah will not look on the Day of Resurrection at the man who approaches a woman in her behind. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn al-Had except al-Layth, and none narrated it from al-Layth except Amr ibn Khalid."
"6364","6358 - Muhammad ibn Amr al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hammad ibn Amr an-Nasibi narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you meet the idolaters on the road, do not greet them first with peace, and force them to its narrowest part. No one narrated this hadith from al-A'mash except Hammad ibn Amr; Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani is alone in transmitting it."
"6365","6359 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The one in whose hand is the knot of marriage is the husband. No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, except Ibn Lahi'ah, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"6366","6360 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Hudayj ibn Muawiyah narrated to us, Kinanah, freedman of Safiyyah, narrated to us, from Safiyyah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me one day and said: Do you have anything, O daughter of Huyayy? For I am hungry. I said: No, by Allah, O Messenger of Allah, except a mudd of flour. He said: Then heat it. She said: I put it in the pot and cooked it thoroughly, then said: It is cooked, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you know whether there is anything in the butter-skin of the daughter of Abu Bakr? I said: I do not know, O Messenger of Allah. She said: He went himself until he came to her house, and said: Is there anything in your skin, O daughter of Abu Bakr? She said: There is nothing in it but a little. He brought it himself, and squeezed its edges into the pot, until I saw what came out at the place of his hand. He said: In the name of Allah. Then he invoked blessing, and said: Call your sisters, for I know they feel what I feel. So I called them, and we ate until we were full. Then Abu Bakr came and sought permission and entered, then Umar came, then another man came. She said: They ate until they were full, and some remained. This hadith was not narrated from Safiyyah except with this chain; Amr ibn Khalid is alone in transmitting it."
"6367","6361 - Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was among the most playful of people with a child. No one narrated this hadith from Ishaq ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Talhah except Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah; Ibn Lahi'ah is alone in transmitting it, and it is not narrated from Anas except with this chain."
"6368","6362 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade meeting the caravans of goods on the way; if one meets them and buys, the owner of the goods has the choice when they reach the market. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"6369","6363 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Uqayl and Yunus, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from his father, he said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar walking in front of the funeral bier. None connected this hadith from Yunus except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"6370","6364 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Fazari, from Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from his father, from A'ishah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him, and whoever vows to disobey Him, let him not disobey Him. No one narrated this hadith from Abdur-Rahman ibn al-Qasim except Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Fazari; Muhammad ibn Salamah is alone in transmitting it."
"6371","6365 - And with it: from Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Fazari, from Atiyyah, from Abu Sa'id, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about a fasting person who ate and drank forgetfully, and he did not order him to make up, saying: That is only food Allah fed him. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri except with this chain; Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah is alone in transmitting it."
"6372","6366 - And with it, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from az-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: There is no marriage except with a guardian and two just witnesses."
"6373","6367 - And with it, from az-Zuhri, from Urwah, from A'ishah, she said: His tooth-stick and his comb never left the mosque of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he would look in the mirror when he combed his beard. No one narrated these two hadiths from az-Zuhri except Sulayman ibn Arqam; Muhammad ibn Salamah is alone in transmitting them."
"6374","6368 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Dinar, from Abu Hariz, freedman of Muawiyah, he said: Muawiyah addressed the people, and mentioned in his sermon that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade things, and I convey that to you and forbid you them: wailing, poetry, images, skins of predators, gold, and silk. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hariz, freedman of Muawiyah, except Abdullah ibn Dinar al-Bahrani, and none narrated it from Abdullah ibn Dinar except Isma'il ibn Ayyash."
"6375","6369 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Isma'il ibn Ayyash narrated to us, Muslim ibn Abdullah narrated to me, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah has treasured ones among His creation whom He keeps alive in well-being, and when He takes them to His Paradise; they are those over whom tribulations pass like pieces of dark night, while they remain in well-being therein. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi' except Muslim ibn Abdullah al-Himsi; Isma'il ibn Ayyash is alone in transmitting it."
"6376","6370 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed toward a short spear. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan except Ibn Lahi'ah."
"6377","6371 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Musa ibn A'yan, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, that he heard Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Amr reporting from his father Abdullah ibn Amr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever abandons prayer once in drunkenness, it is as though he owned the world and all in it and was stripped of it; and whoever becomes drunk four times, it is incumbent upon Allah to give him to drink from the mud of al-Khabal. It was said: What is the mud of al-Khabal, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The pus of the people of Hell."
"6378","6372 - And with it, from Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: Hilal came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the tenths of his honey, and asked him to reserve for him a valley called Salabah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reserved that valley for him. No one narrated these two hadiths from Amr ibn al-Harith except Musa ibn A'yan."
"6379","6373 - Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from A'ishah, that she saw in a dream that three moons fell into her chamber, and she mentioned that to Abu Bakr. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died and was buried in her house, Abu Bakr said: This is the best of your moons."
"6380","6374 - And with it, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, he said: My two ears heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: People will come out of the Fire."
"6381","With the same chain, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I prayed Zuhr with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in Madinah as four rakahs, then he set out on one of his journeys and led us in Asr prayer at al-Shajarah as two rakahs."
"6382","With the same chain, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Shihab: Amrah narrated to him that she was with Aishah, and it was said to her: Abu Said al-Khudri reports from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: “It is not lawful for a woman to travel for three days except with a mahram.” Amrah said: Aishah turned to us and said: “Not every one of you is a mahram for her.”"
"6383","With the same chain, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Shihab, from Salim, from Ibn Umar: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood on the minbar and said: “Whoever among you comes to Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl.”"
"6384","With the same chain, Amr ibn al-Harith narrated from Abu al-Zubayr, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Muadh ibn Jabal: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined Zuhr with Asr and Maghrib with Isha on the expedition of Tabuk, until we returned. No one narrated these hadiths from Amr ibn al-Harith except Bakr ibn Mudar."
"6385","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Amr ibn Mansur al-Mashriqi, from al-Shabi, from Fatimah bint Qays, who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal and said: “He will come to you from here,” gesturing with his hand toward the east."
"6386","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Hakim, from Ziyad ibn Ilaqah, from Usamah ibn Sharik, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as though birds were perched on our heads, none of us speaking, when some people came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, give us ruling on such-and-such, give us ruling on such-and-such. He said: “O people, Allah has lifted hardship, except for one who takes a loan from his brother’s honor — that is the one who falls into hardship and ruin.” They said: Should we seek treatment, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Yes; Allah sent down no disease without sending down its cure, except one disease.” They said: What is it, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “Old age.” They said: Which of Allah’s servants is most beloved to Allah? He said: “The best of them in character.” No one narrated this hadith from Uthman ibn Hakim except Isa ibn Yunus."
"6387","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah narrated to us: Jabir al-Jufi narrated to us, from Amir al-Shabi, from Urwah al-Bariqi: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Good is tied to the forelocks of horses until the Day of Resurrection.” No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Zuhayr."
"6388","With the same chain, Zuhayr narrated to us: Ziyad ibn Khaythamah narrated to us, from al-Aswad ibn Said al-Hamdani, from Jabir ibn Samurah, who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “This ummah will remain upright, its cause manifest over its enemy, until twelve caliphs pass among them, all of them from Quraysh.” When he returned to his house, Quraysh came to him and said: Then what will happen? He said: “Then there will be killing (al-harj).” No one narrated this hadith from al-Aswad ibn Said except Ziyad ibn Khaythamah, and no one narrated it from Ziyad except Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah."
"6389","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Darraj, from Abu al-Haytham, from Abu Said, who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever grows attached to the mosque, Allah grows attached to him.” No one narrated this hadith from Darraj except Ibn Lahiah; Amr ibn Khalid alone narrated it."
"6390","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah and Humayd ibn Hilal, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: I was riding behind Abu Talhah, my knee touching the knee of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and they kept on crying out for Hajj and Umrah. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub, from Humayd ibn Hilal, except Ubaydullah ibn Amr; Hammad ibn Zayd and others narrated it from Abu Qilabah alone."
"6391","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Jabir ibn Zayd, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Usamah ibn Zayd narrated to me that he asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about gold for gold, and that had been the trade of himself and Zayd ibn Arqam, and he said: “No harm in it, hand to hand.”"
"6392","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Abu al-Walid al-Makki, from Jabir ibn Abdillah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade muhaqalah, mukhabarah and muzabanah, and forbade selling date-palms until they ripen — ripening meaning they turn red, or yellow, or can be eaten from. Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah said: Abu al-Walid narrated to us while Ata ibn Abi Rabah was sitting, so I said to Ata: Did you not hear Jabir narrate this hadith? Ata said: Yes; I heard Jabir narrate it from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated these two hadiths from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Ubaydullah ibn Amr."
"6393","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Musa ibn Ayan, from Ishaq ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Abdullah ibn Zamah, who said: I heard Umm Salamah say: Abu Bakr went out trading to Busra in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); Abu Bakr’s cherishing of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companionship did not keep him from his share of it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not keep Abu Bakr from traveling, despite his love for his companionship and his love for Abu Bakr and his eagerness for his companionship, out of admiration for the Messenger of Allah’s (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) approval of trade and his admiration for it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Ishaq ibn Rashid; Musa ibn Ayan alone narrated it."
"6394","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Musa ibn Ayan narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from Ibn Jurayj, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) bought a load of qaraz, or a load of khabat, from a Bedouin — I think he said from Banu Amir ibn Sasah — and when the deal was concluded for him, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Choose (the price).” The Bedouin said: I have never seen a day like today; by your life with Allah, from whom are you? He said: “From Quraysh.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Ayyub, and no one narrated it from Yahya ibn Ayyub except al-Layth ibn Sad and Musa ibn Ayan."
"6395","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Attab ibn Bashir narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Miqsam, from Aishah, who said: Umm Mistah came to me, then went out to relieve herself and Umm Mistah stepped on a bone or a thorn and said: May Mistah be ruined. I said: What an evil thing you have said; you insult a man from among the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said: I bear witness that you are among the heedless believing women; do you know what has been spread about you? I said: No, by Allah. She said: When did you last see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? I said: The Messenger does with his wives as he pleases; he begins with whichever of them he loves and defers whichever of them he loves. She said: Then such-and-such has been spread about you. I fell down unconscious. The news reached my mother Umm Ruman, and when it reached her that Aishah had heard the matter, she came to me and carried me to her house. It reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that Aishah had heard the matter, so he came to her, entered upon her, sat beside her and said: “O Aishah, Allah has widened repentance.” I only grew worse in my distress. While we were like that, Abu Bakr came and entered upon me and said: O Messenger of Allah, why do you wait with this one who has betrayed you and disgraced me? I only grew worse upon worse. Then he sent for Ali and said: “O Ali, what is your view about Aishah?” He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: “You must tell me what you think about Aishah.” He said: Allah has widened (the choice of) women, but send for Barirah her servant and ask her; perhaps she has seen something of her affair. So he sent for Barirah and she came, and he said to her: “Do you bear witness that I am the Messenger of Allah?” She said: Yes. He said: “If I ask you about something, do not conceal it from me.” She said: O Messenger of Allah, there is nothing you ask me about but I will tell you, and I will not conceal anything from you, Allah willing. He said: “You were with Aishah; did you see anything in her you disliked?” She said: No; by the One who sent you with prophethood, I have seen nothing in her since I have been with her except one trait. He said: “What is it?” She said: I kneaded dough of mine and said to Aishah: Watch this dough until I fetch fire to bake; she stood to pray and neglected the dough, and a sheep came and ate it. Then he sent for Usamah and said: “O Usamah, what is your view about Aishah?” He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: “You must tell me what you think about her.” He said: I think you should remain silent about her until Allah gives you word concerning her. Only a short while passed before revelation came down; when it came down we saw joy on the face of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and her vindication came from Allah, exalted is His remembrance. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Rejoice, O Aishah; rejoice, O Aishah; Allah has brought you your vindication.” I said: Not through your praise nor your companion’s praise. At that point she (Umm Mistah’s report context) had spoken, and when he used to come to her he would say: “How is that woman?” No one narrated this hadith from Miqsam except Khusayf; Attab ibn Bashir alone narrated it."
"6396","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Yazid and Ibn Hubayrah, from Abdullah ibn Zurayd al-Ghafiqi, from Ali ibn Abi Talib: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was standing leading them in prayer, then he left, then he came back with water dripping from his head and said: “I stood to lead you, then I remembered that I was junub and had not performed ghusl, so I left and performed ghusl; whoever among you is struck by the same thing that struck me, or finds rumbling in his belly, let him leave and perform ghusl, then let him come and resume his prayer.” This hadith is not narrated from Ali except by this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"6397","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Mansur: Abu Ishaq narrated to me, from al-Harith, from Ali, who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “If I were to appoint over my ummah anyone without consultation among them, I would appoint over them Ibn Umm Abd.” No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq except Mansur; Zuhayr alone narrated it."
"6398","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Qazaah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbid the two rakahs after Asr — so bring me whoever heard him command them."
"6399","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Asim, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, who said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and among what he commanded us of good was that we not wail. A woman said: O Messenger of Allah, the women of the family of so-and-so helped me (in mourning), so I will not pledge to you until I help them in return. She went and helped them, then pledged to him; no woman fulfilled (her pledge) except her and Umm Sulaym."
"6400","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Hafsah bint Sirin, from Umm Atiyyah, who said: We were commanded to go out for the two Eids, including the secluded and the virgin; the menstruating women would go out and stay behind the people, saying takbir along with the people."
"6401","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Amr ibn Salamah, who said: Some men of our tribe came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and heard him say: “Let the one among you who knows most Quran lead you.” So they put me forward before them though I was a boy, and I used to lead them in a patched cloak that was tight; when I prostrated, my backside would show, so they said to my father: Will you not cover his backside from us? And I used to make them eager to learn the Quran. Zuhayr said: He remained the imam of his people in prayer and over their funerals. No one narrated these hadiths from Asim al-Ahwal except Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah."
"6402","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hudayj ibn Muawiyah narrated to us: Husayn narrated to us, from Hilal ibn Yasaf, from al-Agharr, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever says: there is no god but Allah, it will benefit him one day of his lifetime, whatever befalls him before that.” No one narrated this hadith from Husayn except Hudayj ibn Muawiyah."
"6403","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu al-Uryan, who said: Ibn Abbas said: There is no prostration (of recitation) in the Mufassal. So I went to Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdillah ibn Masud and mentioned to him what Ibn Abbas said, and he said: Abdullah ibn Masud said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the Muslims and the polytheists prostrated at al-Najm, and we have continued to prostrate ever since."
"6404","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Zubayd narrated to us, from Muharib ibn Dithar, from Ibn Buraydah, from his father, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey; we halted for rest, nearly a thousand riders with him, and he prayed two rakahs, then turned to us with his eyes shedding tears. Umar ibn al-Khattab stood up to him, ransoming him with father and mother, saying: What is wrong with you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: “I sought my Lord’s permission to seek forgiveness for my mother, and He did not permit me, so my eyes wept out of mercy for her from the Fire. I had forbidden you three things: visiting graves — so visit them, and let visiting them increase you in good; I forbade you sacrificial meat after three days — so eat and keep whatever you wish; and I forbade you drinks (in certain vessels) — so drink, but do not drink intoxicants.” No one narrated this hadith from Zubayd al-Yami except Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah."
"6405","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us, from Aban ibn Abi Ayyash, from Mawraq, who said: I was with Ibn Abbas and he said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When a fasting man sits with people who are eating, the angels send blessings upon him until the fasting person breaks his fast.”"
"6406","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us that Aban ibn Abi Ayyash narrated to him; he said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate at the end of prayer: “O Allah, I seek refuge in You from those four.”"
"6407","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Zuhayr narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us that Aban ibn Abi Ayyash narrated to him, from Abu al-Siddiq al-Naji, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah frees people from the Fire every day and night, and every Muslim has, every day and night, an answered supplication.”"
"6408","With the same chain, Muhammad ibn Juhadah narrated to us: al-Hajjaj al-Bahili narrated to me: Suwayd ibn Hujayr narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Muawiyah, from his father, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I swore by the number of these — gesturing to the fingers of his hands, ten of them — that I would not follow you nor follow what you brought, so I ask you by Allah: what is this religion of yours with which Allah sent you? He said: “Allah sent me with Islam.” He said: What is Islam? He said: “That you say: I have submitted myself to Allah and turned my face to Him, and you establish prayer and give zakah — two supporting brothers — and that Allah accepts no repentance from one who commits shirk after his Islam.” I said: What is the right of our wives over us? He said: “Feed when you eat, clothe when you clothe yourself, do not strike the face, do not revile, and do not desert except in the house.” Then he said: “Here you will be gathered — gesturing toward Syria — walking and riding, on your faces; you will come to Allah on the Day of Resurrection with muzzles over your mouths; the first thing to speak from one of you will be his thigh. You complete seventy nations; you are the last of them and the noblest of them to Allah. There is no dependent who comes to his patron asking from his surplus and is refused, but a bald serpent will come to him on the Day of Resurrection, licking its lips at him. A man from those before you was given abundant wealth and children by Allah; when most of his life had passed and little remained, and death came to him, he said to his family: What kind of man was I to you? They said: The best of men. He said: Either I take back everything I gave you, or you do what I command you. They said: We will do what you command. He said: When I die, throw me into the fire; when I am charcoal, crush me, then scatter me on a windy day. Then Allah called him and he came as he had been, and He said: What made you do what you did? He said: Fear of You, my Lord. He said: Then He pardoned him and showed him mercy.” No one narrated these hadiths from Muhammad ibn Juhadah except Zuhayr."
"6409","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: al-Ala ibn Sulayman al-Raqqi narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah does not take away knowledge by snatching it from people, but by taking away the scholars; when the scholars are gone, people take ignorant leaders, who are asked and give fatwa without knowledge, going astray and leading astray from the straight path.” No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah, except al-Ala ibn Sulayman; people narrate it from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah and Abu Hurayrah."
"6410","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I have exempted you from charity on horses and slaves.” No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Ibn Lahiah; Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani alone narrated it."
"6411","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Mujahid ibn Said ibn Abi Zaynab al-Ashjai narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Malik ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Ashtar narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather: Umar ibn al-Khattab mentioned the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then said to them: Allah’s hand is over the community, and the solitary one is with Satan; truth is a root in Paradise and falsehood is a root in the Fire. My Companions are the best of you, so honor them, then the generation after them, then the generation after them; then lying and killing will appear. This hadith is not narrated from Malik al-Ashtar except by this chain; Amr ibn Khalid alone narrated it."
"6412","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Harith the muadhdhin narrated to us: Yahya ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Nuaym ibn Abi Hind, from Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) urinated at a refuse heap of a people, then performed wudu and wiped over his khuffs. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Yahya ibn Rashid; Muhammad ibn al-Harith alone narrated it."
"6413","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Jufi narrated to us: my uncle Amr ibn Uthman narrated to us: Abu Muslim, the guide of al-Amash, narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: “I asked Jibril, peace be upon him: Do you see your Lord? He said: Between me and Him are seventy veils of light; if I saw the nearest of them I would burn.” No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abu Muslim."
"6414","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Bakr ibn Mudar narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad, freedman of Ibn Ayyash — he narrated to him — from Irak ibn Malik, from Aishah, who said: A poor woman carrying her two sons came to me, so I fed her three dates; she gave each of her two sons a date and they ate them, then her sons asked her for more, so she split the date she had meant to eat between them. I admired her conduct and mentioned what she did to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: “Allah has made Paradise obligatory for her and freed her from the Fire.” No one narrated this hadith from Irak ibn Malik except Ziyad ibn Abi Ziyad; Bakr ibn Mudar alone narrated it."
"6415","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah, from Rabiah ibn Abi Abd al-Rahman: he heard Anas ibn Malik say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was commissioned at forty, stayed in Makkah ten years, then Allah took him at sixty, with not twenty white hairs on his head and beard. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Bakr ibn Mudar."
"6416","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my wife does not refuse the hand of one who touches. He said: “Divorce her.” He said: I love her, and she is a beautiful woman. He said: “Then enjoy her (keep her).” No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Karim except Ubaydullah ibn Amr al-Raqqi."
"6417","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Arqam, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ubayy ibn Kab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the Opening of the Book, then said: “Your Lord says: Son of Adam, I sent down upon you seven verses: three for Me, three for you, and one between Me and you. As for what is for Me: ‘Praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds; the Most Merciful, the Most Compassionate; Master of the Day of Judgment.’ And what is between Me and you: ‘You alone we worship, and from You alone we seek help’ — from you is worship, and upon Me is aid for you. And what is for you: ‘Guide us along the Straight Path’ — this is for you: ‘the path of those You have blessed, not of those who earned anger’ — the Jews — ‘nor of those who went astray’ — the Christians.”"
"6418","With the same chain, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer one day and dropped a surah of the Quran; when he finished his prayer, Ubayy said: O Messenger of Allah, was such-and-such verse abrogated? He said: “No.” He said: Then you did not recite it. He said: “Why did you not prompt me with it?” No one narrated these two hadiths from al-Zuhri except Sulayman ibn Arqam."
"6419","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ghalib ibn Ubaydillah, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Jabir, who said: A man came while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was addressing the people on Friday, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: “Stand and pray two rakahs, making them brief.” No one narrated this hadith from Ghalib ibn Ubaydillah except Muhammad ibn Salamah."
"6420","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Hammad ibn Amr al-Nasibi narrated to us: Zayd ibn Rufay narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Talhah, who said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while his face was radiant and joyful, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, you are in a state I have never seen you in. He said: “And what prevents me? Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me just now and said: Give your ummah glad tidings that whoever sends one blessing upon you, Allah writes for him ten good deeds thereby and wipes away ten bad deeds thereby.” No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Zayd ibn Rufay and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah al-Majishun; Hammad ibn Amr alone narrated it from Zayd ibn Rufay, and al-Walid ibn Salamah al-Tabarani from al-Majishun."
"6421","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid al-Harrani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Musa ibn Ayan, from Zuhayr ibn Muawiyah: al-Hasan ibn Dinar narrated to us: Qatadah narrated to us: Abu Umar al-Ghudani narrated to us, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Any man who owns camels [ … ]” (the text breaks off here)."
"6422","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Musa ibn Ayan, from Yahya ibn Abi Unaysah, from Jabir al-Jufi, from Nafi, from Abu Said al-Khudri, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: “Do not trade in dates until their ripeness appears, and do not trade gold except like for like.” No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Yahya ibn Abi Unaysah; Musa ibn Ayan alone narrated it."
"6423","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Amr narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jundab ibn Sufyan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: “The best prayer after the obligatory prayer is prayer in the depth of the night, and the best fasting after the month of Ramadan is the month of Allah which you call al-Muharram.”"
"6424","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Musa ibn Ayan, from Isa ibn Yunus, from Umar ibn Suhban, from Abu al-Zinad, from Anas, who said: We used to go out as pilgrims with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and before we reached al-Rawha the next day our throats would be hoarse — meaning from raising the voice in talbiyah. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Umar ibn Suhban, nor from Umar except Isa ibn Yunus; Musa ibn Ayan alone narrated it."
"6425","Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Khalid narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Musa ibn Ayan, from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Said al-Khudri, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking by bending the mouths of waterskins. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, except Musa ibn Ayan. Others narrate it from al-Zuhri, from Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah, and so do al-Zuhri’s companions."
"6426","Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us: my father narrated to us: from Musa ibn Ayan, from Isa ibn Yunus, from Umar ibn Suhban, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “A woman in ihram shall not wear a face-veil, nor gloves, nor a burqa; if she wishes to enter ihram while menstruating, let her enter ihram and attend the stations, except tawaf of the House and (sai) between al-Safa and al-Marwah.” No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Suhban except Isa ibn Yunus; Musa ibn Ayan alone narrated it."
"6427","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Mansur al-Bajali al-Kashshi narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Jarir narrated to us, from Qabus ibn Abi Zibyan, from his father, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Allah, mighty and exalted, sent no prophet but as a youth, and no scholar was given knowledge but as a youth. No one narrated this hadith from Qabus except Jarir."
"6428","Muhammad ibn Umar ibn Mansur al-Bajali al-Kashshi narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, who said: Jibril, peace be upon him, came down to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: “Judge with an oath along with a witness,” and he said: “Wednesday is a day of continuous ill omen.” In this hadith, no one said “Jibril came down” from Jafar ibn Muhammad except Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah, and no one narrates “Wednesday is a day of continuous ill omen” from Jafar except Ibrahim ibn Abi Hayyah."
"6429","Muhammad ibn Umar al-Kashshi narrated to us: Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abdullah ibn Abi Qatadah, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say: “The cup-bearer of a people drinks last.” No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except Hammad ibn Zayd; Qutaybah ibn Said alone narrated it."
"6430","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Aziz al-Assal narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from Ibn Shihab, from Anas ibn Malik: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) uttered the talbiyah from the mosque of Dhu al-Hulayfah. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Aziz alone narrated it."
"6431","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ghani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Awn, who said: I heard Muhammad ibn Sirin narrate from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Injury by an animal is unaccountable, injury in a well is unaccountable, injury in a mine is unaccountable, and in buried treasure is the fifth.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman; Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Aziz alone narrated it."
"6432","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ghani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us, from Abu Umayyah ibn Yala, from Nafi, who said: A man called Ibn Jurayj, a disputatious man, came to Ibn Umar and said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, I saw you do something I never saw anyone do. He said: Come now, O Ibn Jurayj, you keep bringing me novelties. He said: I saw you not utter the talbiyah until your mount stands upright with you; I saw you trim your moustache closely; I saw you love yellow dye; and I saw you wear tanned leather sandals? He said: As for my uttering the talbiyah when my mount stands upright with me, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not utter the talbiyah until his mount stood upright with him; as for my trimming my moustache closely, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) trim his moustache closely; as for yellow dye, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) love yellow dye; and as for my wearing tanned sandals, I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) love them and perform wudu in them. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abu Umayyah; Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it, while what is well known among people is from the hadith of Said al-Maqburi, from Ubayd ibn Jurayj."
"6433","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ghani narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us, from Abu Umayyah ibn Yala, from Umm Isa, from Umm al-Dirab, who said: My father died leaving me and a brother of mine, with no wealth for us; my uncle came from Madinah and took us out to Aishah, who admitted me with her into the private chamber since I was a girl, but did not admit the boy. My uncle complained to her of his need, so she ordered for us two portions, two large bowls, two knotted garments, and a young camel. Then she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “The Hour will not come until the child is a cause of anger, rain is scorching heat, the wicked overflow in abundance, the noble recede in ebb, the young dares against the elder, and the wicked dares against the noble.” This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except by this chain; Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it."
"6434","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Muammal narrated to us: Humayd al-Tawil narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “A man may work for a period of his life with the deeds of the people of Paradise, then before his death he turns and works with the deeds of the people of the Fire, dies, and enters the Fire; and a man may work for a period of his life with the deeds of the people of the Fire, then before his death he turns and works with the deeds of the people of Paradise, dies, and enters Paradise.”"
"6435","With the same chain, from Anas: he had a brother nicknamed Abu Umayr, who had a small bird (nughar) that died; the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us and said: “What is wrong with Abu Umayr?” They said: His nughar has perished. He kept saying, joking with him: “O Abu Umayr, what did the little nughayr do? O Abu Umayr, what did the little nughayr do?” No one narrated these two hadiths from Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman except Abd al-Ghani ibn Abd al-Aziz."
"6436","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Bilal al-Andalusi al-Amiri narrated to us: Harmalah ibn Yahya and Abu Musab al-Zuhri narrated to us; they said: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar: Umar ibn al-Khattab consulted the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about his property at Thamgh, whether to give it in charity, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Give in charity what you see fit, but retain its principal: it is neither sold nor inherited.” No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Muttalib except Ibrahim ibn Sad; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6437","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi narrated to us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah and Yahya ibn Ayyub informed me, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Yaqub ibn Utbah ibn al-Mughirah ibn al-Akhnas, from Ibn Umar: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Iblis entered Iraq and relieved himself; he entered Syria but they drove him away until he reached Sibaq; he entered Egypt and laid eggs there, hatched, and spread out his finery.” No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Aqil, nor from Aqil except Ibn Lahiah and Yahya ibn Ayyub; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6438","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi narrated to us: Harmalah ibn Yahya and Abu Musab narrated to us; they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim informed me, from Ubaydullah ibn Umar, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The Muslims are about to be besieged in Madinah, until their farthest outpost is Salah.” No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydullah ibn Umar except Jarir ibn Hazim; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6439","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi ibn Bilal al-Andalusi narrated to us: Harmalah and Abu Musab narrated to us; they said: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Jarir ibn Hazim, from Yahya ibn Said, from Amrah, from Aishah, who said: One morning Hafsah and I were fasting voluntarily when a gift was presented to us and we craved it, so we ate it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to us; Aishah said: Hafsah hastened — she was her father’s daughter — and asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: “No blame upon you both; fast a day in its place.” No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Jarir ibn Hazim; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6440","Muhammad ibn al-Rabi narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Abi Taybah narrated to us: Idris ibn Yahya al-Khawlani narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Sulayman al-Tawil, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah and His angels send blessings upon those who take the pre-dawn meal.” No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Abdullah ibn Sulayman, nor from Abdullah ibn Sulayman except Abdullah ibn Ayyash; Idris ibn Yahya alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Umar except by this chain."
"6441","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs al-Misri narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman ibn Nadlah al-Madani narrated to us: al-Harith ibn Muhammad al-Fihri narrated to us: Ismail ibn Abi Hakim narrated to me: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to me: Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham narrated to me: Umm Salamah narrated to me, from Khadijah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, O son of my uncle, can you tell me when the one who comes to you comes to you? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: “Yes, O Khadijah.” Khadijah said: Jibril came to him one day while I was with him, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “O Khadijah, this is my companion who comes to me; he has come.” I said to him: Stand and sit on my right thigh. He stood and sat on my right thigh, and I said to him: Do you see him? He said: “Yes.” I said to him: Move and sit on my left thigh. He sat, and I said: Do you see him? He said: “Yes.” I said to him: Move and sit in my lap. He sat, and she said to him: Do you see him? He said: “Yes.” Khadijah said: Then I uncovered and cast off my head-cover, and said to him: Do you see him? He said: “No.” I said to him: This, by Allah, is a noble angel; by Allah, this is no devil. Khadijah said: I told that to Waraqah ibn Nawfal ibn Asad ibn Abd al-Uzza ibn Qusayy, as Muhammad the Messenger of Allah had told it to me, and Waraqah said: Your report is true, O Khadijah. No one narrated this hadith from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz except Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, nor from Ismail except al-Harith ibn Muhammad al-Fihri; Yahya ibn Sulayman alone narrated it."
"6442","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs al-Misri narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Imran ibn Muhammad ibn Said ibn al-Musayyab narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Said ibn al-Musayyab, who said: I heard Umm Salamah say: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a mat and a small prayer mat (khumrah) upon which he prayed. This hadith is not narrated from Said ibn al-Musayyab except by this chain; al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri alone narrated it."
"6443","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us: Abu Ghaziyyah Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us: Kathir ibn Abdullah ibn Amr ibn Awf al-Muzani narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Fingers take the place of the siwak when there is no siwak.” No one narrated this hadith from Kathir ibn Abdullah al-Muzani except Abu Ghaziyyah; Harun al-Farwi alone narrated it."
"6444","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us: Ibn Awn narrated to us: Mujahid narrated to me, who said: We were sitting in a circle in which were Abdullah ibn Umar and Ubayd ibn Umayr, when a man came, stood over us and said: Answer so-and-so, answer so-and-so. The people disliked it intensely, and Ibn Umar lowered his head. Ubayd ibn Umayr raised his head and said: O son of our brother, excuse us, excuse us. Ibn Umar raised his head and said: Let us leave; there is no good in it. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Whoever is invited and does not answer has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Ibn al-Mubarak; al-Husayn ibn al-Hasan al-Marwazi alone narrated it."
"6445","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs al-Misri narrated to us: Harun ibn Said al-Ayli narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to me: Abu al-Zahiriyyah narrated to me: Jubayr ibn Nufayr narrated to me: Thawban, freedman of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When one of you performs witr, let him pray two rakahs (afterward); if he rises (for night prayer, they count as its opening), otherwise they stand for him.” This hadith is not narrated from Thawban except by this chain; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6446","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Ali ibn Abdillah al-Kufi narrated to me: Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhammad narrated to us: al-Asbagh ibn Zayd narrated to me: Zayd ibn Ali narrated to me: Marjanah, freedwoman of Ali, narrated to me, who said: Fatimah bint Rasulillah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to me, from her father the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: “In Friday there is an hour; no Muslim servant coincides with it asking Allah for good but He gives it to him.” This hadith is not narrated from Fatimah except by this chain; al-Muharibi alone narrated it."
"6447","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Maymun ibn Kulayb narrated to us: Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji narrated to us: Jafar ibn Muhammad narrated to me, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, who said: We attended the wedding of Ali ibn Abi Talib and Fatimah bint Rasulillah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); we never saw a wedding better than it in hays (a dish of dates and butter). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prepared oil and dates for us and we ate; their bed on their wedding night was a sheep’s skin. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar ibn Muhammad except Muslim ibn Khalid al-Zanji and Abdullah ibn Maymun al-Qaddah; Maymun ibn Kulayb alone narrated it from Muslim ibn Khalid."
"6448","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Wahbullah ibn Rizq Abu Hurayrah al-Misri narrated to us: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us: Ata narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Allah has an angel who, if told: swallow the seven heavens and earths in one morsel, would do so; his tasbih is: Glory be to You wherever You are.” No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Bishr ibn Bakr; Wahbullah ibn Rizq alone narrated it."
"6449","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Madani narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir, who said: When the sun had passed its zenith, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Friday, and we would return finding no shade to rest in. No one narrated this hadith from Sulayman ibn Bilal except Yahya ibn Sulayman."
"6450","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us: Abu Ghaziyyah Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us: Musa ibn Uqbah narrated to me: Ibn Abi Hind narrated to me: Yazid ibn Muhajir narrated to me, who said: I heard al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “What is between my house and my minbar is a garden of the gardens of Paradise, and my minbar is upon my Hawd.” No one narrated this hadith from Musa ibn Uqbah except Abu Ghaziyyah; Harun al-Farwi alone narrated it; and Ibn Abi Hind from whom Musa ibn Uqbah narrated is Said ibn Abi Hind Abu Abdillah."
"6451","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani narrated to us: Bishr ibn Bakr narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to me: Nafi narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Umar: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would stay at Dhu al-Hulayfah as long as he wished; when he wished to enter ihram he would pray in the mosque, then utter the talbiyah when his mount stood upright with him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Bishr ibn Bakr; Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani alone narrated it."
"6452","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Madani narrated to us: Ismail ibn Qays ibn Sad ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Kharijah ibn Zayd ibn Thabit narrated to me, from his father Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whatever intoxicates in large amount, a small amount of it is unlawful.” This hadith is not narrated from Zayd ibn Thabit except by this chain; Yahya ibn Sulayman ibn Nadlah alone narrated it."
"6453","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Bakr al-Salimi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Umar ibn Talhah narrated to me: Abu Suhayl Nafi ibn Malik narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Surah al-Anam was sent down with a company of angels filling what is between the horizons, raising a din with tasbih and taqdis, and the earth trembling,” while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was saying: “Glory be to Allah the Most Great, glory be to Allah the Most Great.” No one narrated this hadith from Abu Suhayl Nafi ibn Malik except Umar ibn Talhah, nor from Umar ibn Talhah except Ibn Abi Fudayk; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Salimi alone narrated it."
"6454","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us: Abu Ghaziyyah Muhammad ibn Musa al-Ansari the judge narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Asad ibn Zurarah narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Asad ibn Zurarah, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) address the people, then glance around and not see Abu Bakr, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Abu Bakr, Abu Bakr; the Holy Spirit Jibril, peace be upon him, has just told me: the best of your ummah after you is Abu Bakr al-Siddiq.” This hadith is not narrated from Asad ibn Zurarah except by this chain; Harun al-Farwi alone narrated it."
"6455","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: al-Zubayr ibn Abbad al-Madani narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The best prayer to Allah is the Maghrib prayer; whoever prays two rakahs after it, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise, wherein he comes and goes.” No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah."
"6456","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs al-Misri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Maymun al-Khayyat al-Makki narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Three are true: Allah does not make one who has a share in Islam like one who has no share; no servant takes Allah as ally and then turns to another as ally; and no man loves a people but will be gathered with them.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Uyaynah except Muhammad ibn Maymun, and no one narrated it from Ismail ibn Abi Khalid except Ibn Uyaynah."
"6457","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman ibn Nadlah narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Musab ibn Thabit ibn Abdillah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came in one day and saw a morsel lying cast aside; he walked to it, took it, wiped it, then ate it, then said: “O Aishah, treat Allah’s blessings as a good neighbor, for seldom do they depart from a household and almost return to them.” No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Urwah except Abdullah ibn Musab and al-Qasim ibn Ghusn; Yahya ibn Sulayman alone narrated it from Abdullah ibn Musab, and Adam ibn Abi Iyas alone narrated it from al-Qasim ibn Ghusn."
"6458","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Shibl ibn al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me: Sumayy, freedman of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, narrated to me, from Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, who said: I heard Nawfal ibn Muawiyah al-Dayli say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drink in three breaths, naming Allah at the first of them and praising Him at the last of them. This hadith is not narrated from Nawfal ibn Muawiyah except by this chain; al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri alone narrated it."
"6459","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: al-Zubayr ibn Abbad al-Madini narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Zabalah al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Qudamah al-Jumahi narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his grandfather, who said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “O Allah, strengthen Islam with Umar ibn al-Khattab.” This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr except by this chain; al-Zubayr ibn Abbad alone narrated it."
"6460","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Muhammad al-Farwi narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim narrated to me, from his mother, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to offer himself every year to the tribes of the Arabs, asking them to shelter him among their people so that he might convey the speech of Allah and His messages, with Paradise for them; yet no tribe of the Arabs responded to him, until Allah willed to manifest His religion, aid His Prophet, and fulfill what He had promised him, and Allah drove him to this clan of the Ansar, who responded to him, and Allah made for His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) a home of emigration. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim except Abdullah ibn Umar, nor from Abdullah ibn Umar except Ishaq al-Farwi; Harun al-Farwi alone narrated it."
"6461","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman ibn Nadlah al-Khuzai narrated to us: Sulayman ibn Muhammad ibn Yahya ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Abdullah ibn Urwah ibn al-Zubayr narrated to me, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn al-Zubayr — while we were with him, having set out for umrah — when we descended from the hillock into the valley, Ibn al-Zubayr performed ghusl, prayed two rakahs, and we performed ghusl with him and prayed two rakahs with him, then he uttered the talbiyah: “Labbayk, O Allah, labbayk; labbayk, no partner have You; labbayk, praise and blessing are Yours, and dominion; no partner have You.” Abdullah ibn Urwah said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr say: “This, by Allah, is the talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do — he entered ihram at the end of prayer.” This hadith is not narrated from Ibn al-Zubayr except by this chain; Yahya ibn Sulayman ibn Nadlah alone narrated it."
"6462","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Salamah al-Muradi narrated to us: Ibn Muadh Yunus ibn Tamim al-Zuraqi narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Yaqub al-Madani narrated to us: Yahya ibn Anbasah al-Madani al-Sadi narrated to me: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz narrated to us: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me: Abu Hurayrah narrated to me, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever peeps into his neighbor’s house and looks at the nakedness of his Muslim brother, or a woman’s hair, or anything of her body, it is due upon Allah to admit him into the Fire.” This hadith is not narrated from Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz except by this chain; Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Salamah al-Muradi alone narrated it."
"6463","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Jarir ibn Hazim informed me: Ayyub narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Awn, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came on the day of Khaybar, and it was said: O Messenger of Allah, the donkeys have been exhausted. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Abu Talhah, who called out: “Allah and His Messenger forbid you the flesh of domestic donkeys, for it is filth.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Awn except Jarir ibn Hazim; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6464","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Harun ibn Musa al-Farwi narrated to us: Abu Ghaziyyah Muhammad ibn Musa narrated to us: Ishaq ibn Said al-Mazini narrated to us: Ibn Abi Dawud al-Mazini narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather Abu Dawud, who said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); when we reached Dhu al-Hulayfah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque, prayed two rakahs, then entered ihram at the end of the prayer with Hajj and Umrah together. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Dawud except by this chain; Harun al-Farwi alone narrated it."
"6465","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Maymun ibn Kulayb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhajir ibn Mismar narrated to us: Safwan ibn Sulaym narrated to us: Yazid ibn Aban al-Raqashi narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “There is no human but has two gates of heaven: from them his deeds ascend and his provision descends; when the believing servant dies, they weep over him.” No one narrated this hadith from Safwan ibn Sulaym except Ibrahim ibn al-Muhajir ibn Mismar."
"6466","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Abu Nuaym Abd al-Awwal ibn Abdillah al-Muallim narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us: Wahib ibn Abdillah al-Maafiri narrated to me, who said: I heard Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani say: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) take the hand of his uncle al-Abbas, then say: “O Abbas, there is no prophethood but caliphate comes after it; from your offspring at the end of time will rule seventeen, among them al-Saffah, among them al-Mansur, among them al-Mahdi — though he is no Mahdi — among them al-Jamuh, among them al-Aqib, among them al-Wahin of your offspring; and woe to my ummah from him — how he will hamstring it, destroy it, and take its wealth, he and his followers, upon other than the religion of Islam; when allegiance is given to his boy, at the eighteenth their rule ends and the people of the West come out of their homes.” This hadith is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except by this chain; Ibn Lahiah alone narrated it."
"6467","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Umar ibn Yunus al-Yamami narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sadus al-Sanani narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Mina narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to al-Abbas: “The world will not pass until one of your offspring, O uncle, rules at the end of time, at the end of their rule — he is the eighteenth — with a blind, deaf tribulation in which nine thousand nine hundred of every ten thousand are killed; only a few escape, and their fighting will be at a place in Iraq.” Al-Abbas wept, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: “What makes you weep? They are the worst of my ummah, shooting out of the religion as an arrow shoots out of the game, seeking the world and caring nothing for the Hereafter.” This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Masud except by this chain; Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Yamami alone narrated it."
"6468","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Muhammad al-Yamami narrated to us: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us: Mamar narrated to us, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Asr; when he was in the fourth (rakah), al-Hasan and al-Husayn came and climbed onto the back of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he placed them before him. Then al-Hasan came forward, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) carried al-Hasan on his right shoulder and al-Husayn on his left shoulder, then said: “O people, shall I tell you of the best of people in grandfather and grandmother? Or shall I tell you of the best of people in uncle and aunt? Shall I tell you of the best of people in maternal uncle and maternal aunt? Shall I tell you of the best of people in father and mother? They are al-Hasan and al-Husayn: their grandfather is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), their grandmother is Khadijah bint Khuwaylid, their mother is Fatimah bint Rasulillah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), their father is Ali ibn Abi Talib, their uncle is Jafar ibn Abi Talib, their aunt is Umm Hani bint Abi Talib, their maternal uncle is al-Qasim son of the Messenger of Allah, their maternal aunts are Zaynab, Ruqayyah and Umm Kulthum, daughters of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Their grandfather is in Paradise, their father is in Paradise, their grandmother is in Paradise, their mother, uncle and aunt are in Paradise, their maternal aunts are in Paradise, their maternal uncle is in Paradise, they two are in Paradise, and their sister is in Paradise.” No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Razzaq except Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Yunus al-Yamami."
"6469","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: al-Zubayr ibn Abbad al-Madini narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Zabalah narrated to us: Abd al-Malik ibn Qudamah narrated to us: my father narrated to me, from his grandfather, who said: I heard Abu Bakr al-Siddiq say: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Every ummah has a trustee, and the trustee of this ummah is Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah.” This hadith is not narrated from Abu Bakr except by this chain; al-Zubayr ibn Abbad al-Madini alone narrated it."
"6470","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Yahya ibn Sulayman ibn Nadlah al-Madani narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Aslami narrated to us: al-Layth ibn Abi Sulaym narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad narrated to me: Anas ibn Malik narrated to us, who said: I prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr and Umar; all of them would raise their hands when opening the prayer, when saying takbir for bowing, and when raising the head, saying takbir for prostration. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad except Layth ibn Abi Sulaym; Ibrahim ibn Muhammad al-Aslami alone narrated it."
"6471","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us: Umar ibn Sahl al-Mazini narrated to us: al-Mubarak ibn Fudalah narrated to us: al-Hasan narrated to us, from Samurah ibn Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I was commanded to fight people until they say: there is no god but Allah; when they say it, they have protected their blood and wealth from me except by its right, and their reckoning is upon Allah.” No one narrated this hadith from Mubarak ibn Fudalah except Umar ibn Sahl al-Mazini; Ishaq ibn al-Dayf alone narrated it."
"6472","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs al-Misri narrated to us: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Hasan ibn Zabalah al-Makhzumi narrated to us: Musa ibn Yaqub al-Zamai narrated to us: Quraybah bint Abdillah ibn Wahb ibn Zamah narrated to me, from her mother Karimah bint al-Miqdad ibn Amr, from Dubaah bint al-Zubayr ibn Abd al-Muttalib, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a sandal with a narrow middle (khasrah). This hadith is not narrated from Dubaah except by this chain; al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar alone narrated it."
"6473","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ayyash ibn Abbas al-Qitbani narrated to me: Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us: Ibn Shihab narrated to me, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sacrificed two white-black horned rams: one for himself and his household, and the other for himself and whoever of his ummah did not sacrifice. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman, nor from Isa except Abdullah ibn Ayyash; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6474","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Mazini narrated to us: Ismail ibn Yahya al-Tamimi narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Umar narrated to us, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, while on the Farewell Hajj, upon his she-camel, with his hand on the shoulder of Ali: “O Allah, have I conveyed? O Allah, have I conveyed? This is my cousin and the father of my offspring. O Allah, cast whoever shows him enmity into the Fire.” No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Umar except Ismail ibn Yahya al-Tamimi; Muhammad ibn Sahl al-Mazini alone narrated it."
"6475","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Abu Nuaym Abd al-Awwal al-Muallim narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us: Usamah ibn Zayd al-Laythi narrated to me, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The worst slain is one killed between two ranks, one of them seeking kingship.” No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Usamah ibn Zayd, nor from Usamah except Ibn Wahb; Abd al-Awwal al-Muallim alone narrated it."
"6476","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to me: Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani narrated to us: Ishaq ibn al-Furat narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to me: Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah narrated to me, who said: I heard Nuaym al-Mujmir say: I heard Marwan say to Abu Hurayrah: By Allah, I love you, were it not that you love al-Hasan ibn Ali. Abu Hurayrah said to Marwan: Why should I not love him, when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one day come to their door and call: “O Hasan,” and al-Hasan came out to him, and he placed his mouth upon his mouth, sucked his tongue, and embraced him — by Allah, I shall never cease to love him. No one narrated this hadith from Umarah ibn Ghaziyyah except Yahya ibn Ayyub, nor from Yahya except Ishaq ibn al-Furat; Ahmad ibn Said al-Hamdani alone narrated it."
"6477","Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Irs narrated to us: Harmalah ibn Yahya narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to me, from his father, from his grandfather, who said: I heard Ammar ibn Yasir at Siffin, on the day he was struck down, calling out: I have met the Almighty, and married the wide-eyed houris; today we meet the beloved — Muhammad and his party. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) enjoined upon me: “The last of your provision from this world will be a cup of milk.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf except through the hadith of his son, nor from Ibrahim ibn Sad except Ibn Wahb; Harmalah ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"6478","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn bint Rishdin al-Misri narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashjai narrated to us: Makhramah ibn Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj narrated to me, from his father, from Abu Harb ibn Zayd ibn Khalid al-Juhani, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, saying: “Give people glad tidings that whoever says: there is no god but Allah, alone, with no partner, enters Paradise.” No one narrated this hadith from Abu Harb ibn Zayd ibn Khalid except Bukayr ibn Abdillah, nor from Bukayr except his son Makhramah; Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashjai alone narrated it."
"6479","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Qudamah ibn Muhammad al-Ashjai narrated to us: Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to me, from his father, who said: I heard Amr ibn al-Harith say: I heard Amir ibn Yahya al-Maafiri say: I heard Hanash al-Sanani say: I heard Fudalah ibn Ubayd say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “None shall take it except like for like” — meaning gold for gold and silver for silver. No one narrated this hadith from Bukayr ibn Abdillah except Makhramah; Qudamah ibn Muhammad alone narrated it."
"6480","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Qudamah ibn Muhammad narrated to us: Makhramah ibn Bukayr narrated to me, from his father, who said: I heard Amr ibn Shuayb say: I heard Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Shihab say: I heard Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn Utbah ibn Masud say: I heard Abu Hurayrah say: Two men came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of them said: O Messenger of Allah, judge between me and this one. My son was a hireling for his wife, and my son is a virgin who never married, and he committed adultery with her. I asked one who does not know, and they told me my son deserved stoning, so I ransomed him for such-and-such. Then I asked one who knows, and they told me my son does not deserve stoning. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I shall judge between you two by the truth: what you gave, he shall return to you; as for your son, he shall be lashed a hundred and exiled a year; and as for his wife, she shall be stoned.” No one narrated this hadith from Amr ibn Shuayb except Bukayr ibn Abdillah, nor from Bukayr except Makhramah, nor from Makhramah except Qudamah ibn Muhammad; Ahmad ibn Salih alone narrated it."
"6481","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn ibn bint Rishdin narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Muslim say: I heard Muhammad ibn Muslim say: I heard Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf say: I heard Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), say: It was said to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Where were you, O Messenger of Allah, regarding the daughter of Hamzah? Or it was said: Will you not propose the daughter of Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib? He said: “Hamzah is my brother through breastfeeding.” No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except his brother, nor from his brother except Bukayr ibn Abdillah, nor from Bukayr except Makhramah; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6482","Muhammad ibn al-Husayn narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Makhramah informed me, from his father, from Amir ibn Sad, who said: I heard Sad say: There were two brothers in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); one of them was better than the other. The better of them died, then the other lived forty nights after him, then died. The merit of the first over the latter was mentioned to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: “Did he not pray?” They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “And he was of no harm?” They said: Yes. He said: “And how do you know how far his prayer raised him?” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said at that: “The parable of the prayers is like a deep, sweet river at a man’s door into which he plunges five times each day; what do you think that leaves of his dirt? You do not know how far his prayer raised him.” No one narrated this hadith from Amir ibn Sad, from his father, except Bukayr ibn Abdillah ibn al-Ashajj, nor from Bukayr except Makhramah; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it. Ibn Akhi al-Zuhri narrated it from al-Zuhri, from Salih ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Farwah, from Amir ibn Sad, from Aban ibn Uthman, from his father."
"6483","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah al-Misri narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Raqqi narrated to us: Jafar ibn Burqan narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to me, who said: Anas ibn Malik came to Madinah, so Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz sent me, saying: Ask him about a hadith narrated by al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf concerning a people who went out in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): he gouged out the eyes of two, cut off (the limbs of) two, and crucified two. Anas said: “Those had affirmed Islam and settled in Madinah, then they left out of aversion to Islam, joined the people of shirk, and raided the pasturing camels of Madinah and drove them off. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was told of them, sent in pursuit of them, and seized these men.” Umar sent back to him, saying: “Would that you had not narrated this hadith to al-Hajjaj; these had turned away from Islam and joined the people of shirk and raided the pasturing camels of Madinah, while al-Hajjaj deems this lawful against one who neither left Islam nor joined the people of shirk.” Umar said: And ask him: Did the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dye (his hair)? For we see here some hair of his as though colored? Anas said: “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was blessed with black hair; if I counted what faced me of his head and beard, I would not count fifteen white hairs; and this hair of his you find colored is only from the perfume placed in the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him).” No one narrated this hadith from Abdullah ibn Muhammad except Jafar ibn Burqan; Muhammad ibn Hamzah al-Raqqi alone narrated it."
"6484","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi narrated to us: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Nafi informed me, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The Muslim is the brother of the Muslim: he does not betray him nor forsake him. The Muslims are one hand against others; their blood is equal in worth, and the least of them grants protection on their behalf.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibrahim ibn Nafi except Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad; Said ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"6485","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us: Abu al-Qasim ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Abi Habibah narrated to me, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from Ikrimah, from Ibn Abbas: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Dubaah to stipulate in Hajj, saying: “My release is where You restrain me.” No one narrated this hadith from Dawud ibn al-Husayn except Ibrahim ibn Ismail; Said ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"6486","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya ibn Said narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, from Mujahid, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be in his house as one of you is in his house: sewing his garment and working as one of you works. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Yahya ibn Said."
"6487","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Abdillah ibn Abi Talhah, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Umm Sulaym asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to come to her house and pray in it, so she could take it as a place of prayer; he did so — he came to her, she took a mat of theirs and sprinkled it with water, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed, and they prayed with him. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said al-Ansari except Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi and Sulayman ibn Kathir."
"6488","Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya narrated to us: Isa ibn Yunus narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah al-Ansari — and His saying: ‘Allah was pleased with the believers when they pledged to you under the tree’ — Jabir said: We pledged to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not to flee, and we did not pledge to him unto death. No one narrated this hadith from al-Awzai except Isa ibn Yunus; Said ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"6489","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab addressed us in Syria and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as I stand among you, and said: “Treat my Companions well, treat my Companions well; then those after them, then those after them; then lying will spread until a man acts upon testimony before he is asked for it, and upon an oath before he is asked to swear it. Whoever wants the middle of Paradise, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the solitary one and is farther from two. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his bad deed is a believer.” No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash; Said ibn Yahya al-Umawi alone narrated it."
"6490","Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar narrated to us: Abu Damrah Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Said, who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrate that Ibn Umar narrated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The two sellers retain the option in their sale until they part, or the sale involves an option.” No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, except Abu Damrah; al-Zubayr ibn Bakkar alone narrated it."
"6491","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya narrated to us: my father narrated to me: Sad ibn Said narrated to us, who said: I heard Anas ibn Malik say: Abu Talhah sent me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a harirah he had made for him, singling him out with it, saying: Go, invite the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for me. I went to him; when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me among his Companions, he fixed his gaze upon me until all the people looked at me, and I felt shy. He said: “Has Abu Talhah sent to us?” I said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Rise.” The people rose with him, and I hurried to Abu Talhah and told him the news. Abu Talhah came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I made something for you alone that cannot hold them. He said: “It will hold them, Allah willing.” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered, invoked blessing over it, then said: “Admit ten.” They entered and ate until satisfied, then left. He said: “Admit another ten.” Ten entered and ate until all were satisfied. Then he took what remained, gathered it, invoked blessing over it, and it returned to what it had been. He said: “Take this for yourselves.” No one narrated this hadith from Sad ibn Said except Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi."
"6492","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Mujahid ibn Musa narrated to us: al-Qasim ibn Malik al-Muzani narrated to us: Said al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadrah, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: We fasted twenty-nine with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) more often than we fasted thirty. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except al-Qasim ibn Malik; Mujahid ibn Musa alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah except by this chain."
"6493","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya al-Umawi narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Yazid ibn Sinan narrated to me, from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Masud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “As though I see Musa ibn Imran in this valley, in ihram between two striped cloaks.” No one narrated this hadith from Asim except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, nor from Zayd except Yazid ibn Sinan; Yahya ibn Sad al-Umawi alone narrated it."
"6494","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Said ibn Yahya narrated to us: my father narrated to us: Malik ibn Mighwal narrated to us, from Mualla al-Kindi, from Mujahid, from Ibn Umar, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the tenth of ten, when a man of the Ansar came and said: O Prophet of Allah, who is the shrewdest and most resolute of people? He said: “Those who remember death most and prepare most for death before death descends; those are the shrewd — they have carried off the honor of this world and the dignity of the Hereafter.” No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except Yahya ibn Said al-Umawi."
"6495","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Adami narrated to us: Abd al-Majid ibn Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Rawwad narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: “The rewards of my ummah were shown to me, even the speck a man removes from the mosque; and the sins of my ummah were shown to me, and I saw no sin greater than a verse or surah given to a man who then forgot it.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Zuhri, from Anas, except Abd al-Majid; Muhammad ibn Yazid al-Adami alone narrated it. And Muhammad ibn Yazid narrated it from Abd al-Majid, from Ibn Jurayj, from al-Muttalib, from Anas."
"6496","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us: Ismail ibn Umar Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us: al-Masudi narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Abdullah ibn Ukaym, who said: A letter of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reached us: “Do not make use of the dead animal’s hide or sinew.” No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except al-Masudi, nor from al-Masudi except Ismail ibn Umar; Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi alone narrated it."
"6497","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Mansur al-Tusi narrated to us: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us: Ammar ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, from Fitr ibn Khalifah, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Ata al-Khurasani, from Humran, who said: I heard Ibn Umar say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Whoever says: Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, and Allah is Greatest, ten good deeds are written for him for every letter; whoever aids in a false dispute remains in Allah’s wrath until he withdraws; whoever’s intercession blocks one of Allah’s prescribed punishments has opposed Allah in His command; and whoever slanders a believing man or woman, Allah will detain him on the Day of Resurrection in Radghat al-Khabal until he exits from what he said — and he will never exit.” No one narrated this hadith from Ata al-Khurasani, from Humran, except al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, nor from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah except Fitr, nor from Fitr except Ammar ibn Ruzayq; Abu al-Jawwab alone narrated it."
"6498","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Ibrahim ibn Said al-Jawhari narrated to us: Abu al-Jawwab narrated to us, from Ammar ibn Ruzayq, from Ikrimah ibn Khalid, from Yahya ibn Jadah, from Ibn Umar, who said: I met Bilal and said: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pray inside the Kabah? He said: He prayed two rakahs between the two pillars, with the middle pillar to his right. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Jadah except Ikrimah ibn Khalid, nor from Ikrimah except Ammar ibn Ruzayq; Abu al-Jawwab alone narrated it."
"6499","Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us: Ali ibn Asim narrated to us; he said: Yunus ibn Ubayd claimed, from al-Hasan, from Mutarrif, from Imran ibn Husayn, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us cauterization, but we were cauterized, and we neither prospered nor succeeded. No one among those who narrated it from Yunus ibn Ubayd placed anyone in the chain of this hadith between al-Hasan and Imran ibn Husayn except Ali ibn Asim."
"6500","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Ali ibn Shuayb al-Simsar narrated to us: Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Salih narrated to us, from Abu al-Wazi, from Abdullah ibn Busr al-Sulami: he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “The Dajjal will surely be encountered by whoever encountered me, or he will be close to my death.” No one narrated this hadith from Muawiyah ibn Salih except Man."
"6501","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Ali al-Ihtiyati narrated to us: Abu Abdillah al-Jawzajani — companion of Ibrahim ibn Adham — narrated to us: Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, from Ata, from Ibn Abbas, who said: This verse was recited before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ‘O people, eat of what is in the earth, lawful and good.’ Sad ibn Abi Waqqas stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, invoke Allah to make me one whose supplication is answered. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: “O Sad, make your food pure and you will be one whose supplication is answered; by the One in Whose hand is Muhammad’s soul, a servant casts an unlawful morsel into his belly and no deed is accepted from him for forty days; and any servant whose flesh grows from ill-gotten gain and usury — the Fire is more deserving of him.” This hadith is not narrated from Ibn Jurayj except by this chain; al-Ihtiyati alone narrated it."
"6502","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us: Bakr ibn Sadaqah narrated to us, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from Aishah, who said: A month and a half would pass and no fire would be lit in the house of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), neither for lamp nor otherwise. I said: Glory be to Allah, upon what did you live? She said: “Upon water and dates; we had neighbors of the Ansar with milch she-camels, and they would sometimes gift us milk.” No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, from Aishah, except Bakr ibn Sadaqah; al-Munkadiri alone narrated it; and others narrated it from Bakr ibn Sadaqah, from Ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa, from al-Qasim, from Aishah."
"6503","Muhammad ibn Isa narrated to us: al-Hasan ibn Dawud al-Munkadiri narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Awn ibn al-Khattab, from Anas ibn Malik: the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The houris in Paradise sing, saying: ” (no words of the song are given in the text). No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Abi Dhib except Ibn Abi Fudayk; al-Munkadiri alone narrated it."
"6504","Muhammad ibn Isa ibn Shaybah narrated to us: Khallad ibn Aslam al-Marwazi narrated to us: Marwan ibn Shuja narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Ikrimah, Mujahid and Ata, from Ibn Abbas — raising the hadith to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) — who said: “The woman in postnatal bleeding and the menstruating woman perform ghusl, enter ihram, and perform all the rites except that she does not circumambulate the House until she is pure.” No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Marwan ibn Shuja."
"6505","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Aslam al-Sadafi al-Misri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Uqayl: he heard Nafi report from Abdullah ibn Umar: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whatever inheritance was divided in the Jahiliyyah stands upon the division of the Jahiliyyah; and whatever inheritance Islam overtakes stands upon the division of Islam.” No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Uqayl, nor from Uqayl except Ibn Lahiah; Muhammad ibn Rumh alone narrated it."
"6506","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Aslam al-Sadafi narrated to us: Abu Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Thawban al-Hamdani, Amr ibn al-Harith, al-Layth ibn Sad and Ibn Lahiah, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abdullah ibn al-Harith ibn Jaz al-Zubaydi, who said: I am the first who heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “None of you shall urinate facing the qiblah,” and the first who told people of it. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Thawban except Rishdin."
"6507","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Aslam al-Sadafi narrated to us: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam narrated to us: Talq ibn al-Samh narrated to us: Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Humayd al-Tawil, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Some people visited him in an illness of his, and he said: O girl, bring our companions even unripe dates, for I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Noble morals are among the deeds of Paradise.” No one narrated this hadith from Humayd except Yahya ibn Ayyub, nor from Yahya except Talq ibn al-Samh; Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdillah ibn Abd al-Hakam alone narrated it."
"6508","Muhammad ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Said al-Fihri narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Ismail al-Madani narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from his grandfather, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When Adam committed the sin he committed, he raised his head to the Throne and said: I ask You by the right of Muhammad to forgive me. Allah revealed to him: What is Muhammad, and who is Muhammad? He said: Blessed be Your name; when You created me I raised my head to Your Throne, and there written was: there is no god but Allah, Muhammad is the Messenger of Allah — so I knew that none is greater in worth to You than one whose name You joined with Your name. Allah revealed to him: O Adam, he is the last of the prophets of your offspring, and his ummah is the last of the nations of your offspring; were it not for him, O Adam, I would not have created you.” No one narrated this hadith from Zayd ibn Aslam except his son Abd al-Rahman, nor from his son except Abdullah ibn Ismail al-Madani; it is not narrated from Umar except by this chain."
"6509","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Aslam narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah ibn al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir narrated to us: my father narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “I was permitted to speak of an angel of the Throne-bearers: his feet are in the lowest earth, the Throne is upon his horn, between his earlobe and his shoulder is a seven-hundred-year flight of a bird; the angel says: Glory be to You wherever You are.” No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Anas ibn Malik, except his son Munkadir; his son alone narrated it from him. And Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated it from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir."
"6510","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Aslam al-Sadafi narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah al-Munkadiri narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us; he said: I heard Abu Muhammad al-Shami narrate that he heard Abu Hurayrah mention that he heard Anas ibn Malik say: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Whenever one of a household dies and they give charity on his behalf after his death, Jibril, peace be upon him, brings it to him upon a plate of light, then stands at the edge of the grave and says: O dweller of the deep grave, this is a gift your family has gifted to you — accept it. It enters to him, and he rejoices in it and is gladdened, while his neighbors to whom nothing is gifted grieve.” This hadith is not narrated from Anas except by this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk alone narrated it."
"6511","Muhammad ibn Dawud ibn Aslam narrated to us: Ubaydullah ibn Abdillah al-Munkadiri narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Ishaq, from Abd al-Majid ibn Abi Abs ibn Jabr, from his father, from his grandfather: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “This Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it; it stands at one of the gates of Paradise. And this Ayr hates us and we hate it; it stands at one of the gates of the Fire.” This hadith is not narrated from Abu Abs ibn Jabr except by this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk alone narrated it."
"6512","Muhammad ibn Dawud narrated to us: Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarhi narrated to us: Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Thaqafi narrated to us, from Abu Umayyah ibn Yala, from Said ibn Abi Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Hurayrah: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Allah revealed to Ibrahim: O My friend, improve your character, even with the disbeliever, and you will enter the entry of the righteous; for My word has preceded that whoever is good in character, I shall shade him under My Throne, give him to drink from My holy enclosure, and bring him near to My neighborhood.” No one narrated this hadith from Said al-Maqburi except Abu Umayyah ibn Yala; Muammal ibn Abd al-Rahman alone narrated it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this chain."
"6513","Muhammad ibn Dawud narrated to us: Ahmad ibn Malik ibn Anas narrated to us: Muhammad ibn al-Walid ibn Amr ibn al-Zubayr narrated to us: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah and Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us; they said: Muhammad ibn Amr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Kabshah, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: “Dinars and dirhams are Allah’s seals in His land; whoever comes with his Master’s seal, his need is fulfilled.” This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this chain."
"6514","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami al-Misri narrated to us: Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi narrated to us: Hamzah ibn Umayr, scribe of Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak, narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Ibrahim Abu Yahya al-Muallim, from Ibrahim al-Saigh, from Abu Khalid al-Dabbi, from Abu Dawud, from Maqil ibn Yasar, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to judge among my people. I said: I am not skilled in judging. He said: “Judge among them, for Allah is with the judge so long as he does not deliberately act unjustly.” This hadith is not narrated from Maqil ibn Yasar except by this chain; Ibrahim al-Saigh alone narrated it. And Abu Khalid al-Dabbi from whom Ibrahim al-Saigh narrated this hadith is Muhammad ibn Khalid al-Dabbi, and Abu Dawud is Nufay ibn al-Harith."
"6515","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us: Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi narrated to us: Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us: Muawiyah ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu al-Zinad, from al-Araj, from Abu Hurayrah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever narrates a hadith and sneezes with it, it is true.” No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zinad except Muawiyah ibn Yahya; Baqiyyah alone narrated it. And it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except by this chain."
"6516","With the same chain: Baqiyyah narrated to us: Habib ibn Umar al-Ansari informed us, from his father, from Ibn Umar, from his father Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “On the Day of Resurrection a caller will call: Let the adversaries of Allah stand — and they are the Qadariyyah.” This hadith is not narrated from Umar except by this chain; Baqiyyah alone narrated it."
"6517","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us: Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us: al-Amash narrated to me, from Anas ibn Malik: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The people of the Fire will be displayed on the Day of Resurrection in rows; the believers will pass by them, and a man of the Fire will see a man of the believers whom he knew in the world and say: O so-and-so, do you not remember the day you sought my help for such-and-such need? And he will say to him: Do you not remember the day I gave you such-and-such? That believer will remember, then intercede for him to his Lord, and his intercession for him will be accepted.” No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti."
"6518","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Zuhrah ibn Mabad, from Abu Said al-Maqburi, from Abu Said al-Khudri: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever fasts a day in the path of Allah, Allah distances him from the Fire by seventy autumns; and whoever dies guarding the frontier is spared the trial of the grave, and his provision continues for him.” No one narrated this hadith from Abu Said al-Maqburi except Zuhrah ibn Mabad; Rishdin alone narrated it."
"6519","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Rishdin ibn Sad narrated to us, from Musa ibn Ayyub al-Ghafiqi, from Sahl ibn Rafi ibn Khadij, from his father: the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by him and called him; he came out to him and walked with him until they reached the mosque, then he left, performed ghusl, then returned, and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw him with traces of ghusl. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked him about his ghusl, and he said: I heard your call while I was with my wife, so I rose before finishing and performed ghusl. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Water is for water.” Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said afterward: “When the two circumcised parts meet, ghusl is obligatory.” No one narrated this hadith from Sahl ibn Rafi except Musa ibn Ayyub; Rishdin alone narrated it."
"6520","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn Abi Uways narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abdillah ibn Dumayrah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Abu Hurayrah, from Aishah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said when death came to him, stretching out his hand and saying: “O Jibril, where are you?” — then grasping it and spreading it, doing that repeatedly, saying: “O Jibril, intercede for me with my Lord to ease death for me.” Abu Hurayrah mentioned that he heard Aishah say: I heard from Jibril what no ear has heard, as he says: “Labbayk.” This hadith is not narrated from Abu Hurayrah, from Aishah, except by this chain; Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh alone narrated it."
"6521","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us: Abdullah ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yuhannis narrated to me, from Yahya ibn Abi Sufyan ibn Sad ibn al-Akhnas, from his grandmother Hukaymah, from Umm Salamah, wife of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): she heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: “Whoever enters ihram for Hajj and Umrah from al-Masjid al-Aqsa to al-Masjid al-Haram, his past and future sins are forgiven, and Paradise becomes due for him.” This hadith is not narrated from Umm Salamah except by this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk alone narrated it."
"6522","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Abu Bakr Abdullah ibn Salih al-Hashimi narrated to us; he said: I heard my father narrate, from his father, who said: I prayed behind Anas ibn Malik a prayer in which he made us forget (an act); so he prostrated after the salam, then turned to us and said: I have done only as I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do. No one narrated this hadith from Salih ibn Ali ibn Abdillah ibn Abbas except his son; Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh alone narrated it."
"6523","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us: Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us: Ubayd ibn Waqid al-Qaysi narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Ata narrated to us, from Umayr ibn Yazid, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith, from Abu Qurad al-Sulami, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he called for water for purification; he dipped his hand in it, then performed wudu, and we followed him and drank it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “What made you do what you did?” We said: Love of Allah and His Messenger. He said: “If you love that Allah and His Messenger love you, then fulfill when entrusted, speak truthfully when you speak, and treat your neighbor well.” This hadith is not narrated from Abu Qurad except by this chain; Ubayd ibn Waqid alone narrated it."
"6524","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Idris ibn Yahya narrated to us, from Abu al-Ashyam, from Wahib ibn Abdillah al-Kabi, from Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever feeds his brother bread until he is full, and gives him drink until he is quenched, Allah distances him from the Fire by seven trenches.” This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Amr except by this chain; Idris ibn Yahya alone narrated it."
"6525","Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us: Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us: Ibn Wahb narrated to us: Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, who said: I heard Abd al-Malik ibn Sariyah al-Akki say: I heard Abdullah ibn Waqid say: The oath in (cases of) blood was already practiced in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). This hadith is not narrated from Abdullah ibn Waqid except by this chain; Ibn Wahb alone narrated it."
"6526","6520 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, I heard him narrating, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir ibn Abdillah, that a man committed fornication with a woman, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered regarding him and he was flogged the hadd, then he was informed that he had been muhsan, so he ordered regarding him and he was stoned. No one narrated this hadith from Ibn Jurayj except Ibn Wahb."
"6527","6521 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, that Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah narrated that Abu Ishaq narrated that al-Aswad and Alqamah both narrated to him, from Abdullah ibn Masud who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) not knowing anything, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Say in every sitting: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words belong to Allah, peace be upon you O Prophet, peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah, I bear witness that there is no god but Allah and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Ishaq, from Alqamah, except Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah, and no one narrated it from Zayd ibn Abi Unaysah except Amr ibn al-Harith; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted it."
"6528","6522 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir narrated to us, Salamah ibn Rawh al-Ayli, the nephew of Uqayl ibn Khalid, narrated to us, from Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, Anas ibn Malik al-Ansari informed me, he said: While I was traveling with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), his mount descended with him from a pass, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was traveling alone, then when the road became easy for him he laughed and said takbir, so we said takbir for his takbir, then he traveled a short distance, then he laughed and said takbir, so we said takbir for his takbir, then we caught up with him, and the people said: O Messenger of Allah, we said takbir for your takbir, but we do not know why you laughed. He said: Jibril, peace be upon him, was leading the camel for me, then when it became easy he turned to me and said: Receive glad tidings and give your ummah glad tidings that whoever says: There is no god but Allah alone, without partner, will enter Paradise, and Allah has forbidden the Fire for him, so I laughed and said takbir, and I rejoiced at that for my ummah. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Uqayl, and none from Uqayl except Salamah ibn Rawh; Abu al-Tahir alone transmitted it."
"6529","6523 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir narrated to us, Man ibn Isa narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Jabir al-Jufi, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: The ring of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was entirely of silver, then it was with Abu Bakr, then it was with Umar, then it was with Uthman for as long as Allah willed, then it was lost while with Uthman. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except Ibrahim ibn Tahman; Man ibn Isa alone transmitted it."
"6530","6524 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father, from Said ibn Nafi, he said: Abu Bashir al-Ansari, the Companion of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), saw me while I was praying the Duha prayer when the sun had risen, so he criticized me for that and forbade me, then he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray until the sun has risen high, for it rises between the two horns of Satan. No one narrated this hadith from Bukayr ibn Abdillah except his son Makhramah; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Abu Bashir except with this chain."
"6531","6525 - And with the same chain: Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed me, that Qatadah ibn Diamah said: Anas ibn Malik narrated to me, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having performed wudu, but he had left on his feet an area like the spot of a fingernail, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Go back and perfect your wudu. No one narrated this hadith from Qatadah except Jarir ibn Hazim; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted it."
"6532","6526 - And with the same chain, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abdillah ibn Salim narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Amr, the freedman of al-Muttalib, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I kept to the siwak until I feared it would strip my teeth of flesh. This hadith is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted it."
"6533","6527 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarhi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Said ibn Abi Ayyub informed me, from Sharahil ibn Zayd al-Maafiri, from Abu Alqamah, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Allah will send for this ummah at the head of every hundred years one who will renew its religion for it. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted it."
"6534","6528 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Man ibn Isa al-Qazzaz narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intended to write to the non-Arab kings, so some non-Arab people with him said to him: They, O Messenger of Allah, do not accept a letter except with a seal, so he took a ring of silver, as if I am looking at its whiteness on his palm, then he engraved in it: Muhammad, Messenger of Allah."
"6535","6529 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Ibrahim narrated to us, Man narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Ala ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am the most self-sufficient of partners from association, so whoever does a deed in which he associates another with Me, I am free of him and it belongs to the one he associated."
"6536","6530 - And with the same chain, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from Mutarrif ibn Tarif, from al-Hakam ibn Utaybah, from al-Hasan al-Urani, from Amr ibn Hurayth, from Said ibn Zayd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Truffles are from the manna, and their water is a cure for the eye."
"6537","6531 - And with the same chain, Ibrahim ibn Tahman narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj ibn al-Hajjaj, from Salamah ibn Khubayb, from Urwah ibn Ali al-Sahmi, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us that one of us put on sandals while standing, and that he clean himself with a bone, or with what comes out of a belly. No one narrated these hadiths from Ibrahim ibn Tahman except Man ibn Isa and Hafs ibn Abdillah, except the hadith of Urwah ibn Ali, for Yazid ibn Abi Hakim shared with them in its narration."
"6538","6532 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Rumh narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad, from Urwah ibn al-Zubayr, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: The Jews and the Christians do not dye, so differ from them. No one narrated this hadith from Urwah except Abu al-Aswad; Ibn Luhayah alone transmitted it."
"6539","6533 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl ibn Abi Hudhayrah al-Misri narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Balisi narrated to us, from Khusayf, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Islam is built upon testifying that there is no god but Allah, establishing the prayer, giving the zakah, hajj of the House, and fasting Ramadan. No one narrated this hadith from Khusayf except Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd al-Rahman; al-Husayn ibn al-Fadl alone transmitted it."
"6540","6534 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Harun ibn Said al-Ayli narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Maruf ibn Suwayd al-Judhami informed me, that he heard Ulayy ibn Rabah saying: I heard Abu Hurayrah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fear the supplication of the oppressed."
"6541","6535 - And with the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The price of a dog is not lawful, nor the payment of a soothsayer, nor the dowry of a prostitute."
"6542","6536 - And with the same chain, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no contagion, no evil omen, and the evil eye is true. No one narrated these hadiths from Ulayy ibn Rabah except Maruf ibn Suwayd; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted them."
"6543","6537 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarhi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Asim ibn Hakim informed me, from Yahya ibn Abi Amr al-Saybani, from his father, from Uqbah ibn Amir al-Juhani, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Pray in the resting places of sheep, and do not pray in the kneeling places of camels. This hadith is not narrated from Uqbah ibn Amir except with this chain; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted it."
"6544","6538 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Yusuf ibn al-Sabbah al-Attar al-Misri narrated to us, Baqiyyah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, Umar ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, from Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not declare openly: I am upon the faith of Jibril and Mikail, peace be upon them. No one narrated this hadith from Ayyub except al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar, and none from al-Hasan except Umar ibn al-Mughirah; Baqiyyah alone transmitted it."
"6545","6539 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir al-Hizami narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Sad al-Muadhdhin narrated to us, from Malik ibn Ubaydah al-Dayli, from his father, from his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Were it not for servants of Allah who bow, and nursing infants, and grazing cattle, punishment would have been poured upon you in torrents, then ground to dust. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Ubaydah al-Dayli except with this chain; Ibrahim ibn al-Mundhir alone transmitted it."
"6546","6540 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Habib narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Ali al-Hilali, from his father who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) during his illness in which he passed away, and Fatimah was at his head. He said: She wept until her voice rose, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his glance to her and said: My beloved Fatimah, what makes you weep? She said: I fear destitution after you. He said: O my beloved, do you not know that Allah looked upon the earth once, and chose from it your father and sent him with His message, then looked upon the earth again and chose from it your husband, and revealed to me that I marry you to him. O Fatimah, we are a household to whom Allah has given seven qualities, given to no one before us, and to be given to no one after us: I am the seal of the prophets, and the most honored of the prophets before Allah, and the most beloved of creation to Allah, and I am your father; and my successor is the best of successors and the most beloved of them to Allah, and he is your husband; and our martyr is the best of martyrs and the most beloved of them to Allah, and he is Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib, and he is the uncle of your father and the uncle of your husband; and from us is the one who has two green wings, flying in Paradise with the angels wherever he wishes, and he is the cousin of your father and the brother of your husband; and from us are the two grandsons of this ummah, and they are your two sons al-Hasan and al-Husayn, and they are the masters of the youth of Paradise, and their father, by the One Who sent me with the truth, is better than them. O Fatimah, by the One Who sent me with the truth, from them is the Mahdi of this ummah when the world becomes chaos and confusion, tribulations appear openly, roads are cut off, and some of them raid others, so no elder will have mercy on the young, and no young will honor the elder, then Allah will send at that time from them one who will conquer the fortresses of misguidance, and sealed hearts he will demolish utterly, he will establish the religion at the end of time as I established it at the beginning of time, he will fill the world with justice as it was filled with tyranny. O Fatimah, do not grieve and do not weep, for Allah is more merciful to you and kinder to you than I, and that is due to your position with me and your place in my heart, and Allah has married you to your husband while he is the most noble of my household in lineage, and the most generous of them in rank, and the most merciful of them to the subjects, and the most just of them in equality, and the most discerning of them in judgment, and I have asked my Lord that you be the first of my household to join me. Ali ibn Abi Talib said: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away, Fatimah did not remain after him except seventy-five days until Allah joined her to him. No one narrated this hadith from Ali ibn Ali except Sufyan ibn Uyaynah; al-Haytham ibn Habib alone transmitted it."
"6547","6541 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim al-Marwazi narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn al-Ashath, the companion of al-Fudayl ibn Iyad, narrated to us, Isa ibn Musa al-Ghunjar narrated to us, Umar ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever speaks much, his slips are many, and whoever has many slips, his sins are many, and whoever has many sins, the Fire is more deserving of him, so whoever believes in Allah and the Last Day, let him speak good or keep silent. No one narrated this hadith from Nafi except Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, and none narrated it from Yahya except Umar ibn Rashid, and none from Umar except Isa al-Ghunjar, and none from Isa except Ibrahim ibn al-Ashath; Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim alone transmitted it."
"6548","6542 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, al-Harith ibn Imran al-Jafari narrated to us, from Jafar ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu once each. No one narrated this hadith from Jafar except al-Harith ibn Imran."
"6549","6543 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Abdah ibn Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, al-Nadr ibn Shumayl narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Ikrimah, from Abu Hurayrah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In Paradise there is a palace of pearl, with no crack in it and no weakness, which Allah has prepared for His friend Ibrahim. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Hammad ibn Salamah, and none narrated it from Hammad except al-Nadr ibn Shumayl and Yazid ibn Harun."
"6550","6544 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid ibn Ishaq al-Tabarani narrated to us, Damrah ibn Rabiah narrated to us, from Ismail ibn Ayyash, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaydi, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, that Abu Hind, the freedman of Banu Bayadah, was a cupper who used to cup the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is pleased to look at one in whose heart Allah has formed faith, let him look at Abu Hind, and he said: Marry him, and marry to him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except al-Zubaydi."
"6551","6545 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Amr ibn Sawwad al-Sarhi narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim informed me, that Ayyub al-Sakhtiyani narrated to him that Nafi narrated to him that Abdullah ibn Umar narrated to him, that Umar ibn al-Khattab asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was at al-Jiranah, after he had returned from Taif, saying: O Messenger of Allah, I vowed in the Jahiliyyah to observe itikaf for a day in the Sacred Mosque, what do you think? He said: Go and observe itikaf for a day. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had given him a slave girl from the khumus, then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) freed the captives of the people, he heard their voices saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has freed us, so he asked: What is this? They said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has freed the captives of the people, so Umar said: Go to that slave girl and set her free. No one narrated this hadith from Jarir ibn Hazim except Ibn Wahb."
"6552","6546 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Habbah al-Badri, he said: On the day of Hunayn, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not look in any direction except that he saw Abu Sufyan ibn al-Harith fighting, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abu Sufyan is the best of my family, or: from the best of my family."
"6553","6547 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Harun ibn Said al-Ayli narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Ubaydillah ibn Umar, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from Usayd ibn Hudayr, he said: I was praying on a moonlit night, and I had tied my horse, so it moved about, and I became frightened, so I entered the house, then in the morning I mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he said: Those were the angels who came to listen to your recitation at the end of the night of Surah al-Baqarah; and Usayd had a beautiful voice. No one narrated this hadith from Ubaydillah ibn Umar except Anas ibn Iyad; Harun al-Ayli alone transmitted it."
"6554","6548 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Khalid al-Samti narrated to us, al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah narrated to us, from Bishr ibn Urwah, from Abdullah ibn Abi Awfa who said: From the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was: O Allah, cool my heart with coolness and snow and cold water, and cleanse me of sins as You cleansed the white garment of filth. No one narrated this hadith from al-Hasan ibn Ubaydillah except Yusuf ibn Khalid."
"6555","6549 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Harun ibn Said narrated to us, Anas ibn Iyad narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abdillah ibn Dumayrah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Ali, that Aishah used to say: I would bathe, I and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), from one vessel, from janabah. This hadith is not narrated from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from Aishah, except with this chain; Anas ibn Iyad alone transmitted it."
"6556","6550 - And with the same chain, from Husayn ibn Abdillah ibn Dumayrah, from his father, from his grandfather, from Qays ibn Sad ibn Ubadah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The owner of the mount is most entitled to its front. No one narrated this hadith from Husayn ibn Abdillah ibn Dumayrah except Anas ibn Iyad."
"6557","6551 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq ibn Jami narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hisham ibn Abi Hurrah al-Sadusi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Ismail ibn Rafi narrated to us, I heard Amr ibn Yahya ibn Umarah ibn Abi Hasan al-Ansari narrating, that he heard al-Qasim ibn Muhammad narrating, that Aishah said: People spoke much about bathing on Friday, but that was only in my house: a group from the people of al-Aliyah entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a hot day, having worked in their date-palms, wearing their woolen garments, and they entered with unpleasant odors, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When this day comes, bathe. No one narrated this hadith from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad except Amr ibn Yahya, and none from Amr except Ismail ibn Rafi, and none from Ismail except al-Fadl ibn al-Ala; Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi alone transmitted it."
"6558","6552 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Hisham al-Sadusi narrated to us, al-Fadl ibn al-Ala narrated to us, Ashath ibn Sawwar narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate: O Allah, forgive me my sin and my ignorance and my excess in my affair, and what You know better than I, O Allah, forgive me my serious and my joking, and my mistake and my intent, and all of that is with me."
"6559","6553 - And with the same chain, from Abu Burdah, from his father who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is none among you whom his deed will admit into Paradise. Some said: Not even you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Not even I, except that Allah envelops me with His mercy. No one narrated these two hadiths from Abu Ishaq except Ashath ibn Sawwar; al-Fadl ibn al-Ala alone transmitted them."
"6560","6554 - Muhammad ibn Ruzayq narrated to us, Ishaq ibn al-Dayf narrated to us, Amr ibn Asim al-Kilabi narrated to us, Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Mamar ibn Rashid, from al-Zuhri, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed away and the Arabs apostatized, Umar said: O Abu Bakr, do you intend to fight all the Arabs when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I was commanded to fight the people until they say: There is no god but Allah. So Abu Bakr said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only said: When they testify that there is no god but Allah, and establish the prayer and give the zakah, they protect from me their blood and wealth. By Allah, if they withheld from me a young goat they used to render to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would fight them over it. No one narrated this hadith from Mamar except Imran al-Qattan; Amr ibn Asim alone transmitted it."
"6561","6555 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghassan Abu Ulathah al-Faraidi al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi narrated to us, Yunus ibn Tamim narrated to us, from al-Awzai, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever Allah clothes with a blessing, let him praise Allah much, and whoever has many worries, let him seek Allahs forgiveness, and whoever finds his provision delayed, let him say much: There is no power nor strength except with Allah, and whoever stays with a people, let him not fast except with their permission, and whoever enters the house of a people, let him sit where they command him, for the people know best the private parts of their house, and from the sin that brings anger upon its doer are malice and envy and laziness in worship, and distress in livelihood. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir except al-Awzai, and none from al-Awzai except Yunus ibn Tamim; Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi alone transmitted it."
"6562","6556 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghassan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Sulayman al-Ruayni narrated to us, al-Layth ibn Sad narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ajlan, from al-Qaqa ibn Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every son of Adam will meet Allah on the Day of Resurrection with a sin he committed, He will punish him for it if He wills or have mercy on him, except Yahya ibn Zakariyya, for he was a master and chaste and a prophet among the righteous. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured toward a speck from the earth, took it, and said: His member was like this speck. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Ajlan except al-Layth, and none from al-Layth except Hajjaj ibn Sulayman; Muhammad ibn Salamah al-Muradi alone transmitted it."
"6563","6557 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghassan narrated to us, Abu Nuaym Abd al-Awwal al-Muallim narrated to us, Abu Umayyah al-Ayli narrated to us, from Zufar ibn Wasil, from Abu Salamah, from Abu Hurayrah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever laughs much, his due is taken lightly, and whoever jokes much, his majesty departs, and whoever jests much, his dignity departs, and whoever drinks water on an empty stomach, his strength breaks, and whoever speaks much, his slips are many, and whoever has many slips, his sins are many, and whoever has many sins, the Fire is more deserving of him. This hadith is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain; Abd al-Awwal al-Muallim alone transmitted it."
"6564","6558 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghassan narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Mabad al-Muradi narrated to us, Ibn Luhayah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my ummah are those who, when they do wrong, seek forgiveness, and when they do good, rejoice, and when they travel, shorten and break fast. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ibn Luhayah; Abdullah ibn Yahya ibn Mabad al-Muradi alone transmitted it."
"6565","6559 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghassan narrated to us, Makki ibn Abdillah al-Ruayni narrated to us, Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: When Jafar ibn Abi Talib came from the land of Abyssinia, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) met him, then when Jafar saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) he hopped out of reverence for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissed between his eyes, and said to him: O my beloved, you resemble people most in my form and character, and you were created from the clay from which I was created. O my beloved, tell me of some of the wonders of the land of Abyssinia. He said: Yes, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you O Messenger of Allah, while I was standing on one of its roads, I saw an old woman with a basket on her head, and a youth came rushing on his horse, pushed her, and threw the basket from her head, so she stood upright, followed him with her gaze, saying: Woe to you tomorrow when the King sits upon His throne and exacts for the oppressed from the oppressor. Jabir said: I looked at the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his tears were flowing down his eyes like embers, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah does not sanctify a nation in which the oppressed does not take his right from the oppressor, without being made to stammer. No one narrated this hadith from Sufyan ibn Uyaynah except Makki ibn Abdillah al-Ruayni."
"6566","6560 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghassan narrated to us, Amr ibn Yusuf ibn Yazid al-Basri narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah narrated to us, from Malik ibn Mighwal, from Nafi, from Ibn Umar who said: While I was traveling by the sides of Badr, a man emerged from a pit, with a chain around his neck, calling me: O Abdullah, give me water, O Abdullah, give me water, and I do not know whether he knew my name or called me with the call of the Arabs, and a black man emerged from that pit, with a whip in his hand, calling me: O Abdullah, do not give him water, for he is a disbeliever, then he struck him with the whip until he returned to his pit, so I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) hastening, and informed him, so he said to me: Have you seen him? I said: Yes. He said: That is the enemy of Allah Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, and that is his punishment until the Day of Resurrection. No one narrated this hadith from Malik ibn Mighwal except Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah al-Kufi."
"6567","6561 - Muhammad ibn Abi Ghassan al-Faraidi narrated to us, my father Abu Ghassan Ahmad ibn Iyad ibn Abi Taybah narrated to me, Yahya ibn Hassan narrated to us, from Sulayman ibn Bilal, from Yahya ibn Said, from Anas ibn Malik who said: I used to serve the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then a roasted chicken was brought, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of creation to You and to me to eat with me from this chicken. Then Ali came and knocked on the door. Anas said: Who is this? He said: Ali. So I said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is occupied, so he left. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) withdrew and ate, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, bring me the most beloved of creation to You and to me to eat with me from this chicken. Then Ali came and knocked hard, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) heard, so he said: O Anas, who is this? I said: Ali. He said: Admit him. So he entered, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I asked Allah three times to bring me the most beloved of creation to Him and to me to eat with me from this chicken. Ali said: And I, O Messenger of Allah, came three times, each time Anas turned me back. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Anas, what carried you to do what you did? I said: I loved that the supplication reach a man from my people. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man is not blamed for loving his people. No one narrated this hadith from Yahya ibn Said except Sulayman ibn Bilal, and none from Sulayman except Yahya ibn Hassan; Muhammad ibn Abi Ghassan alone transmitted it, from his father."
"6568","6562 - Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Wardi al-Misri narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad al-Ruasi narrated to us, Dawud ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ubaydillah al-Arzami, from Abu Burdah, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have a river from Sanaa to Aylah, in it vessels numbering the stars, and it is colder than snow, and sweeter than honey, and whiter than milk, whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst after it, and whoever does not taste it will never be quenched. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Burdah except al-Arzami, and none from al-Arzami except Dawud ibn Hilal; Zuhayr ibn Abbad alone transmitted it."
"6569","6563 - Muhammad ibn al-Harith ibn Abd al-Hamid al-Wardi narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Abbad narrated to us, Dawud ibn Hilal narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Hassan, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Anas ibn Malik, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A servant does not reach the reality of faith until he guards his tongue. No one narrated this hadith from Hisham ibn Hassan except Dawud ibn Hilal; Zuhayr ibn Abbad alone transmitted it."
"6570","6564 - Muhammad ibn Harun al-Sufi al-Misri narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tabban al-Madini narrated to us, my father narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Musa ibn Uqbah, from Aban ibn Taghlib, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There is no suckling after weaning, and no orphanhood after puberty. No one narrated this hadith from Alqamah except Ibrahim, and none narrated it from Ibrahim except Aban ibn Taghlib, and none from Aban except Musa ibn Uqbah, and none from Musa except Muhammad ibn Jafar; Muhammad ibn Ubayd al-Tabban alone transmitted it, from his father, and we did not write it except from this shaykh."
"6571","6565 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar al-Wakii al-Misri narrated to us, Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar narrated to us, Ubaydah ibn Humayd narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wail, from Masruq, from Aishah, she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by two graves being punished, so he said: They are being punished, and they are not being punished for something major: one of them would not guard against urine, and the other would walk with tale-bearing. Then he called for a moist palm stalk, broke it, placed upon this and upon this, and said: Perhaps it will be lightened for them until they dry. No one narrated this hadith from Mansur except Ubaydah ibn Humayd; Ali ibn Jafar al-Ahmar alone transmitted it."
"6572","6566 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn al-Sabbah al-Dulabi narrated to us, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq and Said ibn Abi Arubah, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon Hira, and it shook with them, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck it with his foot, and said: Be firm, for upon you are a prophet, and a truthful one, and two martyrs; and upon it were the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Abu Bakr, and Umar, and Uthman. No one narrated this hadith from Matar except Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan."
"6573","6567 - And with the same chain, Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Salih, from Abu Said al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile my Companions, for if one of you spent like Uhud in gold, he would not reach the mudd of one of them, nor half of it. No one narrated this hadith from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Abu Salih, except Dawud ibn al-Zibriqan. And al-Hasan ibn Abi Jafar narrated it, from Muhammad ibn Juhadah, from Atiyyah, from Abu Said."
"6574","6568 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Ahmad ibn Salih narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, Abd al-Aziz ibn Bilal ibn Abdillah ibn Unays narrated to us, from his father Bilal ibn Abdillah, from Atiyyah ibn Abdillah, from his father Abdillah ibn Unays, that he asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about Laylat al-Qadr? So he said: I saw it then was made to forget it, so seek it in the last half, then he returned and said: In twenty-three passing nights of the month. This hadith is not narrated from Atiyyah ibn Abdillah except with this chain; Ibn Abi Fudayk alone transmitted it."
"6575","6569 - Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abu al-Tahir ibn al-Sarh narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Makhramah ibn Bukayr informed me, from his father who said: I heard Humayd ibn Nafi saying: I heard Zaynab bint Abi Salamah saying: I heard Aishah saying: Sahlah bint Suhayl came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Messenger of Allah, I see in the face of Abu Hudhayfah something from the entering of Salim upon me? The Messenger of Allah said: Suckle him. She said: He has a beard? So he said: Suckle him, what is in the face of Abu Hudhayfah will go away. No one narrated this hadith from Humayd ibn Nafi except Bukayr ibn Abdillah, and none from Bukayr except his son Makhramah; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted it."
"6576","6570 - Muhammad ibn Khalid ibn Yazid al-Bardai narrated to us in Egypt, Abu Salamah Ubayd ibn Khalasah narrated to us at Marrat al-Numan, Abdullah ibn Nafi al-Madani narrated to us, from al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad, from his father, from Jabir ibn Abdillah who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father has taken my wealth, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to the man: Go and bring me your father. Then Jibril descended upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: Allah conveys peace to you, and says: When the old man comes to you, ask him about something he said within himself which his ears have not heard. Then when the old man came, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Your son keeps complaining to me that you take his wealth? He said: Ask him O Messenger of Allah, do I spend it except upon one of his paternal aunts or maternal aunts or upon myself? So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Enough: leave this, inform me of something you said within yourself, which your ears have not heard. The old man said: By Allah O Messenger of Allah, Allah keeps increasing us in certainty through you, I said within myself something my ears have not heard. He said: Say, and I will listen. He said: I said: While wakeful at night. He said: At that, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seized the sons garment and said: You and your wealth belong to your father. No one narrated this hadith with this wording and poetry from al-Munkadir ibn Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir except Abdullah ibn Nafi; Ubayd ibn Khalasah alone transmitted it."
"6577","6571 - Muhammad ibn Sakhtawayh ibn al-Haytham al-Bardai narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Yaqub al-Juzajani narrated to us, Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, from Salih ibn Kaysan, from al-Zuhri, from Urwah, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Call your father and your brother until I write a document, for I fear that one will say, and one will wish, but Allah and the believers refuse except Abu Bakr. No one narrated this hadith from al-Zuhri except Salih ibn Kaysan, and none narrated it from Salih ibn Kaysan except Ibrahim ibn Sad; Yazid ibn Harun and Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Ayyub alone transmitted it."
"6578","6572 - Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahim ibn Thumayr al-Misri narrated to us, Said ibn Ufayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated to us, from Ubaydillah, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Jabir who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is Umrah obligatory, its obligation like the obligation of Hajj? He said: No, and if you perform Umrah it is better for you. The Ubaydillah from whom Yahya ibn Ayyub narrated this hadith is Ubaydillah ibn Abi Jafar. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Zubayr except Ubaydillah ibn Abi Jafar; Yahya ibn Ayyub alone transmitted it, and the well-known version is from the hadith of al-Hajjaj ibn Artah, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir."
"6579","6573 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Mujalid, from al-Shabi, from Abdullah ibn Amr who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe, and the emigrant is one who abandons what Allah has forbidden. No one narrated this hadith from Mujalid except al-Masudi."
"6580","6574 - With the same chain, al-Masudi narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah who said: I bear witness upon the truthful, the believed, Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Selling milk-retained animals is deception, and deception of a Muslim is not lawful. No one narrated this hadith from Jabir except al-Masudi."
"6581","6575 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Muadh ibn Jabal, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I fear for you three things, and they will occur: the slip of a scholar, and the disputation of a hypocrite with the Quran, and worldly life opened upon you. No one narrated this hadith from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr except Abd al-Hakim ibn Mansur."
"6582","6576 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Numayr narrated to us, Yahya ibn Yala ibn al-Harith al-Muharibi narrated to us, from his father, from Ghaylan ibn Jami, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) distributed sheep among his Companions, and gave each ten a sheep. No one narrated this hadith from Ghaylan ibn Jami except Yala ibn al-Harith; his son Yahya alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from Ibn Abi Layla except with this chain."
"6583","6577 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan al-Baghdadi narrated to us in Egypt, al-Hasan ibn Bishr al-Bajali narrated to us, al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Anas ibn Malik who said: On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted safety to the people except four persons: Abd al-Uzza ibn Khatal, and Miqyas ibn Subabah al-Kinani, and Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh, and Umm Sarah, a woman. As for Abd al-Uzza, he was killed while holding the curtains of the Kabah. He said: A man from the Ansar vowed to kill Abdullah ibn Sad ibn Abi Sarh when he saw him, and he was the foster brother of Uthman ibn Affan, so he brought him to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking his intercession, then when the Ansari saw him he wrapped himself with the sword, then went out seeking him, and found him in the circle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he feared to kill him, and kept hesitating, disliking to advance upon him because he was in the circle of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) extended his hand and pledged him, then said to the Ansari: I waited for you to fulfill your vow. He said: O Messenger of Allah, I was in awe of you, why did you not wink to me? He said: It is not for a prophet to wink. As for Miqyas, he had a brother killed by mistake with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent with him a man from Banu Fihr to collect for him the blood-money from the Ansar, then when he had collected the blood-money for him and returned, the Fihri slept, so Miqyas sprang, took a stone and struck his head with it, and killed him, then he came, saying: As for Umm Sarah, she was a freedwoman of Quraysh, so she came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), complained of need, and he gave her something, then a man came to her and handed her a letter for the people of Makkah, seeking closeness to them thereby to be protected regarding his dependents, and he had dependents with them, so Jibril informed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) of that, so he sent after her Umar ibn al-Khattab and Ali ibn Abi Talib, and they caught up with her, searched her, but could not find anything of it, so they turned back returning, then one of them said to his companion: By Allah, we did not lie nor were we lied to, return with us to her. So they returned to her, drew their swords, and said: By Allah, we shall make you taste death or you shall hand us the letter. She denied, then said: I will hand it to you on condition that you do not return me to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So they accepted from her, and she loosened the knot of her head and brought out a letter from her braids, and handed it to them, so they returned with it to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and handed it to him, so he sent to the man and said: What is this letter? He said: I inform you O Messenger of Allah, there is none with you except that he has in Makkah one who protects him regarding his dependents except me, so I wrote this letter that they may be for me regarding my dependents. Then Allah revealed: O you who believe, do not take My enemy and your enemy as allies, extending to them affection, to the end of the verses. No one narrated the first of this hadith, the story of Miqyas, and Ibn Khatal, and Abdullah ibn Sad, from Qatadah, from Anas, except al-Hakam ibn Abd al-Malik; al-Hasan ibn Bishr alone transmitted it."
"6584","6578 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah ibn Bishr narrated to us, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, from Anbasah ibn al-Azhar, from Simak ibn Harb, from Jabir ibn Samurah who said: As if I am looking at the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and his locks reaching this place, and he struck with his hand upon his chest between his breasts. No one narrated this hadith from Simak except Anbasah ibn al-Azhar; Yunus ibn Bukayr alone transmitted it."
"6585","6579 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Yunus narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, he said: I heard al-Rubayyi bint Muawwidh saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) liked cucumber."
"6586","6580 - And with the same chain, Yunus ibn Bukayr narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Ismail ibn Mujammi narrated to me, Uthman ibn Kab al-Qurazi narrated to me, a man from Banu al-Nadir who was in the care of Safiyyah, called al-Rabi, narrated to me, from Safiyyah bint Huyayy, she said: I never saw anyone of better character than the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I saw him when he had mounted me behind him from Khaybar upon the rear of his camel at night, and I would doze and my head would strike the back of the saddle, so he would touch me with his hand and say: O you, gently, O daughter of Huyayy, gently, until when he came to al-Sahba he said: I apologize to you O Safiyyah for what I did to your people, they said to me such-and-such, and they said to me such-and-such. This hadith is not narrated from Safiyyah except with this chain; Yunus ibn Bukayr alone transmitted it."
"6587","6581 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, al-Ala ibn al-Minhal al-Ghanawi narrated to us, Muhannad al-Qaysi narrated to me, and he was trustworthy, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are in prophethood and mercy, and there will be caliphate and mercy, then there will be such-and-such, then there will be biting kingship, they will drink wines, and wear silk, and in that they will be aided until the Hour comes. No one narrated this hadith from al-Ala ibn al-Minhal except Zayd ibn al-Hubab."
"6588","6582 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Sharik narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sad, from Abu Zabyah, from Abu Umamah who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Love is from Allah, and renown in the heaven, so when Allah loves a servant He says: O Jibril, your Lord loves so-and-so so love him. He said: So Jibril calls out, and love for him is sent down upon the people of the earth. This hadith is not narrated from Abu Umamah except with this chain; Sharik alone transmitted it."
"6589","6583 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Numayr narrated to us, from al-Amash, from Abu Qays Abd al-Rahman ibn Tharwan, from Amr ibn Hanzalah, he said: Hudhayfah said: Mudar will not leave a servant of Allah except that they tempt him or kill him, until they do not even protect the tail of a ravine. He said: They said: You say this, while you are a man from Mudar? He said: Shall I not say what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? No one narrated this hadith from al-Amash except Abdullah ibn Numayr."
"6590","6584 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Yahya ibn al-Mubarak al-Kufi narrated to us, Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Ibn Jurayj who said: Musa ibn Uqbah informed me, from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever sits in a gathering in which his chatter is much, then says before standing: Glory be to You our Lord and with Your praise, there is no god but You, I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You, it will be an expiation for what was in that gathering. No one included Sufyan between Hajjaj and Ibn Jurayj in the chain of this hadith among those who narrated it from Hajjaj except Yahya ibn al-Mubarak."
"6591","6585 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Mindal ibn Ali narrated to us, from al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab, from Abu Dawud al-Hamdani, from Buraydah al-Aslami, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Buraydah, shall I not teach you words, whoever Allah intends good for, He teaches them to him, then he never forgets them? He said: I said: Yes O Messenger of Allah. He said: Say: O Allah, I am weak, so strengthen my weakness in Your pleasure, and take my forelock toward good, and make Islam the utmost of my pleasure. O Allah, I am weak so strengthen me, and I am lowly so honor me, and I am poor so enrich me. This hadith is not narrated from Buraydah except with this chain; al-Ala ibn al-Musayyab alone transmitted it."
"6592","6586 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, from Kathir ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ata, from Aishah, she said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. No one narrated this hadith from Ata except Kathir ibn Abd al-Rahman."
"6593","6587 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Yahya al-Himmani narrated to us, Sulayman ibn Bilal narrated to us, Qays ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Qays ibn Makhramah narrated to me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of wrongdoing, for wrongdoing is darknesses on the Day of Resurrection. This hadith is not narrated from al-Miswar ibn Makhramah except with this chain; Sulayman ibn Bilal alone transmitted it."
"6594","6588 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Asim ibn Ali narrated to us, Abu Hilal narrated to us, Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt al-Rasibi narrated to us, and the name of Abu Thubayt is Surayj, from Abu al-Jawza, he said: We entered upon Ibn Abbas, and he had ordered us regarding exchange, then I entered upon him once, and he said: We used to command you, and we forbid you from it. So I said: What shall we do about what we commanded the people? He said: I met one from the Companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who is more knowledgeable of that than I, so he forbade me, and I forbade you as he forbade me. No one narrated this hadith from Uqbah ibn Abi Thubayt except Abu Hilal. And the man whom Ibn Abbas met was Abu Said."
"6595","6589 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Thabit al-Abdi narrated to us, from Harun ibn Riab, from Abu Najih, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Poor, poor, poor is a man who has no wife, even if he has much wealth. Poor, poor, poor is a woman who has no husband, even if she has much wealth. No one narrated this hadith from Harun ibn Riab except Muhammad ibn Thabit."
"6596","6590 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Asbat ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Abu Raja al-Khurasani, from Abbad ibn Kathir, from Said al-Jurayri, from Abu Nadrah, from Jabir ibn Abdillah and Abu Said al-Khudri, they said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Backbiting is worse than fornication. It was said: And how? He said: A man commits fornication then repents, and Allah forgives him, but the backbiter is not forgiven until his companion forgives him. No one narrated this hadith from al-Jurayri except Abbad ibn Kathir; Abu Raja al-Khurasani alone transmitted it, and it is not narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) except with this chain."
"6597","6591 - Muhammad ibn Jafar ibn Ayan narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Shuayb ibn Harb narrated to us, Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq narrated to us, Mujahid narrated to us, from Aishah, she said: The household of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a wild animal, and it would come forward and go back, then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered it would lie down, and not stir, disliking to harm the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). No one narrated this hadith from Mujahid except Yunus ibn Abi Ishaq, and it is not narrated from Aishah except with this chain."
"6598","6592 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Yahya ibn Ayyub al-Maqabiri narrated to us, Ali ibn Ghurab narrated to us, Zuhayr ibn Marzuq narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Judan, from Said ibn al-Musayyab, from Aishah, that she said: O Messenger of Allah, what is the thing which it is not lawful to withhold? He said: Water and salt and fire. She said: This water we know, but what of salt and fire? So he said: Whoever gives salt, it is as if he gave charity of all that that salt flavors, and whoever gives fire, it is as if he gave charity of all that that fire ripens, and whoever gives a Muslim a drink of water where water is found, it is as if he freed a slave, and whoever gives a Muslim a drink of water where water is not found, it is as if he gave him life. Zuhayr ibn Marzuq narrated no other musnad except this; Ali ibn Ghurab alone transmitted it."
"6599","6593 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Khalid ibn Khidash narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr ibn al-Harith, from Abu al-Nadr, from Ziyad, the freedman of Ibn Ayyash, from Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ascended upon the grave of Sad ibn Muadh, and said: If anyone were to be saved from the compression of the grave, Sad would have been saved, and he was compressed a compression, then it was eased from him. No one narrated this hadith from Abu al-Nadr except Amr ibn al-Harith; Ibn Wahb alone transmitted it."
"6600","6594 - Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Abbad ibn Musa al-Khuttali narrated to us, Yusuf ibn Ziyad al-Wasiti narrated to us, Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad ibn Anum al-Ifriqi the judge narrated to us, from al-Agharr Abu Muslim, from Abu Hurayrah who said: One day I entered the market with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he sat with the cloth merchants, and bought trousers for four dirhams, and the people of the market had a weigher. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Weigh and give excess. The weigher said: This word I never heard from anyone. Abu Hurayrah said: So I said to him: Sufficient for you of harshness in your religion that you do not know your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So he threw the scale, and leapt to the hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing it, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pulled his hand from him, and said: This is only done by the non-Arabs to their kings, I am only a man from among you, so weigh and give excess. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the trousers. Abu Hurayrah said: So I went to carry it from him, so he said: The owner of the thing is most entitled to his thing to carry it, except that he be weak, unable for it, then his Muslim brother helps him. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you wear trousers? He said: Yes, by night and day, in travel and residence, for I was commanded with covering, and I found nothing more covering than it. No one narrated this hadith from Abu Hurayrah except al-Agharr, and none from al-Agharr except Abd al-Rahman ibn Ziyad."
